 {"id":"cns-pharma-1","system":"CNS","title":"Pharmacology of CNS Drugs: Sedative-Hypnotics and Antidepressants","url":"cns-pharma-1.html","summary":"CNS channels and neurotransmitters, sedative-hypnotics (BZ, barbiturates, Z-drugs, melatonin/orexin, buspirone), tolerance and dependence, depression and antidepressants (TCAs, SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs, atypicals).","points":["CNS drugs act on ion channels and receptors: GABA-A, NMDA, monoamine transporters","BZ: positive allosteric modulators of GABA-A, ↑ Cl⁻ channel opening frequency; Flumazenil antagonist","Barbiturates: ↑ channel opening duration; narrow safety margin","Z-drugs: zolpidem, zaleplon, zopiclone; chloral hydrate; melatonin/orexin agents; buspirone","Depression: monoamine hypothesis; TCAs block NE/5-HT reuptake","SSRIs, SNRIs, mirtazapine, bupropion, MAOIs, 5-HT2 antagonists: mechanism, uses, adverse effects"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which drug blocks benzodiazepine action at the GABA-A receptor?","opts":["Flumazenil","β-Carbolines","Zolpidem","Buspirone"],"a":0,"why":"Flumazenil هو الـ Antagonist اللي بيحجب BZ. أما β-Carbolines فهني Inverse agonists، تأثيرها عكسي."},{"q":"Barbiturates effect ← GABA-A chloride channel?","opts":["↑ opening frequency","↑ opening duration","Blocks the channel","Opens without GABA"],"a":1,"why":"BZ بتزيد تكرار فتح القناة (Frequency). Barbiturates بتزيد مدة الفتح (Duration)."},{"q":"Usual cause of death ← sedative-hypnotic overdose?","opts":["Hypertension","Respiratory depression","Hyperthermia","Renal failure"],"a":1,"why":"تثبيط التنفس (Respiratory depression) هو السبب المعتاد للوفاة بالجرعة الزائدة."},{"q":"Which drug is a prodrug converted by alcohol dehydrogenase?","opts":["Chloral hydrate","Phenobarbital","Zaleplon","Ramelteon"],"a":0,"why":"Chloral hydrate بيتحوّل بإنزيم Alcohol dehydrogenase لـ Trichloroethanol (المنوّم الفعّال)."},{"q":"Which is NOT a Z-drug?","opts":["Zolpidem","Zaleplon","Triazolam","Zopiclone"],"a":2,"why":"Triazolam بنزوديازيبين (بتنتهي بـ azolam). الـ 3z هني Zopiclone و Zolpidem و Zaleplon."},{"q":"Ramelteon: which statement is correct?","opts":["Acts directly on GABA-A","Controlled substance","Minimal abuse liability","↑ testosterone"],"a":2,"why":"Ramelteon ما بيشتغل على GABA، مو مادة خاضعة للرقابة، احتمال إساءة استعمالو قليل. وبيقلل Testosterone مش بيزيدو."},{"q":"Suvorexant mechanism?","opts":["OX1R, OX2R antagonist","Melatonin agonist","5-HT1A partial agonist","GABA-A agonist"],"a":0,"why":"Suvorexant بيحجب مستقبلات Orexin ← بيقلل نظام اليقظة ← منوّم."},{"q":"Buspirone is used ← ?","opts":["Insomnia","Generalized anxiety","Epilepsy","Anaesthesia"],"a":1,"why":"Buspirone: Partial agonist على 5-HT1A، بيُستعمل بالقلق المعمّم (GAD)."},{"q":"Prototypical TCAs?","opts":["Fluoxetine, sertraline","Imipramine, amitriptyline","Phenelzine, selegiline","Venlafaxine, duloxetine"],"a":1,"why":"النموذجين: Imipramine و Amitriptyline."},{"q":"Which statement ← SSRIs is correct?","opts":["Block alpha receptors","Minimal autonomic toxicity","Inhibit MAO-A","Block 5-HT2A"],"a":1,"why":"SSRIs سميتها الذاتية قليلة لأنها ما بتحصر Alpha و Muscarinic و H1. النموذج: Fluoxetine."},{"q":"Mirtazapine mechanism?","opts":["Presynaptic α2 antagonism ← ↑ NE, 5-HT release","MAO-B inhibition","SERT inhibition only","GABA-A potentiation"],"a":0,"why":"Mirtazapine بيسد α2 (Negative feedback) ← إفراز NE و 5-HT بيزيد. وكمان بيسد 5-HT2."},{"q":"Bupropion is used ← ?","opts":["Smoking cessation","Status epilepticus","Insomnia","Anaesthesia"],"a":0,"why":"Bupropion (NDRI) بيُستعمل للإقلاع عن التدخين، وللاكتئاب والاضطراب العاطفي الموسمي."},{"q":"MAOI with fastest onset, shortest duration?","opts":["Phenelzine","Isocarboxazid","Tranylcypromine","Selegiline"],"a":2,"why":"Tranylcypromine: أسرع بدء، مدة حوالي 1 week مقابل 2–3 weeks لباقي MAOIs."},{"q":"Selective MAO-B inhibitor ← depression, Parkinsonism?","opts":["Phenelzine","Selegiline","Isocarboxazid","Trazodone"],"a":1,"why":"Selegiline انتقائي لـ MAO-B (بيكسّر Dopamine)، وللاكتئاب بصيغة لصقة جلدية."},{"q":"Nefazodone, trazodone act by?","opts":["MAO inhibition","Block 5-HT2A","SERT inhibition only","α2 antagonism"],"a":1,"why":"بيحجبوا 5-HT2A ← تأثير مضاد للاكتئاب ومضاد للقلق."}],"cards":[{"f":"Voltage-gated channels?","b":"Respond to membrane potential change"},{"f":"Ligand-gated channels?","b":"Neurotransmitter binding ← opens; ionotropic; e.g., GABA-A"},{"f":"Metabotropic receptors?","b":"G-protein-coupled; second messengers; e.g., GABA-B"},{"f":"CNS excitatory transmitter?","b":"Glutamate"},{"f":"CNS inhibitory transmitters?","b":"GABA, glycine"},{"f":"Sites of drug action?","b":"8 steps: action potential, synthesis, storage, metabolism, release, reuptake, degradation, receptor"},{"f":"Sedative vs hypnotic?","b":"Sedative: ↓ anxiety, calming; hypnotic: drowsiness, sleep (more CNS depression)"},{"f":"REM sleep?","b":"Rapid eye movements; most dreaming"},{"f":"BZ mechanism?","b":"Bind GABA-A; potentiate GABAergic inhibition; ↑ Cl⁻ channel opening frequency"},{"f":"Barbiturate effect ← Cl⁻ channel?","b":"↑ opening duration"},{"f":"BZ antagonist?","b":"Flumazenil: blocks BZ; may precipitate seizures"},{"f":"Inverse agonists, BZ site?","b":"β-Carbolines"},{"f":"Organ-level effects?","b":"Sedation, hypnosis, anesthesia, anticonvulsant, muscle relaxation, respiratory-cardiovascular"},{"f":"Usual cause of overdose death?","b":"Respiratory depression"},{"f":"Tolerance?","b":"↓ responsiveness ← repeated exposure"},{"f":"Physiologic dependence features?","b":"↑ anxiety, insomnia, CNS excitability, convulsions"},{"f":"BZ cognitive adverse effect?","b":"Dose-related amnesia; impaired new learning"},{"f":"Status epilepticus first-line?","b":"IV lorazepam, diazepam; IM midazolam"},{"f":"BZ examples?","b":"Alprazolam, chlordiazepoxide, clorazepate, clonazepam, diazepam, flurazepam, lorazepam, midazolam"},{"f":"Name clue ← BZ?","b":"azepam, azolam"},{"f":"Barbiturates: key problem?","b":"Low therapeutic index; dependence; abuse"},{"f":"Barbiturate overdose?","b":"Hypothermia, respiratory depression, coma"},{"f":"Thiopental?","b":"Ultra-short barbiturate; anaesthesia"},{"f":"Phenobarbital?","b":"Long-acting; epilepsy; 12+ h"},{"f":"Z-drugs?","b":"Zopiclone, zolpidem, zaleplon (3z); GABA-A, different site from BZ"},{"f":"Chloral hydrate?","b":"Prodrug ← alcohol dehydrogenase ← trichloroethanol; 30–60 min; 6–8 h; t½ 8 h"},{"f":"Chloral hydrate danger?","b":"Serious hepatic, renal failure; aggravates peptic ulcer"},{"f":"Ramelteon, tasimelteon?","b":"Melatonin receptor agonists (SCN); ↓ sleep-onset latency; no GABA effect"},{"f":"Ramelteon adverse effects?","b":"Dizziness, fatigue; ↓ testosterone, ↑ prolactin"},{"f":"Tasimelteon use?","b":"Non-24-hour sleep-wake disorder"},{"f":"Suvorexant?","b":"Orexin OX1R, OX2R antagonist; insomnia"},{"f":"Buspirone?","b":"5-HT1A partial agonist (± D2); generalized anxiety"},{"f":"Amine hypothesis?","b":"Depression ← functional deficiency: NE or serotonin"},{"f":"TCAs mechanism?","b":"Inhibit NE, 5-HT reuptake; prototypes imipramine, amitriptyline"},{"f":"TCAs also block?","b":"Muscarinic, H1, alpha ← orthostatic hypotension"},{"f":"Mirtazapine?","b":"Presynaptic α2 antagonist ← ↑ NE, 5-HT release; 5-HT2 antagonist"},{"f":"Bupropion?","b":"NE, dopamine reuptake inhibitor; smoking cessation, depression, SAD"},{"f":"SSRI prototype?","b":"Fluoxetine"},{"f":"SSRI advantage?","b":"Selective SERT block; minimal autonomic toxicity"},{"f":"SNRIs?","b":"Venlafaxine, desvenlafaxine, duloxetine; NE, 5-HT transporters; no α, anticholinergic, antihistaminic"},{"f":"Venlafaxine vs duloxetine?","b":"Venlafaxine: less NET affinity"},{"f":"MAO-A vs MAO-B?","b":"A: NE, 5-HT, tyramine; B: dopamine"},{"f":"Non-selective MAOIs?","b":"Phenelzine, isocarboxazid, tranylcypromine"},{"f":"Tranylcypromine?","b":"Fastest onset; ~1 week (others 2–3 weeks)"},{"f":"Selegiline?","b":"Selective MAO-B; depression, Parkinsonism; transdermal patch"},{"f":"Nefazodone, trazodone?","b":"5-HT2A block ← antidepressant, antianxiety"},{"f":"Antidepressant uses?","b":"Depression, anxiety (panic, GAD, social phobia), chronic pain, enuresis, eating disorders, smoking cessation, delay orgasm, PMS, PMDD"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-16"},
 {"id":"malaria-2026","system":"protozoa","title":"Malaria: Plasmodium spp.","url":"malaria-2026-1.html","summary":"Plasmodium species, fever patterns, falciparum vs vivax morphology, human and mosquito life cycle, hypnozoite relapse, clinical features, lab diagnosis (smear, RDT, fluorescent, PCR) and treatment.","points":["Female Anopheles bite; infective form sporozoite","4 human species; falciparum most lethal, vivax most widespread","Tertian: falciparum, ovale, vivax; quartan: malariae","Falciparum smear: ring 2-4 μm + banana gametocytes only","Vivax: all stages, Schüffner's dots, enlarged RBC","Pre-erythrocytic 8 days, 20,000-30,000 merozoites; erythrocytic 48 h","Hypnozoite: relapse up to 2 years (vivax, ovale)","Sticky RBCs: cerebral malaria; renal failure: Blackwater fever","Diagnosis: thick/thin smear, RDT (HRP II), fluorescent, PCR","Chloroquine, quinine: anti-erythrocytic; primaquine, pyrimethamine: anti-exoerythrocytic"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Infective form of Plasmodium to man:","opts":["Sporozoite","Merozoite","Gametocyte","Hypnozoite"],"a":0,"why":"Sporozoite is injected by the mosquito bite."},{"q":"Definitive host of Plasmodium:","opts":["Man","Female Anopheles","Culex","Dog"],"a":1,"why":"Sexual development occurs in the mosquito."},{"q":"Only ring forms and gametocytes in peripheral blood:","opts":["P. vivax","P. malariae","P. falciparum","P. ovale"],"a":2,"why":"Schizonts aggregate in brain and organ capillaries."},{"q":"Schüffner's dots are seen in:","opts":["P. falciparum","P. vivax","Both","Neither"],"a":1,"why":"Fine red dots on the infected RBC membrane in P. vivax."},{"q":"Quartan malaria is caused by:","opts":["P. malariae","P. vivax","P. ovale","P. falciparum"],"a":0,"why":"Fever every 4th day."},{"q":"Pre-erythrocytic schizogony lasts:","opts":["48 hours","8 days","30 years","2 years"],"a":1,"why":"Liver stage lasts 8 days."},{"q":"Resting liver stage responsible for relapse:","opts":["Oocyst","Hypnozoite","Ookinete","Trophozoite"],"a":1,"why":"Reactivates up to 2 years."},{"q":"Antigen detected by RDT for P. falciparum:","opts":["HRP II","PfEMP","CSP","MSP"],"a":0,"why":"Immunochromatography, malaria card test."},{"q":"Preferred stain per lecture:","opts":["Gram","ZN","Leishman","H&E"],"a":2,"why":"Giemsa is also acceptable."},{"q":"Renal failure in malaria can manifest as:","opts":["Blackwater fever","Cerebral malaria","Quartan fever","Hypnozoite"],"a":0,"why":"Affects kidneys."},{"q":"Anti-erythrocytic drugs:","opts":["Primaquine, pyrimethamine","Chloroquine, quinine","Both","Neither"],"a":1,"why":"Primaquine, pyrimethamine act on exo-erythrocytic stage."}],"cards":[{"f":"Infective form","b":"Sporozoite"},{"f":"Definitive host","b":"Female Anopheles"},{"f":"Intermediate host","b":"Man"},{"f":"Tertian","b":"Falciparum, ovale, vivax: every 3rd day"},{"f":"Quartan","b":"P. malariae: every 4th day"},{"f":"Falciparum smear","b":"Ring + crescent gametocytes only"},{"f":"Ring size","b":"2-4 μm"},{"f":"Schüffner's dots","b":"P. vivax"},{"f":"Pre-erythrocytic","b":"Liver, 8 days"},{"f":"Erythrocytic","b":"RBC, 48 h, 6-24 merozoites"},{"f":"Hypnozoite","b":"Dormant liver form, relapse"},{"f":"Cerebral malaria","b":"Sticky RBCs block brain capillaries"},{"f":"Blackwater fever","b":"Renal failure"},{"f":"RDT antigen","b":"HRP II (P. falciparum)"},{"f":"Preferred stain","b":"Leishman (Giemsa acceptable)"},{"f":"Anti-erythrocytic","b":"Chloroquine, quinine"},{"f":"Anti-exoerythrocytic","b":"Primaquine, pyrimethamine"}],"subject":"para","date":"2026-11-15"},
 {"id":"malaria-2","kind":"practical","system":"protozoa","title":"Malaria 2: P. malariae & P. falciparum","url":"malaria-prac-2.html","summary":"Classification of Plasmodium, then P. malariae (benign quartan, band form, rosette schizont) vs P. falciparum (malignant tertian, tiny rings with double chromatin, crescent gametocytes), the two-phase life cycle and lab diagnosis (thick and thin films, serology).","points":["Apicomplexa > Sporozoa > Haemosporida > Plasmodium; 4 human species","P. malariae: benign quartan; tropical Africa, Sri Lanka, Burma, parts of India","P. malariae ring: thick, intensely stained, single large chromatin dot; RBC not enlarged","Band form is unique to P. malariae; numerous large pigment granules","P. malariae schizont: 6-12 merozoites (usually 8-10), rosette; can be common in blood","P. falciparum: malignant tertian, often fatal; named for crescent gametocytes","P. falciparum rings: delicate, tiny, at RBC margin; double chromatin (stereo headphones)","P. falciparum schizont: smallest, 8-24 merozoites (usually 16), 2/3 of RBC; rare in blood except severe cases","Gametocytes crescent/banana, ~1.5x RBC, appear ~10 days after rings","Asexual phase in man (intermediate host); sexual phase in female Anopheles (definitive host); thick film detects, thin film differentiates species"],"mcqs":[{"q":"P. falciparum is named after:","opts":["Crescent gametocytes","Band form","Rosette schizont","Schüffner's dots"],"a":0,"why":"Crescentic shape of gametocytes."},{"q":"Band form is a unique feature of:","opts":["P. falciparum","P. vivax","P. ovale","P. malariae"],"a":3,"why":"Cytoplasm elongates across the RBC."},{"q":"P. malariae causes:","opts":["Blackwater fever","Cerebral malaria","Benign quartan malaria","Malignant tertian malaria"],"a":2,"why":"Fever every 4th day (quartan)."},{"q":"Schizont of P. malariae usually has:","opts":["2 merozoites","8-10 merozoites","16 merozoites","24 merozoites"],"a":1,"why":"6-12, usually 8-10, in a rosette."},{"q":"Schizont of P. falciparum usually has:","opts":["16 merozoites","8-10 merozoites","6 merozoites","30,000 merozoites"],"a":0,"why":"8-24, usually 16."},{"q":"Schizonts are rarely seen in the peripheral blood of:","opts":["P. malariae","Both","Neither","P. falciparum"],"a":3,"why":"Except in severe cases."},{"q":"Binucleate ring resembling stereo headphones is seen in:","opts":["Both","Neither","P. falciparum","P. malariae"],"a":2,"why":"Double chromatin, common in falciparum."},{"q":"Falciparum gametocytes appear after the ring stage by about:","opts":["1 hour","10 days","2 days","30 days"],"a":1,"why":"About 10 days."},{"q":"Definitive host of Plasmodium:","opts":["Female Anopheles","Man","Cow","Dog"],"a":0,"why":"Sexual phase occurs in the mosquito."},{"q":"Best blood film to differentiate between species:","opts":["Thick film","Both","Neither","Thin film"],"a":3,"why":"Thin film shows morphology; thick film detects the parasite."},{"q":"Order of Plasmodium:","opts":["Sporozoa","Coccidia","Haemosporida","Apicomplexa"],"a":2,"why":"Phylum Apicomplexa, class Sporozoa, order Haemosporida."}],"cards":[{"f":"Phylum / Class / Order / Genus","b":"Apicomplexa / Sporozoa / Haemosporida / Plasmodium"},{"f":"Human Plasmodium species","b":"vivax, ovale, malariae, falciparum"},{"f":"P. malariae disease","b":"Benign quartan malaria (fever every 4th day)"},{"f":"P. malariae distribution","b":"Tropical Africa, Sri Lanka, Burma, parts of India"},{"f":"Definitive host","b":"Female Anopheles (vector)"},{"f":"Intermediate host","b":"Man"},{"f":"P. malariae ring","b":"Like vivax but thicker, intensely stained, single large chromatin dot"},{"f":"Unique feature of P. malariae","b":"Band form; numerous large pigment granules"},{"f":"P. malariae schizont","b":"6-12 merozoites (usually 8-10), rosette, nearly fills a normal-sized RBC"},{"f":"P. falciparum disease","b":"Malignant tertian malaria, often fatal"},{"f":"Why 'falciparum'?","b":"Crescent-shaped gametocytes"},{"f":"P. falciparum ring","b":"Delicate, tiny, along RBC margin; double chromatin (stereo headphones); several per RBC"},{"f":"P. falciparum schizont","b":"Smallest; 8-24 merozoites (usually 16); fills about 2/3 of RBC; rare in blood except severe cases"},{"f":"P. falciparum gametocyte","b":"Crescent, sausage or banana; about 1.5x RBC diameter; appears about 10 days after rings"},{"f":"Asexual phase","b":"In humans (intermediate host)"},{"f":"Sexual phase","b":"In the mosquito (definitive host)"},{"f":"Thick film","b":"Detects the parasite; easy and fast for light infection in endemic areas"},{"f":"Thin film","b":"Differentiates between species"}],"subject":"para","date":"2026-11-16"},
 {"id":"hemodynamics-2","system":"inflam","title":"Hemodynamic Disturbance 2: Thrombosis, Embolism, Infarction, Shock","url":"hemodynamics-2.html","summary":"Virchow's triad, fate and morphology of thrombus, DIC, embolism types, pulmonary thromboembolism, ischemia, infarction (red vs white), and shock types, stages and prognosis.","points":["Virchow: endothelial injury, altered flow, hypercoagulability","Turbulence: arterial; stasis: venous","Fate: propagation, embolization, dissolution, organization, calcification","Lines of Zahn: true thrombus, absent postmortem","DIC: microthrombi, consumption, bleeding","PTE source: deep leg veins; saddle at bifurcation","Red infarct: venous, loose, dual; white: arterial, solid","Shock: cardiogenic, hypovolemic, septic, anaphylactic, neurogenic"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Stasis mainly causes:","opts":["Venous thrombosis","Arterial thrombosis","Cardiac thrombosis","Vegetations"],"a":0,"why":"Turbulence causes arterial and cardiac thrombosis."},{"q":"Lines of Zahn are found in:","opts":["Thrombus formed during life","Postmortem clot","Both","Neither"],"a":0,"why":"Absent in postmortem clots."},{"q":"DIC ends with:","opts":["Serious bleeding","Only thrombosis","Hypertension","Polycythemia"],"a":0,"why":"Platelets and clotting proteins are consumed."},{"q":"Saddle embolus lodges at:","opts":["Pulmonary artery bifurcation","Aortic arch","Carotid","Portal vein"],"a":0,"why":"Source: deep leg veins."},{"q":"Neurons tolerate ischemia for:","opts":["3-4 min","20-30 min","Hours","Days"],"a":0,"why":"Myocardium 20-30 min."},{"q":"Best prognosis shock:","opts":["Young + hypovolemic","Old + septic","Old + cardiogenic","Young + cardiogenic"],"a":0,"why":"Worst: old + cardiogenic or septic."}],"cards":[{"f":"Virchow's triad","b":"Endothelium, flow, coagulability"},{"f":"Primary hypercoagulability","b":"Antithrombin III, protein C deficiency"},{"f":"Lines of Zahn","b":"Pale platelets + fibrin, dark RBCs"},{"f":"DIC","b":"Widespread microthrombi then bleeding"},{"f":"Saddle embolus","b":"Pulmonary artery bifurcation"},{"f":"Fat embolism","b":"Long-bone fracture, 1-3 days"},{"f":"Decompression sickness","b":"Nitrogen bubbles"},{"f":"Infarct shape","b":"Wedge, apex at vessel"},{"f":"Red infarct","b":"Venous, loose, dual circulation"},{"f":"White infarct","b":"Arterial, solid, end-arterial"},{"f":"Shock lung","b":"ARDS"},{"f":"Shock stages","b":"Compensation, progressive, decompensation"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-14"},
 {"id":"hemodynamics-1","system":"inflam","title":"Hemodynamic Disturbance 1: Hyperemia, Congestion, Edema, Hemostasis, Hemorrhage","url":"hemodynamics-1.html","summary":"Hyperemia vs congestion, nutmeg liver, pulmonary congestion, Starling forces, edema mechanisms and types, transudate vs exudate, hemostasis steps, fibrinolysis and hemorrhage.","points":["Hyperemia: active, arteriolar dilation, red","Congestion: passive, venous outflow down, cyanosis","Nutmeg liver: right heart failure, dark centre","Starling: arterial hydrostatic > oncotic, venous oncotic > hydrostatic","Edema: hydrostatic up, oncotic down, lymphatic block, permeability up, Na + water retention","Transudate SG < 1.012, protein < 3 g/dL; exudate opposite","Hemostasis: injury, spasm, platelet plug, coagulation, fibrinolysis","Petechiae 1-2 mm, purpura > 3 mm, ecchymoses 1-2 cm"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Hyperemia is:","opts":["Active, arteriolar dilation","Passive, venous obstruction","Lymphatic block","Platelet defect"],"a":0,"why":"Active with increased inflow; congestion is passive."},{"q":"Nutmeg liver is caused by:","opts":["Right-sided heart failure","Left-sided heart failure","Hepatitis A","Cholestasis"],"a":0,"why":"Chronic venous congestion."},{"q":"Peau d'orange is due to:","opts":["Lymphatic obstruction","Nephrotic syndrome","Heart failure","Cirrhosis"],"a":0,"why":"Breast carcinoma blocks lymphatics."},{"q":"Exudate protein:","opts":["> 3 g/dL","< 3 g/dL","Zero","Same as urine"],"a":0,"why":"SG > 1.012, permeability up."},{"q":"Platelet release reaction includes:","opts":["ADP, serotonin, TXA2","Plasmin","Fibrin","Collagen"],"a":0,"why":"Recruits more platelets."},{"q":"Purpura size:","opts":["> 3 mm","1-2 mm","1-2 cm","< 0.1 mm"],"a":0,"why":"Petechiae 1-2 mm, ecchymoses 1-2 cm."}],"cards":[{"f":"Hyperemia","b":"Active, inflow up, red"},{"f":"Congestion","b":"Passive, outflow down, cyanosis"},{"f":"Total body water","b":"60% lean weight; 2/3 intracellular"},{"f":"Arterial end","b":"Hydrostatic > oncotic"},{"f":"Venous end","b":"Oncotic > hydrostatic"},{"f":"Ascites","b":"Hydroperitoneum"},{"f":"Anasarca","b":"Severe generalized edema"},{"f":"Transudate","b":"SG < 1.012, protein < 3"},{"f":"Exudate","b":"SG > 1.012, protein > 3"},{"f":"Fibrinolysis","b":"Plasminogen to plasmin"},{"f":"Petechiae","b":"1-2 mm"},{"f":"Ecchymoses","b":"1-2 cm"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-14"},
 {"id":"cell-injury-56","system":"inflam","title":"Cell Injury 5-6: Necrosis, Apoptosis, Adaptation, Accumulations","url":"cell-injury-56.html","summary":"Necrosis and its patterns, outcomes, apoptosis and its pathways, hypertrophy, hyperplasia, atrophy, metaplasia, intracellular accumulations, pigments, calcification and cellular aging.","points":["Necrosis: uncontrolled, inflammation; pyknosis, karyorrhexis, karyolysis","6 patterns: coagulative, liquefactive, caseous, gangrenous, fat, fibrinoid","Apoptosis: programmed, caspases, no inflammation","Intrinsic: BCL2 family, cytochrome c, caspase-9","Extrinsic: Fas, FADD, caspase-8","Hypertrophy size, hyperplasia number, atrophy, metaplasia","Dystrophic vs metastatic calcification","Telomere shortening and telomerase"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Fibrinoid necrosis is characteristic of:","opts":["Immune reactions in vessel walls","TB","Pancreatitis","Brain infarct"],"a":0,"why":"Antigen-antibody complexes leak into vessel walls: bright pink on H&E."},{"q":"Caseous necrosis is typical of:","opts":["Tuberculosis","Brain infarct","Acute pancreatitis","Dry gangrene"],"a":0,"why":"Cheese-like, inside a granuloma."},{"q":"Caspase-8 is activated by the:","opts":["Extrinsic pathway","Intrinsic pathway","Both equally","Neither"],"a":0,"why":"Intrinsic activates caspase-9; extrinsic activates caspase-8 and 10."},{"q":"Which protein prevents cytochrome c leakage?","opts":["BCL2","BAX","BAK","FADD"],"a":0,"why":"BCL2, BCL-XL, MCL1 are anti-apoptotic."},{"q":"Hyperplasia differs from hypertrophy by:","opts":["Increased cell number","Increased cell size","Decreased cell size","Cell replacement"],"a":0,"why":"Hyperplasia number, hypertrophy size."},{"q":"Barrett esophagus is:","opts":["Squamous to columnar metaplasia","Columnar to squamous","Atrophy","Hyperplasia"],"a":0,"why":"Risk: adenocarcinoma."}],"cards":[{"f":"Necrosis nuclear changes","b":"Pyknosis, karyorrhexis, karyolysis"},{"f":"Coagulative necrosis","b":"Ischemia, infarction, structure preserved"},{"f":"Liquefactive necrosis","b":"Pus, bacteria, brain"},{"f":"Caseous necrosis","b":"TB, granuloma"},{"f":"Fat necrosis","b":"Pancreatic lipases, saponification"},{"f":"Fibrinoid necrosis","b":"Immune, vessel wall"},{"f":"Apoptosis","b":"Programmed, no inflammation"},{"f":"Intrinsic pathway","b":"Mitochondria, cytochrome c, caspase-9"},{"f":"Extrinsic pathway","b":"Fas, FADD, caspase-8"},{"f":"Executioner caspases","b":"3 and 6"},{"f":"Anti-apoptotic","b":"BCL2, BCL-XL, MCL1"},{"f":"Pro-apoptotic","b":"BAX, BAK"},{"f":"Hypertrophy","b":"Cell size up"},{"f":"Hyperplasia","b":"Cell number up"},{"f":"Barrett esophagus","b":"Squamous to columnar, adenocarcinoma"},{"f":"Dystrophic calcification","b":"Dead tissue, normal calcium"},{"f":"Metastatic calcification","b":"Viable tissue, hypercalcemia"},{"f":"Lipofuscin","b":"Wear-and-tear, aging"},{"f":"Hemosiderin","b":"Iron storage"},{"f":"Telomerase","b":"Germ and stem cells"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-14"},
 {"id":"cell-injury-34","system":"inflam","title":"Cell Injury 3-4: Mechanisms, Free Radicals, Ischemia","url":"cell-injury-34.html","summary":"Homeostasis, adaptation and injury, causes, ATP depletion, membrane and DNA damage with p53, free radicals, calcium, ischemia and reperfusion, chemical and microbial injury, reversible injury.","points":["Stress beyond adaptation = cell injury (reversible / irreversible)","Hypoxia: ischemia, inadequate oxygenation, decreased O2 carrying capacity","ATP < 5-10%: pump failure, glycolysis, decreased protein synthesis","Membrane damage: 5 mechanisms, 3 membranes","p53: G1 arrest, repair, else apoptosis","Free radicals: catalase, antioxidants, metal-binding proteins","Ca2+ up: phospholipase, protease, endonuclease, ATPase","Reperfusion injury: ROS, Ca2+, neutrophils, complement"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Hallmark of reversible cell injury:","opts":["Cell swelling","Karyolysis","Pyknosis","Karyorrhexis"],"a":0,"why":"Cell swelling (hydropic change) is the earliest sign."},{"q":"ATP depletion causes all EXCEPT:","opts":["Na/K pump failure","Glycolysis shift","Increased protein synthesis","Ribosome detachment"],"a":2,"why":"Protein synthesis decreases."},{"q":"After DNA damage, p53 first:","opts":["Causes apoptosis immediately","Arrests the cell cycle in G1","Mutates","Activates caspases only"],"a":1,"why":"G1 arrest gives time to repair; apoptosis if repair fails."},{"q":"Which enzyme decomposes H2O2 to water and oxygen?","opts":["Catalase","Protease","Phospholipase","Endonuclease"],"a":0,"why":"Catalase."},{"q":"Reperfusion injury mechanisms include:","opts":["Oxidative stress","Ca2+ overload","Complement activation","All of the above"],"a":3,"why":"Plus inflammation (neutrophils)."},{"q":"Acetaminophen injures the liver through:","opts":["Direct toxicity","A toxic metabolite","Ischemia","Hepatitis virus"],"a":1,"why":"Converted to a toxic product in the liver."}],"cards":[{"f":"Homeostasis","b":"Stable internal environment of the cell"},{"f":"Hypoxia","b":"Decreased oxygen supply"},{"f":"Ischemia","b":"Decreased blood supply"},{"f":"ATP < 5-10%","b":"Critical functions fail"},{"f":"Na/K pump failure","b":"Na + water in, cell swelling"},{"f":"p53","b":"Guardian of the genome"},{"f":"p53 mutation","b":"Cancer"},{"f":"Free radical","b":"Unpaired electron"},{"f":"Catalase","b":"H2O2 to H2O + O2"},{"f":"Ca2+ stores","b":"ER + mitochondria"},{"f":"Phospholipase","b":"Breaks membrane"},{"f":"Endonuclease","b":"Fragments DNA"},{"f":"HIF-1","b":"Angiogenesis + glycolysis"},{"f":"Reperfusion injury","b":"Damage after blood returns"},{"f":"Acetaminophen","b":"Toxic metabolite, liver injury"},{"f":"Hydropic change","b":"Reversible swelling"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-14"},
 {"id":"gen-12","system":"genetic","title":"Genetic Disorders: Lectures 1 & 2","url":"gen-12.html","summary":"Normal karyotype, classification of genetic disease (single-gene, chromosomal, multifactorial), mutation types, Mendelian patterns (AD, AR, X-linked), epigenetics, numerical and structural chromosomal abnormalities and Down syndrome.","points":["Karyotype: 46 chromosomes, arrested at metaphase, G banding most used","Classical: single-gene, chromosomal, multifactorial","Mutations: missense, nonsense, silent, frameshift, triplet repeat","AD: one mutated allele, sibling risk 50% · AR: both alleles, sibling risk 25%","X-linked: no father-to-son transmission; carrier mother gives 50% affected sons","Down syndrome: regular trisomy 21 (95%), translocation (4%), mosaic (1%)"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which banding technique is most commonly used in karyotyping?","opts":["Q banding","G banding (Giemsa)","R banding","C banding"],"a":1,"why":"G banding with Giemsa stain is the most used method."},{"q":"A missense mutation causes:","opts":["A premature stop codon","No change in the amino acid","One amino acid replaced by another","A shift in the reading frame"],"a":2,"why":"Missense = a single base change that replaces one amino acid."},{"q":"Recurrence risk for a sibling in an autosomal recessive disorder is:","opts":["50%","25%","100%","12.5%"],"a":1,"why":"Both parents are carriers, so each child has a 25% chance of being affected."},{"q":"Which of these is X-linked?","opts":["Huntington disease","Cystic fibrosis","Duchenne muscular dystrophy","Marfan syndrome"],"a":2,"why":"Duchenne is X-linked recessive."},{"q":"Regular trisomy 21 (95% of Down syndrome) is caused by:","opts":["Robertsonian translocation","Non-disjunction, usually maternal","Isochromosome 21","Mosaicism"],"a":1,"why":"Maternal non-disjunction accounts for about 95% of regular trisomy 21."},{"q":"t(9;22), the Philadelphia chromosome, is associated with:","opts":["Down syndrome","Cri du chat","Chronic myeloid leukemia","Turner syndrome"],"a":2,"why":"Reciprocal translocation t(9;22) is the hallmark of CML."}],"cards":[{"f":"كم كروموسوم بالخلية الجسدية؟","b":"46 = 22 زوج جسمي + 2 جنسي"},{"f":"أي صبغة بالكاريوتايب؟ وأي مرحلة؟","b":"Giemsa (G banding) · metaphase"},{"f":"شو أنواع الأمراض الوراثية الكلاسيكية؟","b":"single-gene · chromosomal · multifactorial"},{"f":"الفرق بين hereditary و congenital؟","b":"hereditary من الأهل · congenital موجود عند الولادة"},{"f":"أي طفرة بتعمل stop codon؟","b":"Nonsense (مثل β0-thalassemia)"},{"f":"الفرق بين missense و silent؟","b":"missense بيبدّل حمض أميني · silent ما بيبدّل"},{"f":"خطر الإعادة بالإخوة بـ AD؟","b":"50%"},{"f":"خطر الإعادة بالإخوة بـ AR؟","b":"25%"},{"f":"نمط وراثة Huntington؟","b":"AD"},{"f":"نمط وراثة Cystic fibrosis؟","b":"AR (الأكثر شيوعاً)"},{"f":"نمط وراثة Duchenne؟","b":"X-linked recessive"},{"f":"في انتقال أب ← إبن بـ X-linked؟","b":"لا — بنات الأب المصاب كلهن حاملات"},{"f":"شو ال hemizygous؟","b":"الذكر عندو X واحد، فبيبيّن المرض"},{"f":"الفرق بين euploid و aneuploid؟","b":"euploid مضاعف n طبيعي · aneuploid زيادة/نقص كروموسوم"},{"f":"سبب أغلب الـ aneuploidy؟","b":"Non-disjunction (و anaphase lag)"},{"f":"Robertsonian translocation بين أي كروموسومات؟","b":"acrocentric: مثلاً 14;21"},{"f":"Philadelphia chromosome؟","b":"Reciprocal 9;22 ← CML"},{"f":"Cri du chat؟","b":"deletion بالكروموسوم 5"},{"f":"Trisomies جسمية؟","b":"21 Down · 18 Edwards · 13 Patau"},{"f":"أنواع Down ونسبها؟","b":"Regular 95% · Translocation 4% · Mosaic ~1%"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"gen-34","system":"genetic","title":"Genetic Disorders: Lectures 3 & 4","url":"gen-34.html","summary":"Single-gene disorders (PKU, cystic fibrosis, Marfan, Ehlers-Danlos, G6PD deficiency), cell-growth defects, multifactorial disease, non-classic inheritance and genetic analysis (prenatal, carrier screening, karyotyping, FISH).","points":["5 classes: enzyme, membrane/transport, structural protein, drug reaction, cell growth","PKU: phenylalanine hydroxylase deficiency (AR)","Cystic fibrosis: CFTR chloride transport defect (AR)","Marfan: FBN1, fibrillin 1 (AD) · Ehlers-Danlos: collagen I and III","Multifactorial: genes + environment, recurrence 2-7%","FISH: probe hybridization; deletion = signal lost"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Marfan syndrome is caused by a mutation in which gene?","opts":["COL1A1","FBN1 (chromosome 15)","CFTR","PAH"],"a":1,"why":"FBN1 encodes fibrillin 1, the scaffold for elastin."},{"q":"PKU results from deficiency of:","opts":["Galactose-1-phosphate uridyltransferase","Phenylalanine hydroxylase","Glucose-6-phosphatase","Homogentisate oxidase"],"a":1,"why":"Without PAH, phenylalanine is converted to phenylpyruvate instead of tyrosine."},{"q":"Cystic fibrosis involves defective:","opts":["Chloride transport (CFTR)","Collagen synthesis","Iron absorption","Clotting factor VIII"],"a":0,"why":"CFTR chloride defect leads to thick mucus."},{"q":"Primaquine can cause severe hemolysis in:","opts":["Marfan syndrome","G6PD deficiency","Cystic fibrosis","PKU"],"a":1,"why":"G6PD protects red cells from oxidative stress; primaquine blocks it."},{"q":"In FISH, a translocation appears as:","opts":["Signal lost","Extra signals","Signals that move or merge","No change"],"a":2,"why":"Deletion = signal lost; duplication = extra signals; translocation = signals move/merge."},{"q":"Non-invasive prenatal screening (NIPS) can:","opts":["Give a definitive diagnosis","Show risk only","Replace karyotyping","Detect all genes"],"a":1,"why":"NIPS shows risk only; invasive prenatal diagnosis (amniocentesis or CVS) confirms."}],"cards":[{"f":"كم فئة لأمراض الجين الواحد؟ {{single-gene}}","b":"5: إنزيم · غشاء · بنية · دوا · نمو"},{"f":"وراثة PKU؟ والإنزيم الناقص؟","b":"جسمية متنحية {{AR}} · PAH"},{"f":"بـ PKU: بدل tyrosine، الـ Phe بيتحوّل لشو؟","b":"phenylpyruvate"},{"f":"بروتين CF؟","b":"CFTR (نقل الكلور {{chloride}})"},{"f":"وراثة Marfan وجينو؟","b":"سائدة {{AD}} · FBN1 عالكروموسوم 15"},{"f":"شو نتيجة فحص nitroprusside بـ Marfan؟","b":"سلبي (إيجابي بـ homocystinuria)"},{"f":"وراثة EDS؟ وأي كولاجين؟","b":"سائدة {{AD}} · النوع I و III"},{"f":"G6PD + primaquine = شو؟","b":"انحلال دم {{hemolysis}}"},{"f":"كم نسبة السرطانات العيلية؟ {{familial}}","b":"5% (أغلبها سائدة)"},{"f":"خطر التكرار بالمتعددة العوامل؟","b":"2–7% درجة أولى {{first-degree}} · 9% بعد أخوين"},{"f":"الأنواع الأربعة لاستثناءات مندل؟","b":"Triplet · Mitochondrial · Imprinting · Gonadal mosaicism"},{"f":"شو هو NIPS؟","b":"سونار + مؤشرات دم الأم · خطر بس، مش تشخيص"},{"f":"إجراءات الفحص الباضع؟ {{IPD}}","b":"بزل السلى {{amniocentesis}} و CVS"},{"f":"استطبابات الفحص قبل الولادة؟ {{prenatal}}","b":"عمر الأم >34 · ولد سابق بشذوذ كروموسومي · جنس لمرض X-linked"},{"f":"شو أشيع عينة لفحص الحاملين؟ {{carrier screening}}","b":"لعاب {{saliva}}"},{"f":"خطوات الكاريوتايب؟","b":"زرع + metaphase ← صبغ ← مجهر/تصوير ← ترتيب أزواج"},{"f":"خطوات FISH؟","b":"فصل ← مسبار ← ارتباط ← مجهر فلوري"},{"f":"شو بيصير بالـ FISH إذا في حذف؟ {{deletion}}","b":"الإشارة بتختفي"},{"f":"كروموسوم فيلادلفيا؟","b":"انتقال {{translocation}} · CML"},{"f":"كم فئة بتستفيد من الخدمات الوراثية؟","b":"10 فئات"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"imm-hyper","system":"immuno","title":"Hypersensitivity Reactions","url":"imm-hyper.html","summary":"Four types of hypersensitivity: Type I (IgE, immediate), Type II (antibody-mediated), Type III (immune complex) and Type IV (T-cell mediated, delayed), with mechanisms, examples and a comparison table.","points":["Type I: IgE, minutes, mast cells; asthma, hay fever, anaphylaxis","Type II: IgG/IgM vs cell surface; complement, ADCC, cellular dysfunction","Type III: immune complexes; Arthus, SLE, serum sickness","Type IV: T cells, 48-72 h; granuloma, Mantoux, contact dermatitis","CD8+ CTLs kill virus-infected and tumor cells"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which antibody mediates Type I hypersensitivity?","opts":["IgG","IgM","IgE","IgA"],"a":2,"why":"IgE binds mast cells and triggers immediate reactions."},{"q":"Graves disease is an example of Type II acting through:","opts":["Complement lysis","Cellular dysfunction (stimulating TSH receptor)","ADCC","Immune complex deposition"],"a":1,"why":"Antibodies stimulate the TSH receptor without cell injury."},{"q":"The Arthus reaction is:","opts":["Local immune complex vasculitis with necrosis","Anaphylaxis","Granuloma formation","Antibody-mediated lysis"],"a":0,"why":"Type III: large complexes cause fibrinoid necrosis in the skin."},{"q":"The Mantoux test reaction peaks at:","opts":["5-10 minutes","8-12 hours","24-72 hours","7 days"],"a":2,"why":"Type IV (DTH) reaches its peak 24-72 hours after PPD injection."},{"q":"Serum sickness is which type?","opts":["Type I","Type II","Type III","Type IV"],"a":2,"why":"Foreign proteins form immune complexes that deposit in vessels and joints."},{"q":"Which cells kill virus-infected and tumor cells in Type IV?","opts":["CD4+ helper T cells","CD8+ cytotoxic T cells","Mast cells","Eosinophils"],"a":1,"why":"CD8+ CTLs kill antigen-bearing cells."}],"cards":[{"f":"شو الـ Hypersensitivity؟","b":"رد مناعي مبالغ فيه ومؤذي ضد مستضد عند شخص حسّاس"},{"f":"شو بيلزم قبل ما يصير فرط حساسية؟","b":"Priming (تعرّض سابق)"},{"f":"كم نوع؟ وشو أول حروفهم؟","b":"4: ACID — Anaphylactic · Cytotoxic · Immune complex · Delayed"},{"f":"الجسم المضاد بـ Type I؟","b":"IgE"},{"f":"إيمتى بيصير Type I؟","b":"5-10 دقايق"},{"f":"الخلايا الأساسية بـ Type I؟","b":"Mast cells + eosinophils"},{"f":"شو الأتوبي atopic؟","b":"IgE مرتفع بالمصل + قابلية وراثية"},{"f":"علامات الأنافيلاكسيس؟","b":"Hypotension · Urticaria · Dyspnea"},{"f":"الأجسام بـ Type II؟","b":"IgG (غالباً) · IgM (نادراً)"},{"f":"3 تأثيرات Type II؟","b":"Complement · ADCC · Cellular dysfunction"},{"f":"C3b شو بيعمل؟","b":"Opsonin ← phagocytosis"},{"f":"بـ ADCC شو بتستعمل NK؟","b":"Perforin + granzyme ← apoptosis"},{"f":"Graves بـ Type II شو سببو؟","b":"أجسام مضادة بتنبّه مستقبل TSH ← thyrotoxicosis"},{"f":"C5a شو بيعمل؟","b":"Chemotaxis للعدلات والوحيدات"},{"f":"أجسام Type III؟","b":"IgG · IgM · أحياناً IgA"},{"f":"Arthus reaction؟","b":"نخر موضّع من immune complex vasculitis"},{"f":"SLE: ضد شو؟","b":"Nuclear components (DNA, histones)"},{"f":"Serum sickness: إيمتى بيتكوّن الجسم المضاد؟","b":"7-12 يوم"},{"f":"Type IV: كم بيتأخر؟","b":"48-72 ساعة (DTH)"},{"f":"Mantoux: شو بيشوفو مجهرياً؟","b":"Perivascular cuffing (CD4+ + macrophages)"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"imm-def","system":"immuno","title":"Immunodeficiency & AIDS","url":"imm-def.html","summary":"Primary immunodeficiencies (B-cell, T-cell, complement, phagocytic), secondary immunodeficiency, AIDS and its opportunistic infections and neoplasms, and Kaposi sarcoma.","points":["PID groups: B-cell, T-cell, complement, phagocytic","SCID (X-linked cytokine receptor / AR ADA), DiGeorge (22q11), Hyper-IgM (CD40L)","Bruton (Btk), CVID (no plasma cells), IgA deficiency (1:850)","CGD (NADPH oxidase), Chediak-Higashi (no phagosome-lysosome fusion)","C2 most common, C3 most serious, C5-C9 Neisseria","AIDS: HIV, opportunistic infections, neoplasms (Kaposi, HHV8)"],"mcqs":[{"q":"X-linked hyper-IgM syndrome is caused by a mutation in:","opts":["Btk","CD40L","ADA","NADPH oxidase"],"a":1,"why":"CD40L on CD4 T cells fails to bind CD40, blocking isotype switching."},{"q":"DiGeorge syndrome is associated with deletion of:","opts":["22q11","21q22","15q11","5p"],"a":0,"why":"Thymic aplasia with 22q11 deletion (CATCH 22)."},{"q":"Bruton agammaglobulinemia involves which enzyme?","opts":["Btk (B-cell tyrosine kinase)","ADA","NADPH oxidase","Proteinase"],"a":0,"why":"Btk mutation blocks pre-B cell maturation."},{"q":"Chronic granulomatous disease results from deficiency of:","opts":["ADA","CD40L","NADPH oxidase","C3"],"a":2,"why":"No respiratory burst means no ROS killing."},{"q":"Deficiency of C5-C9 predisposes to:","opts":["Neisserial infections","Pneumocystis pneumonia","Cryptococcus meningitis","Candida esophagitis"],"a":0,"why":"Late complement components are needed for lysis of Neisseria."},{"q":"The AIDS-defining tumor caused by HHV8 is:","opts":["Burkitt lymphoma","Kaposi sarcoma","Cervical carcinoma","Hepatocellular carcinoma"],"a":1,"why":"Kaposi sarcoma: HHV8 plus altered T-cell immunity."}],"cards":[{"f":"الفرق بين PID و SID؟","b":"Primary = وراثي · Secondary = مكتسب (الأشيع)"},{"f":"شو 4 مجموعات PID؟","b":"B-cell · T-cell · Complement · Phagocytic"},{"f":"أشيع SCID؟","b":"X-linked (50-60%) cytokine receptor"},{"f":"سبب AR SCID؟","b":"ADA deficiency"},{"f":"DiGeorge: أي كروموسوم؟","b":"22q11 deletion"},{"f":"CATCH 22؟","b":"Cardiac · Abnormal facies · Thymic aplasia · Cleft palate · Hypocalcemia"},{"f":"Hyper-IgM: أي طفرة؟","b":"CD40L (X-linked)"},{"f":"Hyper-IgM: أي خلل؟","b":"Isotype switching"},{"f":"Bruton: أي إنزيم؟","b":"B-cell tyrosine kinase (Btk)"},{"f":"Bruton: إيمتى الأعراض؟","b":"بعد 6 شهور، بالصبيان"},{"f":"CVID: شو المشكلة؟","b":"B cells ما بتتمايز لـ plasma cells"},{"f":"CVID: أي سرطانات لاحقاً؟","b":"Gastric cancer + lymphoma"},{"f":"أشيع نقص مناعة خلقي؟","b":"Isolated IgA deficiency (1:850)"},{"f":"CGD: أي إنزيم؟","b":"NADPH oxidase ← respiratory burst"},{"f":"Chediak-Higashi: شو الخلل؟","b":"No phagosome-lysosome fusion"},{"f":"وظايف المتمّم؟","b":"Inflammation · direct killing · opsonization"},{"f":"أشيع نقص متمّم؟","b":"C2"},{"f":"نقص C5-C9 بيعطي؟","b":"Neisserial infections / meningitis"},{"f":"ثلاثية AIDS؟","b":"Opportunistic infections · neoplasms · neurologic"},{"f":"Kaposi: أي فيروس؟","b":"HHV8"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"imm-tol","system":"immuno","title":"Tolerance, Autoimmunity & Transplantation","url":"imm-tol.html","summary":"Central and peripheral tolerance, autoimmune diseases and their triggers, Sjogren syndrome, graft rejection (hyperacute, acute, chronic), ways to improve graft survival, and graft versus host disease.","points":["Central tolerance: thymus (T) and bone marrow (B), apoptosis","Peripheral tolerance: anergy, Treg suppression, deletion","Triggers: costimulators, molecular mimicry, polyclonal B activation, modified or sequestered antigens","Sjogren: anti-SS-A (Ro) and SS-B (La), sicca syndrome","Rejection: hyperacute (preformed Ab), acute, chronic (fibrosis)","GVHD: donor CD8+ T cells attack the host"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Central tolerance occurs in:","opts":["Spleen and lymph nodes","Thymus (T cells) and bone marrow (B cells)","Liver","Skin"],"a":1,"why":"Immature self-reactive lymphocytes die by apoptosis in central organs."},{"q":"Anergy means:","opts":["Apoptosis of the cell","Irreversible inactivation without death","Suppression by Treg","Antibody production"],"a":1,"why":"The cell survives but is functionally inactive."},{"q":"Rheumatic heart disease is an example of:","opts":["Sequestered antigen release","Molecular mimicry","Polyclonal B activation","Epitope modification by smoking"],"a":1,"why":"Anti-streptococcal antibodies cross-react with myocardial proteins."},{"q":"Sjogren syndrome is associated with antibodies against:","opts":["dsDNA and Sm","SS-A (Ro) and SS-B (La)","Centromere","Mitochondria"],"a":1,"why":"Detected in up to 90% of patients."},{"q":"Hyperacute rejection is caused by:","opts":["Donor T cells","Preformed antibodies in the recipient","Cytokine-driven fibrosis","Immunosuppressive therapy"],"a":1,"why":"Previous transplant or transfusion leaves preformed antibodies that bind graft endothelium."},{"q":"The main effector cell in GVHD is:","opts":["Recipient B cell","Donor CD8+ T cell","Recipient neutrophil","Donor mast cell"],"a":1,"why":"Donor CD8+ T cells attack proliferating recipient cells."}],"cards":[{"f":"شو هو self-tolerance؟","b":"المناعة ما بتهاجم مستضدات الجسم"},{"f":"وين بتتعلّم T cells؟","b":"Thymus"},{"f":"central tolerance: شو بيصير؟","b":"الخلايا المعادية للذات بتموت بالـ apoptosis"},{"f":"أماكن central tolerance؟","b":"Thymus (T) · Bone marrow (B)"},{"f":"3 طرق peripheral tolerance؟","b":"Anergy · Treg · Deletion"},{"f":"Anergy؟","b":"تعطيل بدون موت"},{"f":"طريقتين أذى بالمناعة الذاتية؟","b":"CD8 cytotoxic T cells · autoantibodies"},{"f":"أقوى رابط جيني؟","b":"Ankylosing spondylitis ↔ HLA-B27"},{"f":"مثال molecular mimicry؟","b":"Rheumatic heart disease"},{"f":"فيروسات polyclonal B activation؟","b":"EBV · HIV"},{"f":"التدخين مع أي مرض؟","b":"RA (modified self antigen)"},{"f":"UV بيعمل شو؟","b":"بيكشف nuclear antigens ثم lupus"},{"f":"Sjögren: أجسام ضد شو؟","b":"SS-A (Ro) · SS-B (La)"},{"f":"Sjögren: عمر وجنس؟","b":"نساء 50-60"},{"f":"Mikulicz syndrome؟","b":"التهاب الغدد الدمعية واللعابية"},{"f":"Sjögren: سرطان لاحق؟","b":"Marginal zone lymphoma"},{"f":"أكتر عضو بيتزرع؟","b":"Kidney"},{"f":"Hyperacute: السبب؟","b":"Preformed antibodies (نقل دم / زرع سابق)"},{"f":"Chronic rejection: الصفة الرئيسية؟","b":"Fibrosis · onion skinning"},{"f":"GVHD: الخلايا الأساسية؟","b":"CD8+ T cells"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"imm-amy","system":"immuno","title":"Amyloidosis","url":"imm-amy.html","summary":"Amyloid as an extracellular pathologic protein deposit (95% fibrils, 5% non-fibrillar), AL vs AA and minor fibril proteins, systemic, hereditary and localized types, clinical features, diagnosis, special stains and morphology.","points":["Amyloid fibrils: 7.5-10 nm, non-branching; 95% fibrils + 5% AP, ApoE, GAGs","AL: Ig light chains, plasma cells, myeloma (primary); AA: SAA from liver, chronic inflammation (secondary)","Others: TTR, beta2-microglobulin (hemodialysis), Abeta (Alzheimer), endocrine, prion","Hereditary: FMF (AR, pyrin), familial neuropathies (mutant TTR); localized: single organ, AL","Diagnosis: rectal biopsy, fat aspirate + Congo red (apple-green under polarized light), EM definite"],"mcqs":[{"q":"AL amyloid is derived from:","opts":["Serum amyloid A","Immunoglobulin light chains","Transthyretin","Beta2-microglobulin"],"a":1,"why":"AL comes from plasma cell light chains, linked to multiple myeloma."},{"q":"AA amyloid is derived from:","opts":["Light chains","SAA made by the liver","Calcitonin","Prion protein"],"a":1,"why":"IL-6 and IL-1 raise SAA in chronic inflammation."},{"q":"Amyloid under polarized light after Congo red shows:","opts":["Blue-violet","Apple-green birefringence","Rose pink","Yellow"],"a":1,"why":"Apple-green birefringence is characteristic."},{"q":"Best biopsy site for amyloidosis:","opts":["Skin","Rectum","Muscle","Lung"],"a":1,"why":"Rectal biopsy is the best site."},{"q":"Amyloid of long-term hemodialysis is:","opts":["AL","AA","Beta2-microglobulin","Abeta"],"a":2,"why":"Beta2-microglobulin is not filtered by dialysis membranes."},{"q":"Familial Mediterranean fever is inherited as:","opts":["Autosomal dominant","Autosomal recessive","X-linked","Mitochondrial"],"a":1,"why":"FMF: autosomal recessive, pyrin gene, AA fibrils."}],"cards":[{"f":"AL مشتق من شو؟","b":"Immunoglobulin light chains (plasma cells)"},{"f":"AL مع أي مرض؟","b":"Multiple myeloma (primary)"},{"f":"AA مشتق من؟","b":"SAA (liver)"},{"f":"شو بيزيد SAA؟","b":"IL-6 + IL-1 (inflammation)"},{"f":"TTR بينقل شو؟","b":"Thyroxine + retinol"},{"f":"أميلويد الغسيل الكلوي؟","b":"β2-microglobulin"},{"f":"أميلويد Alzheimer؟","b":"Aβ (from AβPP)"},{"f":"Prion مثال مرض؟","b":"Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (CJD)"},{"f":"قطر الخيوط؟","b":"7.5-10 nm"},{"f":"نسبة الخيوط؟","b":"95% (5% non-fibrillar)"},{"f":"مكوّنات non-fibrillar؟","b":"AP · ApoE · GAGs"},{"f":"Bence Jones protein؟","b":"Light chains بالبول والدم (myeloma)"},{"f":"Secondary أسبابو؟","b":"TB · bronchiectasis · osteomyelitis · RA · IBD"},{"f":"Senile عمرو؟","b":"70-80 سنة (normal TTR)"},{"f":"FMF وراثتو؟","b":"Autosomal recessive (pyrin, AA)"},{"f":"Localized أشكالو؟","b":"Nodular mass: lung · larynx · skin · tongue (AL)"},{"f":"أفضل مكان خزعة؟","b":"Rectum"},{"f":"أشهر صبغة؟","b":"Congo red (apple-green under polarized light)"},{"f":"التشخيص النهائي؟","b":"Electron microscopy"},{"f":"شكل العضو؟","b":"Enlarged · firm · waxy"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"inf-heal","system":"inflam","title":"Healing & Repair (Inflammation 5-6)","url":"inf-heal.html","summary":"Repair by regeneration or fibrous scar, labile/stable/permanent cells, granulation tissue and angiogenesis, ECM deposition and remodelling, healing by first and second intention, wound strength, factors affecting healing and complications (hypertrophic scar, keloid, dehiscence, contracture).","points":["Regeneration (normal tissue) vs healing (fibrous scar)","Steps: scavenging, regeneration, granulation tissue, ECM deposition, remodelling","Labile and stable cells regenerate; permanent cells (neurons, cardiac myocytes) do not","Granulation tissue: angiogenesis (VEGF) + fibroblasts (PDGF, FGF); pink, soft, leaky","1st intention: clean opposed edges; 2nd intention: separated edges, more granulation, contraction by myofibroblasts","Infection is the most important local factor delaying healing; keloid extends beyond wound boundaries"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which cell type cannot regenerate?","opts":["Epidermal cells","Hepatocytes","Cardiac myocytes","GI epithelium"],"a":2,"why":"Cardiac myocytes and neurons are permanent cells."},{"q":"The hallmark of healing is:","opts":["Fibrin clot","Granulation tissue","Scab","Keloid"],"a":1,"why":"Granulation tissue is pink, soft, granular and leaky."},{"q":"Angiogenesis is stimulated mainly by:","opts":["PDGF","VEGF and angiopoietin","IL-1","TNF"],"a":1,"why":"VEGF and angiopoietin drive new vessel formation."},{"q":"Wound contraction is caused by:","opts":["Neutrophils","Macrophages","Myofibroblasts","Hepatocytes"],"a":2,"why":"Myofibroblasts have smooth-muscle features and pull wound edges."},{"q":"Which is the single most important local cause of delayed healing?","opts":["Foreign body","Infection","Wound size","Early motion"],"a":1,"why":"Infection causes persistent injury and inflammation."},{"q":"Keloid differs from hypertrophic scar because it:","opts":["Is flat","Extends beyond the original wound and does not regress","Contains no collagen","Is caused by deficiency"],"a":1,"why":"Keloid grows beyond wound boundaries and is more common in black people."}],"cards":[{"f":"Repair شو بيرجّع؟","b":"Tissue architecture + function"},{"f":"Regeneration معناها؟","b":"Tissue returns to normal"},{"f":"Healing بتنتج شو؟","b":"Fibrous tissue → scar"},{"f":"Fibrosis بمكان فيه exudate؟","b":"Organization"},{"f":"أول خطوة بالشفاء؟","b":"Scavenging (macrophages)"},{"f":"Labile cells مثال؟","b":"Epidermis · GI epithelium"},{"f":"Stable cells مثال؟","b":"Hepatocytes (G0)"},{"f":"Permanent cells؟","b":"Neurons · cardiac myocytes"},{"f":"علامة الشفاء المميّزة؟","b":"Granulation tissue"},{"f":"Angiogenesis محفّزها؟","b":"VEGF + angiopoietin"},{"f":"EPCs من وين؟","b":"Bone marrow"},{"f":"PDGF معناها؟","b":"Platelet-derived growth factor"},{"f":"الخلية الرئيسية للـ ECM؟","b":"Fibroblast"},{"f":"ECM deposition بيبدأ؟","b":"Day 3-5"},{"f":"Metalloproteinases بتحتاج؟","b":"Zinc"},{"f":"Neutrophils بيوصلو؟","b":"24 hours"},{"f":"Neovascularization الذروة؟","b":"Day 5"},{"f":"Wound contraction بسبب؟","b":"Myofibroblasts"},{"f":"أهم سبب موضعي لتأخير الشفاء؟","b":"Infection"},{"f":"Keloid بتتميّز بـ؟","b":"Beyond wound boundaries · no regression"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"inf-out","system":"inflam","title":"Inflammation 3-4: Outcomes, Chronic & Granulomas","url":"inf-out.html","summary":"Outcomes of acute inflammation (resolution, scarring, abscess, chronic), six morphologic types, lymphatics, chronic inflammation, macrophages, granulomatous inflammation and systemic effects of inflammation.","points":["5 signs: redness, heat, swelling, pain, loss of function (mediators + leukocyte damage)","Vasodilation → redness + heat; permeability → edema → swelling","Outcome depends on injury, site, host response","6 types: catarrhal, serous, fibrinous, suppurative, ulceration, pseudomembranous","Chronic: mononuclear cells, destruction, repair; no vascular response","Granuloma: epithelioid macrophages + lymphocyte collar + giant cell; foreign body vs immune","Systemic: fever (prostaglandins), CRP (IL-6), leukocytosis (CSFs), septic shock (TNF)"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Swelling in acute inflammation results mainly from:","opts":["Vasodilation","Increased vascular permeability with edema","Leukocytosis","Fever"],"a":1,"why":"Vasodilation gives redness + heat; permeability lets fluid and protein leak, causing edema."},{"q":"Which is NOT a factor deciding the outcome of acute inflammation?","opts":["Type and severity of injury","Site affected","Host response","Patient's blood group"],"a":3,"why":"Outcome depends on injury, site, and host response."},{"q":"Pus is best described as:","opts":["Protein-poor fluid","Dead neutrophils, debris, microbes and fluid from liquefaction","Fibrin only","Clear blister fluid"],"a":1,"why":"Lysosomal enzymes liquefy tissue; pus always contains bacteria."},{"q":"Pseudomembranous inflammation occurs only in:","opts":["Colon and oropharynx","Lung and pleura","Skin and joints","Kidney and liver"],"a":0,"why":"Classically Clostridium difficile colitis."},{"q":"Which feature is absent in chronic inflammation compared with acute?","opts":["Tissue destruction","Mononuclear cells","Vascular response (heat, redness, edema)","Attempts at repair"],"a":2,"why":"Chronic inflammation lacks the vascular response."},{"q":"A granuloma consists of:","opts":["Neutrophils around pus","Epithelioid macrophages with a lymphocyte collar, giant cells, fibroblasts","Fibrin and fibroblasts","Eosinophils and mast cells"],"a":1,"why":"Central necrosis may be present."},{"q":"Septic shock in severe infection is driven mainly by high levels of:","opts":["IL-6","TNF","CSFs","Interferon-gamma"],"a":1,"why":"TNF causes low BP, DIC and metabolic abnormalities."}],"cards":[{"f":"5 علامات الالتهاب الحاد؟","b":"Redness · Heat · Swelling · Pain · Loss of function"},{"f":"الاحمرار والحرارة من؟ والانتفاخ من؟","b":"Vasodilation · ↑ Permeability → edema"},{"f":"حاجز الوعاء الدموي؟","b":"Endothelium + tight junctions + basement membrane"},{"f":"3 عوامل مصير الالتهاب الحاد؟","b":"Injury type/severity · site · host response"},{"f":"4 مصائر؟","b":"Resolution · scarring · abscess · chronic"},{"f":"Abscess من؟","b":"Pyogenic bacteria (staph aureus)"},{"f":"Pus فيه؟","b":"Dead neutrophils · debris · microbes · fluid"},{"f":"أخف شكل؟","b":"Catarrhal"},{"f":"Serous مثال؟","b":"Blister (burns)"},{"f":"Fibrinous وين؟","b":"Serosal membranes · joints"},{"f":"Pseudomembranous جرثومة؟","b":"C. difficile (colon + oropharynx)"},{"f":"Lymphangitis علامة؟","b":"Red streaks near wound"},{"f":"Chronic بلا شو؟","b":"Vascular response"},{"f":"خلايا المزمن؟","b":"Mononuclear cells (macrophages)"},{"f":"Macrophage بتنتنشّط بـ؟","b":"Interferon"},{"f":"Fistula؟","b":"Opening between two surfaces"},{"f":"Granuloma خلاياه؟","b":"Epithelioid macrophages + lymphocytes + giant cell"},{"f":"Foreign body granuloma مثال؟","b":"Suture material"},{"f":"Immune granuloma مثال؟","b":"TB (T-cell mediated)"},{"f":"أسباب Granuloma؟","b":"TB · leprosy · syphilis · cat-scratch · sarcoidosis · Crohn"},{"f":"CRP من وين؟","b":"Liver (IL-6)"},{"f":"Leukocytosis بتحفّزها؟","b":"CSFs on bone marrow"},{"f":"Septic shock مفتاح؟","b":"High TNF · low BP · DIC"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"inf-intro","system":"inflam","title":"Inflammation 1-2: Acute Inflammation & Mediators","url":"inf-intro.html","summary":"Definition and five Rs, acute vs chronic, vascular response (vasodilation, permeability mechanisms, stasis, exudates), leukocyte cellular events (margination to phagocytosis), leukocyte defects, and chemical mediators with the benefits of exudate.","points":["Inflammation = tissue + microcirculation reaction to insult; protective, not necessarily infection","5 Rs: recognition, recruitment, removal, regulation, resolution","Acute: edema hallmark; chronic: tissue damage hallmark","Permeability: contraction, direct injury, leukocyte-dependent, transcytosis (VEGF)","Transudate < 3 g/dl vs exudate > 3 g/dl","Margination → rolling (selectin) → adhesion (integrin/ICAM) → CD31 transmigration → chemotaxis → phagocytosis","Mediators: complement, kinin, clotting; amines, AA metabolites, cytokines, ROS, NO; exudate benefits"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Hallmark of acute inflammation is:","opts":["Tissue damage","Edema (exudation of fluid)","Granuloma","Fibrosis"],"a":1,"why":"Acute: minutes, neutrophils, edema. Chronic hallmark is tissue damage."},{"q":"Most common mechanism of increased vascular permeability:","opts":["Direct injury","Endothelial contraction (venules, histamine)","Transcytosis","Leukocyte-dependent injury"],"a":1,"why":"Fast and short-lived (minutes), in venules via vasoactive mediators."},{"q":"Exudate differs from transudate by:","opts":["Protein < 3 g/dl","Protein > 3 g/dl, SG > 1.015, cells","No cells","Cavity only"],"a":1,"why":"Transudate has low protein, SG < 1.015."},{"q":"Which molecule mediates leukocyte rolling?","opts":["Integrin","CD31","Selectin","ICAM only"],"a":2,"why":"Selectins (weak, temporary) cause rolling; integrin + ICAM/VCAM firm adhesion; CD31 transmigration."},{"q":"Chronic granulomatous disease is a defect of:","opts":["Integrin","Microbicidal activity (NADPH oxidase)","Chemotaxis","Production"],"a":1,"why":"LAD-1 is integrin deficiency; CGD is a killing defect."},{"q":"C5b-C9 forms:","opts":["Opsonin","Anaphylatoxin","Membrane attack complex","Kininogen"],"a":2,"why":"MAC punctures microbe membrane; C3b opsonizes; C5a is chemotactic."}],"cards":[{"f":"5 Rs؟","b":"Recognition · Recruitment · Removal · Regulation · Resolution"},{"f":"Hallmark الحاد؟","b":"Edema"},{"f":"Hallmark المزمن؟","b":"Tissue damage"},{"f":"5 علامات الحاد؟","b":"Redness · Swelling · Hotness · Pain · Function disturbance"},{"f":"Vasodilation بتعطي؟","b":"Redness + Heat"},{"f":"أشيع آلية نفاذية؟","b":"Endothelial contraction (histamine)"},{"f":"VEGF بيحفّز؟","b":"Transcytosis"},{"f":"Transudate؟","b":"< 3 g/dl, SG < 1.015"},{"f":"Exudate؟","b":"> 3 g/dl, SG > 1.015, cells"},{"f":"Serosanguineous؟","b":"Serous + RBC"},{"f":"أول خطوة لرحلة الكريات؟","b":"Margination"},{"f":"Selectin؟","b":"Rolling"},{"f":"Integrin + ICAM/VCAM؟","b":"Firm adhesion"},{"f":"CD31؟","b":"Transmigration"},{"f":"Chemotactic endogenous؟","b":"C5a · LTB4 · IL-8"},{"f":"Opsonins؟","b":"IgG · C3b"},{"f":"LAD-1؟","b":"Integrin deficiency"},{"f":"CGD؟","b":"NADPH oxidase defect"},{"f":"Bradykinin؟","b":"Vasodilation + permeability + pain"},{"f":"فوائد النضح؟","b":"Dilution · antibodies · fibrin · plasma systems · nutrition · immunity"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-14"},
 {"id":"imm-all","system":"immuno","title":"Immunology: Complete System Review","url":"imm-all.html","summary":"One place for the comparison tables and cheat sheets of every Immunology lecture: Hypersensitivity, Immunodeficiency & AIDS, Tolerance / Autoimmunity / Transplantation, and Amyloidosis.","points":["Hypersensitivity: types I-IV","Immunodeficiency: primary, secondary, AIDS","Tolerance, autoimmunity, graft rejection, GVHD","Amyloidosis: AL vs AA, types, diagnosis"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which immunoglobulin mediates type I hypersensitivity?","opts":["IgE","IgG","IgM","IgA"],"a":0,"why":"Type I reactions are IgE-mediated, acting through mast cells within minutes."},{"q":"A delayed-type (type IV) reaction typically appears after:","opts":["5-10 minutes","48-72 hours","7-12 days","Several seconds"],"a":1,"why":"Type IV is T-cell mediated and peaks at 48-72 hours, as in the Mantoux test."},{"q":"In Graves disease the antibodies:","opts":["Lyse thyroid cells with complement","Deposit as immune complexes in glomeruli","Stimulate the TSH receptor","Activate mast cells through IgE"],"a":2,"why":"This is the cellular dysfunction mechanism of type II: antibodies against a receptor without tissue injury."},{"q":"Which statement describes ADCC?","opts":["C3b opsonizes the target for phagocytosis","An antibody links an NK cell to the target, which dies by perforin and granzyme","IgE triggers degranulation of mast cells","Sensitized CD4+ T cells release cytokines"],"a":1,"why":"ADCC needs neither complement nor phagocytosis."},{"q":"Serum sickness usually begins:","opts":["Within minutes","After 2-3 days","7-12 days after exposure","After several years"],"a":2,"why":"It is a type III reaction that follows antibody production against foreign serum protein."},{"q":"A boy has increased IgM and decreased IgG, IgA and IgE. The defect is:","opts":["Btk","CD40L","ADA","NADPH oxidase"],"a":1,"why":"Hyper-IgM is an X-linked CD40L defect that blocks isotype switching."},{"q":"Bruton agammaglobulinemia is caused by a mutation in:","opts":["CD40L","ADA","Btk","Cytokine receptor gamma chain"],"a":2,"why":"Btk mutations block B-cell maturation, so B cells and all immunoglobulins are low."},{"q":"DiGeorge syndrome results from:","opts":["CD40L mutation","22q11 deletion with thymic aplasia","NADPH oxidase defect","Absent plasma cell differentiation"],"a":1,"why":"Thymic aplasia causes T-cell deficiency; the CATCH 22 features accompany it."},{"q":"Chronic granulomatous disease is a defect of:","opts":["Phagosome-lysosome fusion","NADPH oxidase","Btk","C3"],"a":1,"why":"Without NADPH oxidase there is no respiratory burst, so the phagocyte cannot kill ingested organisms."},{"q":"Which complement deficiency is the most common?","opts":["C3","C5","C2","C9"],"a":2,"why":"C2 is the most common (often mild, SLE-like); C3 is the most serious."},{"q":"Recurrent Neisseria infections suggest a deficiency of:","opts":["C2","C5-C9","C1q","Factor H only"],"a":1,"why":"Late components form the membrane attack complex, which is needed against Neisseria."},{"q":"Central tolerance takes place in the:","opts":["Lymph nodes and spleen","Skin and mucosa","Thymus and bone marrow","Liver and kidney"],"a":2,"why":"Immature self-reactive T and B cells are deleted by apoptosis in the thymus and bone marrow."},{"q":"Which antibodies are characteristic of Sjögren syndrome?","opts":["Anti-dsDNA","Anti-SS-A (Ro) and anti-SS-B (La)","Anti-centromere","Anti-Smith only"],"a":1,"why":"They are found in up to 90% of cases."},{"q":"Hyperacute graft rejection is caused by:","opts":["Donor CD8+ T cells","Fibrosis over months","Preformed antibodies","Regulatory T cells"],"a":2,"why":"Preformed antibodies (from transfusion or a previous transplant) cause immediate thrombosis and necrosis."},{"q":"Graft-versus-host disease is mainly mediated by:","opts":["Recipient antibodies","Donor CD8+ T cells","Recipient NK cells","Complement"],"a":1,"why":"Donor T cells attack recipient tissues, classically after bone marrow transplantation."},{"q":"Congo red-stained amyloid under polarized light shows:","opts":["Red fluorescence","Blue-violet color","Apple-green birefringence","No change"],"a":2,"why":"Apple-green birefringence is the diagnostic feature."},{"q":"AA amyloid derives from:","opts":["Immunoglobulin light chains","Serum amyloid A made by the liver","Transthyretin","Beta-2 microglobulin"],"a":1,"why":"Chronic inflammation raises IL-1 and IL-6, which drive hepatic SAA production."},{"q":"Amyloid in long-term hemodialysis patients is composed of:","opts":["Transthyretin","Calcitonin","Beta-2 microglobulin","Amyloid beta"],"a":2,"why":"Beta-2 microglobulin is not filtered by dialysis membranes and accumulates."}],"cards":[{"f":"Type I hypersensitivity: antibody, cells, timing","b":"IgE, mast cells and eosinophils, minutes (5-10)"},{"f":"Three mechanisms of type II hypersensitivity","b":"Complement-dependent, ADCC, cellular dysfunction"},{"f":"Examples of type III hypersensitivity","b":"Arthus reaction, SLE, serum sickness, post-streptococcal GN"},{"f":"Type IV: timing and hallmark lesion","b":"48-72 hours; granuloma (epithelioid cells, lymphocyte collar, Langhans giant cell)"},{"f":"Mantoux test","b":"PPD skin test; red and indurated, peak at 24-72 h"},{"f":"The four groups of primary immunodeficiency","b":"B cell, T cell, complement and phagocytic defects"},{"f":"X-linked SCID vs autosomal recessive SCID","b":"Cytokine receptor (gamma chain) defect vs ADA deficiency"},{"f":"CATCH 22","b":"DiGeorge: Cardiac, Abnormal facies, Thymic aplasia, Cleft palate, Hypocalcemia, 22q11 deletion"},{"f":"Hyper-IgM syndrome","b":"CD40L defect; high IgM, low IgG, IgA, IgE"},{"f":"Bruton vs CVID","b":"Bruton: Btk, boys, B cells absent. CVID: no plasma cell differentiation, risk of gastric cancer and lymphoma"},{"f":"CGD vs Chediak-Higashi","b":"CGD: NADPH oxidase, no respiratory burst. CHS: no phagosome-lysosome fusion"},{"f":"AIDS triad","b":"Opportunistic infections, secondary neoplasms, neurologic disease"},{"f":"Kaposi sarcoma","b":"HHV8; violaceous plaques with spindle cells and slit-like vessels"},{"f":"Peripheral tolerance mechanisms","b":"Anergy, Treg suppression and deletion"},{"f":"Molecular mimicry example","b":"Streptococcus antigens and heart tissue in rheumatic heart disease"},{"f":"Three types of graft rejection","b":"Hyperacute (preformed Ab), acute (cellular or humoral), chronic (fibrosis, onion skinning)"},{"f":"Rejection vs GVHD","b":"Rejection: recipient attacks graft. GVHD: donor T cells (CD8+) attack the recipient"},{"f":"AL vs AA amyloid","b":"AL: light chains from plasma cells (myeloma). AA: SAA from the liver in chronic inflammation"},{"f":"Amyloid stains","b":"Congo red: red, apple-green under polarized light. Thioflavin T/S: UV fluorescence"},{"f":"Best biopsy sites for amyloid","b":"Rectum (best), kidney, gingiva; fat aspirate is specific but not sensitive"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-13"},
 {"id":"cns-anti-1","system":"CNS","title":"Antiepileptics","url":"cns-antiepileptics-1.html","summary":"Epilepsy, seizure classification (focal vs generalized), pathophysiology (glutamate vs GABA, T-type Ca2+ in absence), principles of therapy, and the antiepileptic drugs: phenytoin, carbamazepine, valproic acid, phenobarbital, benzodiazepines, ethosuximide, vigabatrin, lamotrigine, topiramate, levetiracetam, adjuvants, drug selection and guidelines.","points":["Epilepsy = recurrent seizures; a single seizure is not epilepsy; febrile seizures are not epilepsy","Focal (one hemisphere) vs generalized (both, loss of consciousness); status epilepticus = emergency","Seizures: too much glutamate/aspartate or too little GABA; absence seizures = T-type Ca2+ channels in the thalamus","Drug actions: increase GABA, decrease glutamate, block Na+ channels, block Ca2+ channels","Phenytoin and carbamazepine block Na+; valproic acid broad-spectrum; ethosuximide for absence","Vigabatrin: visual field defects; lamotrigine: rash, safer in pregnancy; levetiracetam: cleanest profile","First choice: focal = carbamazepine, tonic-clonic/myoclonic = valproic acid, absence = ethosuximide, status = diazepam","Start after the second seizure with one drug; stop after 2 seizure-free years, gradually; folic acid 5 mg in pregnancy"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which drug is the first line for childhood absence seizures?","opts":["Phenytoin","Ethosuximide","Carbamazepine","Phenobarbital"],"a":1,"why":"Ethosuximide بيسد قنوات T-type Ca²⁺ بالثلاموس، وهو الأول للنوبات الغيابية وكمان أقل مضادات الصرع سمّية."},{"q":"Absence seizures are caused by overactivation of:","opts":["T-type Ca²⁺ channels","NMDA receptors","GABA-A receptors","P/Q-type Ca²⁺ channels"],"a":0,"why":"النوبة الغيابية سببها فرط تنشيط قنوات T-type Ca²⁺ بخلايا المرحّل الثلاموسية."},{"q":"First line drug for focal seizures?","opts":["Valproic acid","Lamotrigine","Carbamazepine","Levetiracetam"],"a":2,"why":"حسب جدول الشريحة الخيار الأول للجزئية هو Carbamazepine ."},{"q":"Which drug causes gingival hyperplasia and hirsutism?","opts":["Phenytoin","Valproic acid","Topiramate","Tiagabine"],"a":0,"why":"Phenytoin بيعمل تضخم لثة وكثرة شعر وتضخم عقد لمفية."},{"q":"Which drug induces its own metabolism (autoinduction)?","opts":["Valproic acid","Phenytoin","Carbamazepine","Lamotrigine"],"a":2,"why":"Carbamazepine بيحفّز استقلاب نفسو."},{"q":"Carbamazepine ↑ ADH secretion leading to:","opts":["Hypernatremia","Hyponatremia & edema","Hyperkalemia","Hypocalcemia"],"a":1,"why":"زيادة ADH ← احتباس مي ← نقص صوديوم (hyponatremia) ووذمة."},{"q":"Which drug has the highest risk of major congenital malformations?","opts":["Lamotrigine","Levetiracetam","Valproic acid","Ethosuximide"],"a":2,"why":"Valproic acid أعلى خطر تشوهات خلقية كبرى. أما Lamotrigine و Levetiracetam فمفضّلين بالحمل."},{"q":"Rare but fatal adverse effect of valproic acid?","opts":["Fulminant hepatic toxicity","Gingival hyperplasia","Visual loss","Renal stones"],"a":0,"why":"Fulminant hepatic toxicity نادر بس قاتل. وكمان pancreatitis و alopecia ."},{"q":"Which drug causes irreversible visual field loss?","opts":["Topiramate","Vigabatrin","Tiagabine","Gabapentin"],"a":1,"why":"Vigabatrin : فقدان رؤية غير عكوس عند 30 لـ 40 بالميّة. الحيلة: Vi يعني Vision ."},{"q":"Skin rash and Stevens-Johnson syndrome risk is highest with lamotrigine when combined with:","opts":["Phenytoin","Valproic acid","Levetiracetam","Ethosuximide"],"a":1,"why":"خطر SJS باللاموتريجين بيزيد لما ينعطى مع Valproic acid ."},{"q":"Which drug should be avoided in glaucoma?","opts":["Levetiracetam","Topiramate","Phenobarbital","Ethosuximide"],"a":1,"why":"Topiramate بيرفع ضغط العين (↑↑ IOP) ، وكمان حصى كلى وشق حنك ونقص وزن."},{"q":"Levetiracetam acts by binding to:","opts":["SV2A","T-type Ca²⁺ channel","GABA transaminase","NMDA receptor"],"a":0,"why":"Levetiracetam بيرتبط ببروتين الحويصلات المشبكية SV2A فبيقل Glutamate ."},{"q":"Gabapentin and pregabalin inhibit:","opts":["GABA reuptake","Presynaptic P/Q-type Ca²⁺ channels","Na⁺ channels","GABA transaminase"],"a":1,"why":"بيسدّوا قنوات P/Q-type Ca²⁺ قبل المشبك فبينقص Glutamate ."},{"q":"Tiagabine mechanism?","opts":["GABA reuptake inhibition","GABA-T inhibition","Na⁺ block","SV2A binding"],"a":0,"why":"Tiagabine بيمنع إعادة امتصاص GABA فبيرتفع تركيزو."},{"q":"First line for status epilepticus (adults)?","opts":["Phenytoin","Diazepam IV","Valproic acid","Ethosuximide"],"a":1,"why":"الخيار الأول Diazepam بالوريد للبالغين وبالمستقيم للأطفال. التاني Fosphenytoin أو Levetiracetam ."},{"q":"Which is NOT an epilepsy?","opts":["Febrile seizure","Absence seizure","Myoclonic seizure","Tonic-clonic seizure"],"a":0,"why":"Febrile seizure عند الأطفال بالحرارة العالية، من 6 أشهر لـ 5 سنوات، وهو مش صرع."},{"q":"Best antiepileptic drugs in pregnancy?","opts":["Valproic acid, phenytoin","Lamotrigine, levetiracetam","Carbamazepine, phenobarbital","Topiramate, vigabatrin"],"a":1,"why":"أفضلهم بالحمل Lamotrigine و Levetiracetam ."},{"q":"Folic acid dose before pregnancy in epileptic women?","opts":["0.4 mg/day","1 mg/day","5 mg/day","50 mg/day"],"a":2,"why":"الشريحة: حمض الفوليك 5 ملغ باليوم قبل الحمل بوقت كافي لتقليل عيوب الأنبوب العصبي."},{"q":"Antiepileptic drugs can be considered for withdrawal if seizure free for:","opts":["> 6 months","> 1 year","> 2 years","> 10 years"],"a":2,"why":"إذا بلا نوبات لأكتر من سنتين، والإيقاف تدريجي على أشهر."},{"q":"Which drug is a water-soluble prodrug used parenterally?","opts":["Fosphenytoin","Phenytoin","Levetiracetam","Topiramate"],"a":0,"why":"Fosphenytoin طليعة دوا بتذوب بالماء وبتنعطى بالوريد."},{"q":"Which is an enzyme INHIBITOR?","opts":["Phenytoin","Carbamazepine","Phenobarbital","Valproic acid"],"a":3,"why":"Valproic acid بيثبّط إنزيمات الكبد. الباقيين بيحفّزوها."},{"q":"Which drug has mixed mechanisms (↑ GABA, block Na⁺, block Ca²⁺) and covers all seizure types?","opts":["Phenytoin","Valproic acid","Ethosuximide","Vigabatrin"],"a":1,"why":"Valproic acid : يثبّط GABA-T ، يسد Na⁺ و Ca²⁺ ."}],"cards":[{"f":"Epilepsy?","b":"Neurological disorder: sudden, excessive, synchronous discharge of cerebral neurons"},{"f":"Seizure?","b":"Transient alteration of brain function ← abnormal neuronal discharge; single seizure ≠ epilepsy"},{"f":"Convulsion?","b":"Involuntary, violent, spasmodic contraction of skeletal muscles"},{"f":"Focal seizure?","b":"Confined to one hemisphere; simple (aware), complex (impaired), secondary generalization"},{"f":"Generalized seizure types?","b":"Absence, myoclonic, tonic-clonic; both hemispheres, loss of consciousness"},{"f":"Status epilepticus?","b":"Prolonged seizure >20 min; most common: generalized tonic-clonic; life-threatening"},{"f":"Febrile seizure?","b":"Children 6 months-5 years, high fever; NOT epilepsy"},{"f":"Pathophysiology of seizures?","b":"Imbalance: ↑ excitation (glutamate, aspartate) or ↓ inhibition (GABA)"},{"f":"NMDA receptor: ion?","b":"Na⁺ (excitatory: glutamate, aspartate)"},{"f":"GABA receptor: ion?","b":"Cl⁻ (inhibitory)"},{"f":"Absence seizure cause?","b":"T-type Ca²⁺ channel overactivation in thalamic relay neurons: thalamus-cortex rhythm"},{"f":"4 treatment principles?","b":"↑ GABA; ↓ excitatory neurotransmitters; block Na⁺; block Ca²⁺"},{"f":"1st generation AEDs?","b":"Phenytoin, carbamazepine, valproic acid, phenobarbital, benzodiazepines, ethosuximide"},{"f":"2nd generation AEDs?","b":"Vigabatrin, lamotrigine, topiramate, levetiracetam, gabapentin & pregabalin, tiagabine"},{"f":"Phenytoin: mechanism, use?","b":"Block voltage-gated Na⁺; tonic-clonic seizures"},{"f":"Phenytoin: adverse effects?","b":"Nystagmus, diplopia, ataxia; enzyme induction; megaloblastic anemia; gingival hyperplasia; lymphadenopathy; hirsutism; osteomalacia; fetal hydantoin syndrome; spina bifida"},{"f":"Fosphenytoin?","b":"Water-soluble prodrug of phenytoin; parenteral use"},{"f":"Why vit D + folic acid with phenytoin?","b":"↑ metabolism of vit D, folic acid ← osteomalacia, megaloblastic anemia"},{"f":"Carbamazepine: use?","b":"1st line focal; 2nd line tonic-clonic; trigeminal neuralgia"},{"f":"Carbamazepine: unique effects?","b":"↑ ADH → hyponatremia & edema; autoinduction"},{"f":"Valproic acid: mechanism?","b":"Inhibits GABA transaminase (↑ GABA); blocks Na⁺, Ca²⁺ channels"},{"f":"Valproic acid: use?","b":"ALL types of seizures (focal & generalized)"},{"f":"Valproic acid: adverse effects?","b":"Enzyme inhibition; neutropenia; teratogenic; alopecia; pancreatitis; fulminant hepatic toxicity"},{"f":"Highest malformation risk AED?","b":"Valproic acid"},{"f":"Phenobarbital: mechanism?","b":"Allosteric modulation GABA-A; GABA-like (GABA agonist)"},{"f":"Phenobarbital: use, key adverse?","b":"Tonic-clonic, status epilepticus; tolerance, dependence, respiratory depression (toxic)"},{"f":"Benzodiazepines: mechanism?","b":"Allosteric modulation of GABA-A receptors"},{"f":"Benzodiazepines: 1st line for?","b":"Status epilepticus; febrile seizures in children"},{"f":"Benzodiazepines: adverse?","b":"Tolerance & physical dependence; memory disturbance"},{"f":"Ethosuximide: mechanism?","b":"Blocks T-type Ca²⁺ channels in thalamocortical neurons"},{"f":"Ethosuximide: use?","b":"First line absence seizures; LEAST toxic AED"},{"f":"Vigabatrin: mechanism?","b":"Irreversibly inhibits GABA transaminase → ↑ GABA"},{"f":"Vigabatrin: adverse?","b":"Irreversible visual loss (30-40%); check visual fields every 6 months"},{"f":"Vigabatrin: use?","b":"Focal seizures only; refractory cases"},{"f":"Lamotrigine: mechanism?","b":"Block Na⁺ channels; ↓ glutamate release"},{"f":"Lamotrigine: adverse?","b":"Skin rash, Stevens-Johnson (↑ with valproic acid); insomnia"},{"f":"Lamotrigine: special?","b":"Preferred in pregnancy; widely prescribed for focal seizures"},{"f":"Topiramate: mechanism?","b":"Block Na⁺; ↑ GABA; block AMPA/kainate receptors"},{"f":"Topiramate: adverse?","b":"↑ IOP (avoid glaucoma); renal stones; cleft palate; weight loss"},{"f":"Topiramate: extra use?","b":"Migraine prophylaxis"},{"f":"Levetiracetam: mechanism?","b":"Binds SV2A (synaptic vesicle protein) → ↓ glutamate release"},{"f":"Levetiracetam: advantages?","b":"Broad spectrum; low toxicity; favorable PK; no drug interactions"},{"f":"Gabapentin, pregabalin: mechanism?","b":"Inhibit presynaptic P/Q Ca²⁺ channels → ↓ Ca²⁺ influx → ↓ glutamate release"},{"f":"Gabapentin, pregabalin: use?","b":"Adjuvant focal seizures; neuropathic pain"},{"f":"Tiagabine: mechanism?","b":"Inhibits GABA reuptake → ↑ GABA"},{"f":"Adjuvant drug?","b":"Additional therapy to boost the main drug when it is not enough alone"},{"f":"1st line: focal seizures?","b":"Carbamazepine"},{"f":"1st line: generalized tonic-clonic, myoclonic?","b":"Valproic acid"},{"f":"1st line: childhood absence?","b":"Ethosuximide"},{"f":"1st line: pregnancy?","b":"Lamotrigine or levetiracetam"},{"f":"1st line: status epilepticus?","b":"Diazepam IV (adult) / rectal (children)"},{"f":"When to start AED?","b":"After a second epileptic seizure"},{"f":"Treatment strategy?","b":"Monotherapy → substitute → combine 2 drugs"},{"f":"When to stop AED?","b":"Seizure free >2 years; withdraw gradually over months"},{"f":"Pregnancy: folic acid?","b":"5 mg/day, well before pregnancy ← ↓ neural tube defects"},{"f":"Breast feeding with AEDs?","b":"Acceptable with nearly ALL"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-17"},
 {"id":"cns-neuro-3","system":"CNS","title":"Neurodegenerative Drugs (Alzheimer)","url":"cns-neurodegenerative-3.html","summary":"Neurodegenerative diseases, Alzheimer's triad (memory loss, cognitive impairment, behavioral abnormalities), pathophysiology (↓ acetylcholine, ↑ glutamate in cortex and hippocampus), cholinesterase inhibitors (donepezil, rivastigmine, galantamine) as 1st line, and memantine (NMDA antagonist) as 2nd line or add-on in severe disease.","points":["Neurodegenerative disease = progressive loss of selected neurons in discrete brain areas → movement disorders, cognition disorders, or both","Most common: Alzheimer and Parkinson","Alzheimer triad: progressive memory loss, progressive cognitive impairment (can't recognize familiar people), behavioral abnormalities","Behavioral: aggression, emotional lability, depression, motor hyperactivity","Pathophysiology: neurotransmitter dysregulation → ↓ acetylcholine and ↑ glutamate in cortical and hippocampal regions","Image findings: atrophy of cortex, atrophy of hippocampus, enlarged ventricles","Cholinesterase inhibitors (donepezil, rivastigmine, galantamine) = 1st line, more selective for CNS cholinesterase, modest reduction in rate of cognitive loss","ChEI side effects: bradycardia, insomnia, nausea, vomiting, anorexia","Memantine = NMDA receptor antagonist, 2nd line; used if ChEIs are contraindicated or as add-on in severe disease; delays memory loss","Memantine side effects: insomnia, neuropsychiatric changes, confusion, agitation"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which drug group is the first-line therapy for Alzheimer's disease?","opts":["NMDA antagonists","Cholinesterase inhibitors","Dopamine agonists","Benzodiazepines"],"a":1,"why":"مثبطات الكولينستراز هي الخيار الأول، وميمانتين بالمرتبة التانية."},{"q":"Which is NOT a cholinesterase inhibitor?","opts":["Donepezil","Rivastigmine","Galantamine","Memantine"],"a":3,"why":"ميمانتين بيحجب مستقبلات NMDA، مو مثبط كولينستراز."},{"q":"The neurotransmitter changes in Alzheimer's disease are:","opts":["↑ Acetylcholine, ↓ glutamate","↓ Acetylcholine, ↑ glutamate","↓ Both","↑ Both"],"a":1,"why":"الأستيل كولين بينقص والغلوتامات بيزيد، بالقشرة وبالحصين."},{"q":"Which is part of the Alzheimer triad?","opts":["Resting tremor","Progressive memory loss","Seizures","Rigidity"],"a":1,"why":"الثالوث: فقدان ذاكرة + ضعف إدراكي + اضطراب سلوكي."},{"q":"Memantine acts as:","opts":["Cholinesterase inhibitor","GABA agonist","NMDA receptor antagonist","Dopamine antagonist"],"a":2,"why":"ميمانتين مضاد لمستقبل NMDA، يعني بيخفف تأثير الغلوتامات."},{"q":"A common side effect of donepezil is:","opts":["Tachycardia","Bradycardia","Constipation","Weight gain"],"a":1,"why":"زيادة الأستيل كولين بتعطي بطء قلب، غثيان، قيء، أرق، فقدان شهية."},{"q":"Memantine is used in Alzheimer's when:","opts":["As the only 1st line drug always","ChEIs are contraindicated, or as add-on in severe disease","The patient has epilepsy","The patient is pregnant"],"a":1,"why":"خط تاني: مانع لمثبطات الكولينستراز أو إضافة بالمرض الشديد."},{"q":"Which is a behavioral abnormality in Alzheimer's?","opts":["Aggression","Ptosis","Polyuria","Hypotension"],"a":0,"why":"السلوك: عدوانية، تقلب عاطفي، اكتئاب، فرط حركة."},{"q":"Which finding is seen in Alzheimer's brain imaging?","opts":["Small ventricles","Enlarged ventricles","Hypertrophy of cortex","Normal hippocampus"],"a":1,"why":"ضمور القشرة والحصين مع توسع البطينات."},{"q":"Side effects of memantine include:","opts":["Bradycardia and vomiting","Confusion and agitation","Anorexia only","Hypoglycemia"],"a":1,"why":"ميمانتين: أرق، تخليط، هيجان، تغيرات نفسية عصبية."}],"cards":[{"f":"Neurodegenerative disease?","b":"Progressive loss of selected neurons in discrete brain areas"},{"f":"2 most common neurodegenerative diseases?","b":"Alzheimer and Parkinson"},{"f":"Alzheimer triad?","b":"Progressive memory loss, cognitive impairment, behavioral abnormalities"},{"f":"Cognitive impairment in Alzheimer?","b":"Unable to recognize familiar people"},{"f":"Behavioral abnormalities?","b":"Aggression, emotional lability, depression, motor hyperactivity"},{"f":"Neurotransmitters in Alzheimer?","b":"↓ Acetylcholine, ↑ glutamate (excitatory)"},{"f":"Brain regions affected?","b":"Cortical and hippocampal"},{"f":"Imaging findings?","b":"Atrophy of cortex and hippocampus, enlarged ventricles"},{"f":"1st line therapy for Alzheimer?","b":"Cholinesterase inhibitors"},{"f":"Names of ChEIs?","b":"Donepezil, rivastigmine, galantamine"},{"f":"ChEIs mechanism?","b":"Inhibit cholinesterase (more selective for CNS) → ↑ ACh"},{"f":"ChEIs effect?","b":"Modest reduction in the rate of loss of cognitive functions"},{"f":"ChEIs side effects?","b":"Bradycardia, insomnia, nausea, vomiting, anorexia"},{"f":"Memantine class?","b":"NMDA receptor antagonist"},{"f":"Memantine line?","b":"2nd line"},{"f":"When is memantine used?","b":"ChEIs contraindicated, or add-on in severe disease"},{"f":"Memantine effect?","b":"Delays the rate of memory loss"},{"f":"Memantine side effects?","b":"Insomnia, neuropsychiatric changes, confusion, agitation"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-18"},
 {"id":"path-neoplasia-1","system":"neoplasia","title":"Neoplasia 1 (الأورام)","url":"path-neoplasia-1.html","summary":"Neoplasm definition, benign vs malignant, nomenclature, differentiation, anaplasia, growth rate, local invasion, metastasis, dysplasia and CIS.","points":["Neoplasm: New growth: abnormal mass, growth exceeds + uncoordinated with normal tissue","Classification: Benign: localized, no spread, surgical excision","Tumor structure: Parenchyma: neoplastic cells","Nomenclature: Benign: cell of origin + -oma","Differentiation + anaplasia: Well, moderately, poorly, undifferentiated (anaplastic)","Rate of growth + invasion: Benign: slow; malignant: rapid, correlates with differentiation","Metastasis: Single most important feature of malignancy","Dysplasia, CIS: Dysplasia: disordered growth, premalignant, reversible, confined to epithelium"],"mcqs":[{"q":"A tumor that persists in growing after the stimulus stops is described as:","opts":["Reactive","Autonomous","Regenerative","Physiologic"],"a":1,"why":"الورم مستقل (autonomous): بيكمّل نمو حتى بعد ما يوقف المحفّز."},{"q":"The word cancer comes from the Latin for:","opts":["Swelling","Crab","Sword","Cell"],"a":1,"why":"Cancer جاية من اللاتينية بمعنى سرطان البحر (crab). أما Tumor فمعناها تورّم."},{"q":"Cancer ranks as a cause of death:","opts":["1st","2nd after cardiovascular diseases","3rd","Rare"],"a":1,"why":"ثاني سبب للوفاة بعد أمراض القلب والأوعية."},{"q":"Which is a feature of benign tumors?","opts":["Invade adjacent tissue","Metastasize","Remain localized","Cause death"],"a":2,"why":"الحميد بيضل موضعي (localized)."},{"q":"Borderline malignant tumors:","opts":["Metastasize widely","Invade surrounding tissue but do not metastasize","Are always encapsulated","Are common"],"a":1,"why":"الحدّي بيغزو الجوار بس ما بينتشر، ونادر."},{"q":"The two basic components of every tumor:","opts":["Cells + fat","Parenchyma + stroma","Epithelium + endothelium","Nucleus + cytoplasm"],"a":1,"why":"برانشيما (الخلايا الورمية) + سدى (نسيج ضام وأوعية)."},{"q":"Desmoplasia is:","opts":["Scanty stroma","Abundant collagenous stroma, stony hard tumor","Necrosis","Mitosis"],"a":1,"why":"Desmoplasia سدى كولاجيني غزير ← ورم قاسي كالحجر."},{"q":"Benign tumors are named by adding:","opts":["-sarcoma","-carcinoma","-oma","-itis"],"a":2,"why":"الحميد: اسم الخلية الأصلية + -oma."},{"q":"A benign epithelial tumor with finger-like projections:","opts":["Adenoma","Papilloma","Cystadenoma","Fibroma"],"a":1,"why":"Papilloma نتوءات كالأصابع من سطح ظهاري."},{"q":"Hollow cystic benign tumor, mostly ovary:","opts":["Cystadenoma","Polyp","Lipoma","Teratoma"],"a":0,"why":"Cystadenoma كتلة كيسية مجوفة غالباً بالمبيض."},{"q":"Malignant tumor of epithelial origin:","opts":["Sarcoma","Carcinoma","Lipoma","Teratoma"],"a":1,"why":"ظهاري خبيث ← Carcinoma. ضام خبيث ← Sarcoma."},{"q":"Malignant tumor of cartilage:","opts":["Chondroma","Chondrosarcoma","Osteoma","Fibroma"],"a":1,"why":"Chondrosarcoma ورم خبيث بالغضروف."},{"q":"Which tumor arises from totipotential cells?","opts":["Lipoma","Teratoma","Adenoma","Papilloma"],"a":1,"why":"Teratoma من خلايا متعددة القدرات، أكتر من طبقة جنينية."},{"q":"Which is malignant despite -oma ending?","opts":["Lipoma","Melanoma","Fibroma","Osteoma"],"a":1,"why":"استثناءات: Lymphoma و Melanoma و Glioma و Seminoma."},{"q":"Benign tumors are:","opts":["Always well differentiated","Poorly differentiated","Anaplastic","Undifferentiated"],"a":0,"why":"الحميد دايماً متمايز جيداً."}],"cards":[{"f":"Neoplasm?","b":"New growth: abnormal mass, growth exceeds + uncoordinated with normal tissue, persists after stimuli cease"},{"f":"Tumor, cancer, oncology?","b":"Tumor: swelling. Cancer: all malignant tumors (Latin: crab). Oncology: science of cancer"},{"f":"Cancer: genetic basis?","b":"Genetic disorder: DNA mutation, passed to progeny, autonomous proliferation"},{"f":"Cancer rank as cause of death?","b":"2nd after cardiovascular diseases"},{"f":"Benign tumor features?","b":"Innocent features, localized, no spread, surgical excision, usually not affecting survival"},{"f":"Malignant tumor features?","b":"Characteristic morphology, invades + destroys, metastasizes, can cause death"},{"f":"Borderline malignant?","b":"Localized, invades surrounding tissue, no metastasis, rare"},{"f":"Tumor components?","b":"Parenchyma (neoplastic cells) + stroma (connective tissue, blood vessels)"},{"f":"Desmoplasia?","b":"Abundant collagenous stroma ← stony hard tumor (scirrhous carcinoma of breast)"},{"f":"Benign tumor naming?","b":"Cell of origin + suffix -oma"},{"f":"Adenoma?","b":"Benign tumor from glands or glandular pattern (e.g. renal cell adenoma)"},{"f":"Papilloma?","b":"Benign epithelial tumor: finger-like projections from surface"},{"f":"Cystadenoma?","b":"Benign hollow cystic mass, mostly ovary"},{"f":"Polyp?","b":"Benign epithelial mass projecting above mucosal surface, mostly GIT"},{"f":"Carcinoma vs sarcoma?","b":"Carcinoma: malignant epithelial. Sarcoma: malignant mesenchymal"},{"f":"Carcinoma types?","b":"Squamous cell, adenocarcinoma, transitional cell, basal cell"},{"f":"Mixed tumor?","b":"Epithelial + mesenchymal; divergent differentiation of one cell line (e.g. pleomorphic adenoma, carcinosarcoma)"},{"f":"Teratoma?","b":"Totipotential cells, > 1 germ layer; gonads; dermoid cyst; benign or malignant"},{"f":"Exceptions to -oma naming?","b":"Lymphoma, melanoma, glioma, seminoma: malignant"},{"f":"Differentiation?","b":"Extent neoplastic cells resemble normal cells, morphology + function"},{"f":"Anaplasia?","b":"Reversal to primitive level; lack of differentiation"},{"f":"Cytologic atypia features?","b":"Pleomorphism, hyperchromasia, ↑ N/C ratio"},{"f":"Other malignant signs?","b":"Abnormal mitoses, necrosis, tumor giant cells, loss of polarity"},{"f":"Rate of growth and differentiation?","b":"Well differentiated: slow. Poorly differentiated: rapid"},{"f":"Benign tumor invasion?","b":"Cohesive expansile, capsule (not all), enucleation"},{"f":"Malignant tumor invasion?","b":"Infiltrates, no capsule, no cleavage plane; excision with safety margin"},{"f":"Most reliable features of malignancy?","b":"1: metastasis. 2: local invasion"},{"f":"Metastasis?","b":"Secondary implants away from primary tumor"},{"f":"Distant metastasis at diagnosis?","b":"≈ 30% of solid tumor patients"},{"f":"Pathways of spread?","b":"Lymphatic, hematogenous, seeding body cavities"},{"f":"Most common initial spread of carcinomas?","b":"Lymphatic"},{"f":"Sentinel node?","b":"First node in regional lymphatic basin receiving lymph from primary tumor"},{"f":"Sentinel node mapping?","b":"Radiolabeled tracers + blue dyes; frozen section at surgery"},{"f":"Why liver + lungs commonly involved?","b":"Portal drainage → liver; caval blood → lungs"},{"f":"Seeding characteristic of?","b":"Ovarian carcinomas: peritoneum, pleura"},{"f":"Dysplasia?","b":"Disordered growth of epithelium; non-neoplastic, premalignant, reversible"},{"f":"Carcinoma in situ?","b":"Severe atypia confined to epithelium; basement membrane intact"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-19"},
 {"id":"cns-parkinson-4","system":"CNS","title":"Parkinson Drugs","url":"pharm-parkinson-4.html","summary":"Parkinsonism (tremor, rigidity, bradykinesia), pathophysiology (↓ dopamine → relative ACh overactivity), and drugs: levodopa + carbidopa, COMT inhibitors (entacapone, tolcapone), MAO-B inhibitors (selegiline, rasagiline), dopamine agonists, amantadine, and anticholinergics.","points":["Parkinsonism: progressive movement disorder; tremors, rigidity, bradykinesia, postural and gait abnormalities; age > 65","Substantia nigra → neostriatum: dopamine inhibitory, ACh excitatory; neuron loss → ↓ DA → relative ACh overactivity","Treatment goal: restore DA / ACh balance","Levodopa crosses BBB (dopamine cannot); carbidopa inhibits peripheral DOPA decarboxylase → levodopa dose ↓ 4–5 times","Levodopa: t½ 1–2 h, on/off phenomena (add COMT inhibitor), brown saliva/urine, vitamin B6 ↓ effect, antipsychotics ↑ symptoms","COMT inhibitors: entacapone (peripheral, safer); tolcapone (central + peripheral, fulminant hepatic necrosis)","MAO-B inhibitors: selegiline (amphetamine-like metabolites, insomnia); rasagiline (5× potency, no amphetamine-like metabolites)","DA agonists: bromocriptine (pulmonary fibrosis), apomorphine, pramipexole","Amantadine: ↑ DA release + cholinergic blockade; livedo reticularis","Anticholinergics (benztropine, trihexyphenidyl, procyclidine): dry mouth, constipation; avoid in glaucoma, BPH, pyloric stenosis"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Dopamine in the neostriatum is:","opts":["Excitatory","Inhibitory","Neutral","Cholinergic"],"a":1,"why":"الدوبامين مثبّط وبيقلل النشاط الحركي الزايد."},{"q":"Parkinson's mechanism leads to relative overactivity of:","opts":["Dopamine","Serotonin","Acetylcholine","GABA"],"a":2,"why":"لما الدوبامين بينقص، الأستيل كولين بيصير زايد نسبياً."},{"q":"Which crosses the BBB?","opts":["Dopamine","Levodopa","3-O-methyldopa","Carbidopa"],"a":1,"why":"ليفودوبا بيعبر الحاجز، والدوبامين لأ."},{"q":"Carbidopa inhibits:","opts":["COMT","MAO-B","DOPA decarboxylase","ACh esterase"],"a":2,"why":"كاربيدوبا بيمنع تحويل ليفودوبا لدوبامين خارج الدماغ."},{"q":"Brownish saliva and urine with levodopa is due to:","opts":["Bile","Melanin from dopamine oxidation","Bilirubin","Hemoglobin"],"a":1,"why":"ميلانين من أكسدة الدوبامين."},{"q":"Which vitamin decreases levodopa effectiveness?","opts":["B12","C","B6","D"],"a":2,"why":"B6 بيزيد التكسير المحيطي لليفودوبا."},{"q":"COMT inhibitor with risk of fulminant hepatic necrosis:","opts":["Entacapone","Tolcapone","Selegiline","Carbidopa"],"a":1,"why":"تولكابون، وإنتاكابون أأمن."},{"q":"Which has amphetamine-like metabolites?","opts":["Rasagiline","Selegiline","Entacapone","Bromocriptine"],"a":1,"why":"سيليجيلين، وبيسبب أرق."},{"q":"Pulmonary fibrosis is associated with:","opts":["Bromocriptine","Amantadine","Benztropine","Levodopa"],"a":0,"why":"برومكريبتين (DA agonist)."},{"q":"Anticholinergics are contraindicated in:","opts":["Hypertension","Glaucoma","Asthma","Anemia"],"a":1,"why":"الزرق، وكمان تضخم البروستات وتضيّق البواب."}],"cards":[{"f":"Parkinsonism?","b":"Progressive neurological disorder, movement impairment"},{"f":"Basic symptoms?","b":"Tremors, rigidity, bradykinesia, postural + gait abnormalities"},{"f":"Bradykinesia?","b":"Slow initiation and execution of voluntary movement"},{"f":"Mechanism of Parkinson?","b":"Neuron destruction → ↓ DA → relative ACh overactivity"},{"f":"Treatment goal?","b":"Restore DA / ACh balance"},{"f":"Why carbidopa?","b":"Inhibits DOPA decarboxylase; levodopa dose ↓ 4–5 times"},{"f":"Levodopa PK?","b":"Oral, empty stomach, t½ 1–2 h"},{"f":"On/off phenomena?","b":"Sudden unpredictable mobility changes; add COMT inhibitor"},{"f":"Brown saliva and urine?","b":"Melanin from dopamine oxidation"},{"f":"Vitamin B6 + levodopa?","b":"↑ peripheral breakdown → ↓ effectiveness"},{"f":"Antipsychotics in Parkinson?","b":"DA blockade → ↑ symptoms"},{"f":"COMT inhibitors?","b":"Entacapone, tolcapone"},{"f":"Tolcapone vs entacapone?","b":"Tolcapone central + peripheral, hepatic necrosis; entacapone peripheral, safer"},{"f":"MAO-B inhibitors?","b":"Selegiline, rasagiline; ↓ DA breakdown"},{"f":"Selegiline problem?","b":"Amphetamine-like metabolites → insomnia"},{"f":"Rasagiline vs selegiline?","b":"5× potency, no amphetamine-like metabolites"},{"f":"DA agonists?","b":"Bromocriptine, apomorphine, pramipexole; pulmonary fibrosis"},{"f":"Amantadine?","b":"↑ DA release, cholinergic blockade; livedo reticularis"},{"f":"Anticholinergics?","b":"Benztropine, trihexyphenidyl, procyclidine"},{"f":"Anticholinergic SE and contraindications?","b":"Dry mouth, constipation; avoid glaucoma, BPH, pyloric stenosis"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-19"},
 {"id":"path-neoplasia-3-4","system":"neoplasia","title":"Neoplasia 3 and 4 (الأورام: الوبائيات والأساس الجزيئي)","url":"path-neoplasia-3-4b.html","summary":"Epidemiology, geographic and age factors, heredity, preneoplastic disorders, 4 gene classes, oncogenes (RAS, CML, MYC), tumor suppressors (p53), apoptosis and DNA repair genes, 7 hallmarks, telomerase, multistep carcinogenesis.","points":["Epidemiology and Cancer Incidence: Epidemiology: environment, heredity, cultural influences ↔ specific neoplasms","Geographic, Environmental Factors and Age: Sporadic cancers: environment > heredity","Heredity: Inherited, Familial, Autosomal Recessive: Hereditary predisposition + environment","Acquired Preneoplastic Disorders: Persistent regenerative proliferation: chronic hepatitis B, C ← HCC; ulcerative colitis ← colorectal CA; Barrett ← esophageal adenocarcinoma","Molecular Basis of Cancer: 4 Gene Classes: Mutation = heart of carcinogenesis","Proto-oncogenes and Oncogenes: Proto-oncogenes: promote growth, proliferation","Tumor Suppressor, Apoptosis and DNA Repair Genes: Tumor suppressor genes: growth inhibiting: p53, Rb, NF, VHL, BRCA","Seven Hallmarks of Cancer: 7 changes, malignant phenotype","Multistep Carcinogenesis: Carcinogenesis: multistep, phenotypic + genetic, accumulation of multiple mutations"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Stomach cancer is 7-8× higher in Japan than USA mainly due to:","opts":["Genetic race only","Salted, smoked food, nitrosamines, H. pylori","UV exposure","Smoking"],"a":1,"why":"السبب أكل مملّح ومدخّن ومخلّل ومواد Nitrosamines وجرثومة H. pylori."},{"q":"Most common childhood cancer death cause group:","opts":["Carcinomas","Acute leukemia + CNS tumors","Sarcomas only","Melanoma"],"a":1,"why":"الكارسينوما نادرة عند الأطفال، واللي بيطلع ابيضاض حاد وأورام الجهاز العصبي المركزي."},{"q":"Cancer rise with age is explained by:","opts":["Hormones only","Accumulation of somatic mutations, ↓ immunity","Diet only","Radiation only"],"a":1,"why":"الطفرات الجسدية Somatic mutations بتتراكم والمناعة بتنزل."},{"q":"Autosomal dominant inherited cancer syndromes are due to:","opts":["Defective DNA repair","Single mutant gene, ↑ tumor risk","Environmental only","Viruses"],"a":1,"why":"جين طافر واحد بيرفع خطر الورم كتير. وخلل الإصلاح هو للمتنحية."},{"q":"Which is NOT a feature of familial cancer?","opts":["Early age of onset","Bilateral tumors","≥ 2 relatives affected","Clear transmission pattern"],"a":3,"why":"نمط الانتقال بالعائلية مش واضح."},{"q":"Chronic hepatitis B, C predisposes to:","opts":["Colorectal carcinoma","Hepatocellular carcinoma","Esophageal adenocarcinoma","Lymphoma"],"a":1,"why":"التهاب الكبد المزمن بيزيد خطر سرطان الخلايا الكبدية."},{"q":"Barrett esophagus predisposes to:","opts":["SCC","Adenocarcinoma of esophagus","Lymphoma","Melanoma"],"a":1,"why":"مريء باريت بيزيد خطر السرطان الغدي بالمريء."},{"q":"Leukoplakia (oral mucosa, vulva, penis) predisposes to:","opts":["SCC","Adenocarcinoma","Lymphoma","Sarcoma"],"a":0,"why":"اللويحة البيضاء بتزيد خطر السرطان الحرشفي."},{"q":"Gene class that promotes growth:","opts":["Tumor suppressor","Proto-oncogene","Apoptosis gene","DNA repair gene"],"a":1,"why":"الجين المولّد للأورام بيحفّز النمو."},{"q":"Most common abnormality of proto-oncogenes in human tumors:","opts":["MYC amplification","RAS point mutation","p53 loss","bcl-2 loss"],"a":1,"why":"طفرة نقطية بجين RAS، موجودة بـ 15-20% من الأورام."},{"q":"CML is caused by translocation:","opts":["t(8;14)","t(9;22)","t(11;22)","t(14;18)"],"a":1,"why":"انتقال 9 و22 بيدمج ABL مع BCR."},{"q":"Imatinib mesylate inhibits:","opts":["MYC","RAS","BCR-ABL kinase","p53"],"a":2,"why":"Imatinib بيثبّط إنزيم BCR-ABL."}],"cards":[{"f":"Epidemiology: value?","b":"Links environment, heredity, culture ↔ specific neoplasms"},{"f":"Why lung CA mortality ↑ in women?","b":"↑ smoking"},{"f":"Why liver CA mortality ↑ in men?","b":"HCV infection"},{"f":"Why cervical CA mortality ↓?","b":"Pap smear, CIN treatment"},{"f":"Stomach CA Japan vs USA?","b":"7-8× higher: salted, smoked, pickled food, nitrosamines, H. pylori"},{"f":"Melanoma NZ vs Iceland?","b":"6× mortality: UV + fair skin"},{"f":"Commonest cancers in children?","b":"Acute leukemia, CNS tumors ≈ 60% of deaths"},{"f":"Why cancer ↑ with age?","b":"Somatic mutations accumulate, ↓ immune competence"},{"f":"3 hereditary categories?","b":"Inherited syndromes (AD), familial, AR defective DNA repair"},{"f":"Familial cancer features?","b":"Early onset, ≥ 2 relatives, multiple / bilateral"},{"f":"Chronic hepatitis B, C risk?","b":"Hepatocellular carcinoma"},{"f":"Barrett esophagus risk?","b":"Esophageal adenocarcinoma"},{"f":"Endometrial hyperplasia cause?","b":"↑ Estrogen ← endometrial carcinoma"},{"f":"Villous adenoma?","b":"Highly malignant potential"},{"f":"Benign → malignant examples?","b":"Adenoma → adenocarcinoma, leiomyoma → leiomyosarcoma, nevus → melanoma"},{"f":"4 gene targets?","b":"Proto-oncogenes, tumor suppressors, apoptosis genes, DNA repair genes"},{"f":"Proto-oncogene vs oncogene?","b":"Normal growth promoter vs mutant autonomous version"},{"f":"RAS?","b":"GTP-binding protein; point mutation; stuck GTP-bound; 15-20% tumors"},{"f":"CML?","b":"t(9;22) ABL-BCR; BCR-ABL kinase; imatinib"},{"f":"Most involved transcription factor?","b":"MYC ← cyclin D2"},{"f":"Oncogene activation mechanisms?","b":"Point mutation, amplification, translocation, epigenetic"},{"f":"p53?","b":"Guardian of the Genome, chr 17p13.1, > 50% of tumors"},{"f":"bcl-2?","b":"Apoptosis gene, chr 18"},{"f":"DNA repair gene examples?","b":"hMLH1, hPMS1, hPMS2"},{"f":"7 hallmarks?","b":"Growth signals, no inhibition, evade apoptosis, limitless replication, angiogenesis, invasion, genomic instability"},{"f":"Telomerase?","b":"Maintains telomeres: 85-95% of cancers"},{"f":"Multistep: initiation vs progression?","b":"First mutation vs sequence of new mutations"},{"f":"Is one mutation enough?","b":"No"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-19"},
 {"id":"path-neoplasia-5-6","system":"neoplasia","title":"Neoplasia 5 and 6 (الأورام: التكوّن الوعائي، الانتقال، المسرطنات)","url":"path-neoplasia-5-6c.html","summary":"Tumor angiogenesis, invasion and metastasis steps, chemical carcinogens (direct vs indirect), initiation vs promotion, radiation (UV and ionizing), and oncogenic microbes (HPV, EBV, HBV, HCV, HTLV-1, H. pylori).","points":["Tumors > 1-2 mm need new vessels (angiogenesis): VEGF, bFGF, angiogenin; needed for growth and metastasis","Invasion/metastasis: 1) loss of adherence (↓ E-cadherin) 2) ECM invasion (integrin, metalloproteinase, cathepsin D, collagenase) 3) migration (cytokines) 4) vascular dissemination (intravasation, platelets CD11, extravasation)","Direct carcinogens: active alone, weak (alkylating agents: cyclophosphamide, chlorambucil)","Indirect carcinogens (procarcinogens): need P-450 conversion, largest group, potent; aflatoxin → HCC, nitrosamines → stomach, β-naphthylamine → rubber/azo dyes","Initiation: irreversible DNA damage, not enough alone; promotion: reversible, ↑ proliferation, no DNA damage","Chemical carcinogen targets: RAS and p53; Pott: chimney sweeps and soot","UVB causes skin cancer (pyrimidine dimers); UVC filtered by ozone","Ionizing radiation: chromosome breakage; leukemia is commonest, then thyroid, breast, lung; skin, bone, GIT resistant","HPV 16, 18, 31: E6 degrades p53, E7 binds Rb; EBV: Burkitt, Hodgkin subset, nasopharyngeal; HBV/HCV: HCC; HTLV-1: T-cell leukemia; H. pylori: gastric"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Solid tumors need vascularization beyond:","opts":["1-2 mm","5 mm","1 cm","2 cm"],"a":0,"why":"الورم بدون أوعية ما بيكبر أكتر من 1-2 ملم."},{"q":"Which is an angiogenic factor?","opts":["VEGF","E-cadherin","Integrin","Collagenase"],"a":0,"why":"VEGF وbFGF وangiogenin."},{"q":"Step 1 of metastasis:","opts":["ECM invasion","Loss of adherence","Migration","Extravasation"],"a":1,"why":"فقدان الالتصاق بسبب نقص E-cadherin."},{"q":"Enzymes degrading the ECM:","opts":["Cytochrome P-450","Metalloproteinase, cathepsin D, collagenase","Telomerase","Integrin"],"a":1,"why":"الخلايا الورمية بتفرز إنزيمات هاضمة للمصفوفة."},{"q":"Direct-acting carcinogens are:","opts":["Potent, need conversion","Weak, active by themselves","The largest group","Need P-450"],"a":1,"why":"المباشرة ضعيفة وبتشتغل لحالها."},{"q":"Aflatoxin (Aspergillus flavus) causes:","opts":["HCC","Cervical CA","Leukemia","Melanoma"],"a":0,"why":"سرطان كبد."},{"q":"Initiation is:","opts":["Reversible","Irreversible DNA damage","No DNA damage","Carcinogenic alone"],"a":1,"why":"ضرر دائم بالحمض النووي، بس وحدو ما بيكفي."},{"q":"UV type responsible for skin cancer:","opts":["UVA","UVB","UVC","Gamma"],"a":1,"why":"UVB، وUVC بيفلترو الأوزون."},{"q":"HPV E6 protein:","opts":["Binds Rb","Degrades p53","Inhibits RAS","Activates MYC"],"a":1,"why":"E6 بيحلّل p53، وE7 بيرتبط بـ Rb."},{"q":"HTLV-1 causes:","opts":["Cervical CA","T-cell leukemia / lymphoma","HCC","Gastric CA"],"a":1,"why":"فيروس RNA، ابيضاض ولمفوما تائية."}],"cards":[{"f":"Tumor size limit without vessels?","b":"1-2 mm"},{"f":"Angiogenesis needed for?","b":"Growth + metastasis"},{"f":"Angiogenic factors?","b":"VEGF, basic FGF, angiogenin"},{"f":"Metastasis step 1?","b":"Loss of adherence ← ↓ E-cadherin"},{"f":"Metastasis step 2?","b":"ECM invasion: integrin, metalloproteinase, cathepsin D, collagenase"},{"f":"Metastasis step 3?","b":"Migration: cytokines"},{"f":"Metastasis step 4?","b":"Vascular dissemination: intravasation, platelets (CD11), extravasation"},{"f":"Percival Pott?","b":"Chimney sweeps, scrotal CA, soot"},{"f":"Direct carcinogens?","b":"Active alone, weak: alkylating agents"},{"f":"Indirect carcinogens?","b":"Need P-450 conversion, largest group, potent"},{"f":"Aflatoxin?","b":"Aspergillus flavus: HCC"},{"f":"Nitrosamines?","b":"Food preservatives: stomach CA"},{"f":"β-naphthylamine?","b":"Rubber industry, azo dyes"},{"f":"Initiation?","b":"Irreversible DNA damage, not sufficient alone"},{"f":"Promotion?","b":"Reversible, ↑ proliferation, no DNA damage"},{"f":"Targets of chemical carcinogens?","b":"RAS, p53"},{"f":"UVB / UVC?","b":"UVB: skin CA (pyrimidine dimers); UVC: filtered by ozone"},{"f":"Ionizing radiation?","b":"Chromosome breakage; leukemia commonest, then thyroid, breast, lung"},{"f":"Radiation-resistant tissues?","b":"Skin, bone, GIT"},{"f":"HPV oncoproteins?","b":"E6 degrades p53, E7 binds Rb"},{"f":"EBV tumors?","b":"Burkitt, B-cell lymphoma, Hodgkin subset, nasopharyngeal, gastric"},{"f":"HBV, HCV?","b":"HCC: chronic inflammation, regeneration"},{"f":"HTLV-1?","b":"RNA virus: T-cell leukemia / lymphoma"},{"f":"H. pylori?","b":"Gastric adenocarcinoma + lymphoma"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-21"},
 {"id":"path-neoplasia-7-8","system":"neoplasia","title":"Neoplasia 7 and 8 (الأورام: التأثير على المضيف، التدريج والتشخيص)","url":"path-neoplasia-7-8c.html","summary":"Effects of tumors on the host, cachexia, paraneoplastic syndromes, grading and TNM staging, laboratory diagnosis (frozen section, FNA, cytology, IHC) and tumor markers.","points":["Tumor effects on host: pressure, functional activity, bleeding, infection, rupture, infarction; cachexia and paraneoplastic syndromes are malignant features","Diagnosis of a mass: histopathology after excision","Cachexia: progressive loss of fat and lean mass, weakness, anorexia, anemia; severity relates to tumor size and spread; mediators TNF-α, IL-1, IFN-γ, PIF, LMF; about 1/3 of cancer deaths","Paraneoplastic syndromes: ~10% of patients, not local, not metastatic, not from native hormones; may precede diagnosis","Cushing: ACTH-like, small-cell lung (50%); hypercalcemia: PTH-like (commonest); hyponatremia: ADH, small-cell lung; polycythemia: erythropoietin, renal cell carcinoma","Trousseau: hypercoagulable state; hypoglycemia: insulin-like; skeletal metastasis hypercalcemia is NOT paraneoplastic","Grade (I-IV): differentiation, H&E, mitoses; grade IV nearly anaplastic","Stage: size, nodes, distant metastasis; TNM (Tis, T1-4, N0-3, M0-1)","Diagnosis tools: frozen section (margins), FNA, exfoliative cytology (Pap), IHC, flow cytometry, molecular tests","Markers support diagnosis, response, follow-up (not primary diagnosis): PSA prostate, CA-125 ovarian, AFP liver/germ cell, CEA colon, calcitonin medullary thyroid, hCG trophoblastic"],"mcqs":[{"q":"All are features of benign tumors EXCEPT:","opts":["Pressure on adjacent structures","Functional activity","Bleeding, secondary infection","Cachexia, paraneoplastic syndrome"],"a":3,"why":"الهزال والمتلازمات الورمية المصاحبة من صفات الورم الخبيث."},{"q":"Accurate diagnosis of a mass is usually achieved by:","opts":["Clinical judgment always","Histopathology after excision","Tumor markers","Plain X-ray"],"a":1,"why":"الفحص النسيجي بعد الاستئصال هو التشخيص الدقيق."},{"q":"Cachexia severity correlates with:","opts":["Tumor grade only","Tumor size and extent of spread","Patient age","Tumor markers"],"a":1,"why":"شدة الهزال بتتناسب مع حجم الورم وانتشاره."},{"q":"Commonest paraneoplastic syndrome:","opts":["Cushing","Hypercalcemia","Polycythemia","Hypoglycemia"],"a":1,"why":"فرط كالسيوم الدم هو الأشهر، وCushing أشهر اضطراب غدي صماوي."},{"q":"Cushing's paraneoplastic syndrome is mostly from:","opts":["Renal cell carcinoma","Small-cell lung carcinoma","Colon cancer","Prostate cancer"],"a":1,"why":"سرطان الرئة صغير الخلايا، يفرز مادة شبيهة بـ ACTH."},{"q":"Polycythemia as paraneoplastic is associated with:","opts":["Renal cell carcinoma","Gastric cancer","Breast cancer","Lymphoma"],"a":0,"why":"مادة شبيهة بالإريثروبويتين."},{"q":"Hypercalcemia from skeletal metastases is:","opts":["Paraneoplastic","NOT paraneoplastic","Due to ADH","Due to ACTH"],"a":1,"why":"انحلال العظم بالنقائل مو متلازمة ورمية مصاحبة."},{"q":"Tumor grading depends on:","opts":["Size and spread","Differentiation and mitoses","Lymph nodes","Distant metastasis"],"a":1,"why":"التدريج: درجة التمايز، أما التصنيف المرحلي فللحجم والانتشار."},{"q":"In TNM, M1 means:","opts":["No nodes","Regional nodes","Distant metastases present","In situ"],"a":2,"why":"M1 = نقائل بعيدة."},{"q":"PSA is a marker for:","opts":["Prostate cancer","Ovarian cancer","Liver cancer","Breast cancer"],"a":0,"why":"PSA للبروستات، وCA-125 للمبيض، وAFP للكبد."}],"cards":[{"f":"Tumor effects on host?","b":"Pressure, function, bleeding, infection, rupture, infarction"},{"f":"Cachexia?","b":"Progressive loss of fat and lean mass, weakness, anorexia, anemia"},{"f":"Cachexia severity relates to?","b":"Tumor size and spread"},{"f":"Cachexia factors?","b":"TNF-α, IL-1, IFN-γ, PIF, LMF"},{"f":"Cachexia treatment?","b":"Remove the tumor"},{"f":"Deaths from cachexia?","b":"One third of cancer deaths"},{"f":"Paraneoplastic incidence?","b":"About 10%"},{"f":"Commonest endocrinopathy?","b":"Cushing (small-cell lung, ACTH-like)"},{"f":"Commonest paraneoplastic?","b":"Hypercalcemia (PTH-like)"},{"f":"Hyponatremia cause?","b":"Inappropriate ADH, small-cell lung"},{"f":"Polycythemia cause?","b":"Erythropoietin-like, renal cell carcinoma"},{"f":"Trousseau?","b":"Hypercoagulable state (venous thrombosis)"},{"f":"Grading basis?","b":"Differentiation, H&E, mitoses"},{"f":"Grade IV?","b":"Nearly anaplastic"},{"f":"Staging basis?","b":"Size, nodes, distant metastases"},{"f":"T4?","b":"Very large, very invasive, spread to adjacent organs"},{"f":"N3 / M1?","b":"More distant nodes / distant metastases"},{"f":"Frozen section use?","b":"Nature of lesion, margins"},{"f":"Cytology types?","b":"FNA, exfoliative (Pap smear)"},{"f":"Tumor markers for primary diagnosis?","b":"No: low sensitivity and specificity"},{"f":"PSA / CA-125 / AFP?","b":"Prostate / ovarian / liver cell and germ cell testis"},{"f":"Calcitonin / catecholamines?","b":"Medullary thyroid / pheochromocytoma"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-21"},
 {"id":"cns-antipsychotic-5","system":"CNS","title":"Antipsychotic Drugs","url":"cns-antipsychotic-5b.html","summary":"Psychosis (positive vs negative symptoms), dopamine and serotonin pathophysiology, typical vs atypical antipsychotics, uses, and adverse effects (EPS timeline, NMS, hyperprolactinemia, α/muscarinic blockade, agranulocytosis).","points":["Psychosis: temporary loss of contact with reality","Positive symptoms (acute): hallucinations, delusions, thought disorder; negative (chronic): apathy, social withdrawal, lack of initiative","Mesolimbic/mesocortical dopamine ↑ → positive; 5HT₂A ↑ → negative","Dopamine too low: parkinsonism, hyperprolactinemia; too high: vomiting, hallucinations","Typical (haloperidol, chlorpromazine, prochlorperazine): block mainly D₂, work on positive symptoms","Atypical (risperidone, olanzapine, clozapine, quetiapine, aripiprazole): D₂ less, 5HT₂A more, work on negative symptoms and typical non-responders","Uses: schizophrenia; prochlorperazine for nausea/vomiting; chlorpromazine for intractable hiccups","EPS timeline: dystonia (hours-days), akathisia (days-weeks), parkinsonism (weeks-months), tardive dyskinesia (months-years, irreversible)","NMS: rigidity, fever, altered mental status, unstable BP; stop drug, dantrolene, bromocriptine","Other: prolactin ↑ (amenorrhea, galactorrhea, gynecomastia), α block (orthostatic hypotension), muscarinic block, weight gain (atypical), chlorpromazine cholestatic jaundice, clozapine agranulocytosis"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which antipsychotic most likely causes a Parkinson-like syndrome?","opts":["Risperidone","Olanzapine","Haloperidol","Aripiprazole"],"a":2,"why":"هالوبيريدول من الجيل الأول وبيحجب D₂ بقوة."},{"q":"Psychosis is best defined as:","opts":["Permanent loss of memory","Temporary loss of contact with reality","Excess sleep","Loss of movement"],"a":1,"why":"فقدان مؤقت للاتصال بالواقع."},{"q":"All are positive symptoms EXCEPT:","opts":["Hallucinations","Delusions","Thought disorder","Social withdrawal"],"a":3,"why":"الانعزال الاجتماعي عرض سلبي."},{"q":"Negative symptoms are linked mostly to:","opts":["Dopamine ↓","5HT₂A ↑","ACh ↑","GABA ↑"],"a":1,"why":"السيروتونين ← السلبية، والدوبامين ← الإيجابية."},{"q":"Atypical antipsychotics:","opts":["Block D₂ only","Block D₂ less and 5HT₂A more","Activate D₂","Block 5HT only"],"a":1,"why":"D₂ أقل و5HT₂A أكتر، فأعراضها الحركية أقل."},{"q":"Dystonia appears after:","opts":["Hours to days","Days to weeks","Months to years","Years"],"a":0,"why":"الديستونيا أول شي، وTD آخر شي."},{"q":"Irreversible EPS:","opts":["Dystonia","Akathisia","Parkinsonism","Tardive dyskinesia"],"a":3,"why":"Tardive dyskinesia بعد شهور وسنين وغالباً دائمة."},{"q":"Treatment of neuroleptic malignant syndrome:","opts":["Continue drug","Stop drug, dantrolene, bromocriptine","Give haloperidol","Give clozapine"],"a":1,"why":"وقف الدوا مع علاج داعم."},{"q":"Agranulocytosis is associated with:","opts":["Haloperidol","Clozapine","Risperidone","Aripiprazole"],"a":1,"why":"كلوزابين، تثبيط نخاع العظم."},{"q":"Galactorrhea is due to:","opts":["Prolactin ↑ from D₂ block","Muscarinic block","α block","5HT block"],"a":0,"why":"حجب D₂ بالنخامية ← برولاكتين زايد."}],"cards":[{"f":"Psychosis?","b":"Temporary loss of contact with reality"},{"f":"Positive symptoms?","b":"Excess, distortion; acute: hallucinations, delusions, thought disorder"},{"f":"Negative symptoms?","b":"Decrease, absence; chronic: apathy, social withdrawal, lack of initiative"},{"f":"Cause of positive symptoms?","b":"Mesolimbic, mesocortical dopamine ↑"},{"f":"Cause of negative symptoms?","b":"Serotonin 5HT₂A ↑"},{"f":"Dopamine too low?","b":"Parkinsonism, hyperprolactinemia"},{"f":"Dopamine too high?","b":"Vomiting, hallucinations"},{"f":"Typical antipsychotics?","b":"Haloperidol, chlorpromazine, prochlorperazine"},{"f":"Atypical antipsychotics?","b":"Risperidone, olanzapine, clozapine, quetiapine, aripiprazole"},{"f":"Typical mechanism?","b":"Block mainly D₂ → positive symptoms"},{"f":"Atypical mechanism?","b":"D₂ less, 5HT₂A more → negative symptoms"},{"f":"Prochlorperazine use?","b":"Nausea and vomiting"},{"f":"Chlorpromazine other use?","b":"Intractable hiccups"},{"f":"EPS onset order?","b":"Dystonia (hours-days), akathisia (days-weeks), parkinsonism (weeks-months), TD (months-years)"},{"f":"Akathisia?","b":"Restlessness"},{"f":"Tardive dyskinesia?","b":"Repetitive movements eyes, hands, lips; often irreversible"},{"f":"NMS features?","b":"Rigidity, fever, altered mental status, unstable BP"},{"f":"NMS treatment?","b":"Stop drug; dantrolene, bromocriptine"},{"f":"Prolactin effects?","b":"Amenorrhea, galactorrhea, gynecomastia, infertility"},{"f":"α block effects?","b":"Orthostatic hypotension, male sexual dysfunction"},{"f":"Muscarinic block effects?","b":"Dry mouth, urinary retention, constipation, loss of accommodation"},{"f":"Weight gain?","b":"Atypical drugs, 5HT block"},{"f":"Chlorpromazine toxicity?","b":"Cholestatic jaundice"},{"f":"Clozapine toxicity?","b":"Agranulocytosis, bone marrow suppression"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-21"},
 {"id":"cns-anesthetics-6","system":"CNS","title":"General Anesthetics (CNS Pharmacology)","url":"cns-anesthetics-6c.html","summary":"General anesthesia, phases, classification, mechanisms (GABA-A, NMDA, K2P), stages, inhalation pharmacokinetics and adverse effects (malignant hyperthermia), IV anesthetics, ketamine, midazolam.","points":["🛌 التخدير العام والتخدير المتوازن","⏱️ مراحل العملية","💊 التصنيف","🔬 آلية العمل","📈 المراحل الأربعة","🫁 حركية الاستنشاقي","🔥 أذى الاستنشاقي وارتفاع الحرارة الخبيث","💉 الوريدية وبروبوفول","⚠️ ثيوبنتال وإيتوميديت","🧠 كيتامين وميدازولام"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Asthmatic patient: inhaled anesthetic best avoided due to airway irritation?","opts":["Isoflurane","Sevoflurane","Enflurane","Desflurane"],"a":3,"why":"Desflurane مهيّج للرئة وبيسبب Bronchospasm."},{"q":"5-year-old: dissociative state, open eyes, nystagmus, intact reflexes, strong analgesia:","opts":["Ketamine","Midazolam","Thiopental","Propofol"],"a":0,"why":"Ketamine بيعمل Dissociative anesthesia ومفضّل بالأطفال."},{"q":"General anesthesia is:","opts":["Irreversible CNS depression","Reversible CNS depression","CNS stimulation","Local nerve block"],"a":1,"why":"حالة قابلة للعكس من تثبيط الجهاز العصبي المركزي."},{"q":"NOT one of the 5 effects:","opts":["Amnesia","Analgesia","Hypertension","Skeletal muscle relaxation"],"a":2,"why":"التأثيرات الخمسة: نسيان، فقدان وعي، تسكين، ارتخاء عضلات، تثبيط المنعكسات اللاإرادية."},{"q":"Why balanced anesthesia?","opts":["Single drug cheaper","Single drug dose toxic","Single drug short","Single drug painful"],"a":1,"why":"التركيز المطلوب بدوا واحد سام."},{"q":"Metoclopramide preoperatively prevents:","opts":["Hypotension","Aspiration pneumonia (vomiting)","Pain","Amnesia"],"a":1,"why":"بيمنع التقيؤ والالتهاب الرئوي بالاستنشاق."},{"q":"Induction usually by:","opts":["Inhalation agent","IV anesthetic","Opioid","Muscle relaxant"],"a":1,"why":"البدء بدوا وريدي والاستمرار بغاز."},{"q":"Gaseous anesthetic:","opts":["Isoflurane","Nitrous oxide","Halothane","Desflurane"],"a":1,"why":"Nitrous oxide الغاز الوحيد، الباقي سوائل متطايرة."},{"q":"GABA-A activating anesthetic:","opts":["Ketamine","Nitrous oxide","Propofol","Isoflurane only"],"a":2,"why":"Propofol وEtomidate وDiazepam وThiopental."},{"q":"NMDA receptor blockers:","opts":["Propofol, thiopental","Nitrous oxide, ketamine","Etomidate, midazolam","Isoflurane, halothane"],"a":1,"why":"Nitrous oxide وKetamine."},{"q":"Inhaled anesthetics open:","opts":["Na⁺ channels","K2P leaky K⁺ channels","Ca²⁺ channels","NMDA"],"a":1,"why":"قنوات البوتاسيوم ← فرط استقطاب."},{"q":"Final effect of the modern mechanisms:","opts":["Depolarization","Hyperpolarization","No change","Ca²⁺ influx"],"a":1,"why":"فرط استقطاب ← ما في Action potential."},{"q":"Ideal stage for surgery:","opts":["I","II","III","IV"],"a":2,"why":"المرحلة 3 Surgical anesthesia."},{"q":"Stage II is associated with:","opts":["Apnea","Laryngospasm risk, delirium","Amnesia only","Regular respiration"],"a":1,"why":"هيجان وخطر Laryngospasm."},{"q":"Stage IV:","opts":["Analgesia","Excitement","Surgical","Medullary paralysis, death if unsupported"],"a":3,"why":"شلل النخاع المستطيل."},{"q":"High blood:gas partition coefficient means:","opts":["Rapid induction","Slow induction, slow recovery","Rapid recovery","No effect"],"a":1,"why":"ذوبان أعلى بالدم ← بطيء."},{"q":"High brain:gas coefficient means:","opts":["Slow induction","Rapid induction","Slow recovery only","Toxicity"],"a":1,"why":"ذوبان بالدماغ ← سريع."},{"q":"Malignant hyperthermia: cause:","opts":["GABA excess","Ryanodine receptor abnormality, Ca²⁺ release","NMDA block","K⁺ leak"],"a":1,"why":"خلل بـ Ryanodine receptor وتحرر كالسيوم هائل."},{"q":"Malignant hyperthermia treatment:","opts":["Flumazenil","Dantrolene","Naloxone","Atropine"],"a":1,"why":"Dantrolene بيحجب قنوات الكالسيوم."},{"q":"Halothane adverse effects:","opts":["Bronchospasm","Arrhythmia, hepatitis","Adrenal suppression","Hallucinations"],"a":1,"why":"Arrhythmia وHalothane hepatitis."},{"q":"Inhaled anesthetics on uterus:","opts":["Contract","Relax, ↑ postpartum bleeding","No effect","Rupture"],"a":1,"why":"بيرخوا العضل الأملس."},{"q":"IV anesthesia terminates by:","opts":["Metabolism","Redistribution","Renal excretion","Exhalation"],"a":1,"why":"إعادة التوزع من الدماغ للأنسجة."},{"q":"Propofol infusion syndrome includes all EXCEPT:","opts":["Metabolic acidosis","Rhabdomyolysis","Hyperkalemia","Hypokalemia"],"a":3,"why":"بيعمل فرط بوتاسيوم مش نقص."},{"q":"Thiopental injected SC causes:","opts":["Sedation","Necrosis, gangrene","Analgesia","Nothing"],"a":1,"why":"محلولو قلوي جداً."},{"q":"Etomidate suppresses:","opts":["Insulin","Adrenal steroids","Thyroid","Growth hormone"],"a":1,"why":"خطر بمرضى Sepsis."}],"cards":[{"f":"General anesthesia?","b":"Reversible CNS depression"},{"f":"5 effects?","b":"Amnesia, unconsciousness, analgesia, muscle relaxation, autonomic reflex inhibition"},{"f":"Why not single drug?","b":"Toxic concentration"},{"f":"Balanced anesthesia?","b":"Multiple drugs: IV, inhaled, sedative-hypnotics, opioids, NMB"},{"f":"Preanesthetic?","b":"Anxiolytic, metoclopramide"},{"f":"Induction?","b":"IV anesthetic"},{"f":"Maintenance?","b":"Inhalation anesthetic"},{"f":"Volatile liquids?","b":"Isoflurane, sevoflurane, desflurane, enflurane, halothane"},{"f":"Gas?","b":"Nitrous oxide"},{"f":"IV agents?","b":"Propofol, thiopental, etomidate, ketamine, midazolam"},{"f":"Old theory?","b":"Lipid solubility"},{"f":"GABA-A drugs?","b":"Propofol, etomidate, diazepam, thiopental"},{"f":"NMDA blockers?","b":"Nitrous oxide, ketamine"},{"f":"K2P?","b":"Inhaled anesthetics"},{"f":"Stage II?","b":"Excitement: delirium, laryngospasm"},{"f":"Stage III?","b":"Surgical anesthesia"},{"f":"Stage IV?","b":"Medullary paralysis"},{"f":"High blood:gas?","b":"Slow induction, recovery"},{"f":"High brain:gas?","b":"Rapid induction"},{"f":"Malignant hyperthermia incidence?","b":"1:20000"},{"f":"MH cause?","b":"Ryanodine receptor, Ca²⁺ release"},{"f":"MH treatment?","b":"Dantrolene"},{"f":"Halothane adverse?","b":"Arrhythmia, hepatitis"},{"f":"Desflurane adverse?","b":"Bronchospasm"},{"f":"Propofol?","b":"Most common induction; TIVA"},{"f":"Fospropofol?","b":"Water-soluble, less painful"},{"f":"Thiopental onset?","b":"20 s; 5-15 min"},{"f":"Thiopental SC?","b":"Necrosis, gangrene"},{"f":"Etomidate adverse?","b":"Adrenal suppression (sepsis), nausea"},{"f":"Ketamine state?","b":"Dissociative anesthesia"},{"f":"Midazolam reversal?","b":"Flumazenil"},{"f":"Pediatrics?","b":"Faster induction, recovery"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-21"},
 {"id":"cns-local-anesthetics-7","system":"CNS","title":"Local Anesthetics (CNS Pharmacology)","url":"cns-local-anesthetics-7.html","summary":"Local anesthesia definition, Na⁺ channel block mechanism, action potential phases, chemistry (ester/amide), lidocaine effects, toxicity, available forms, vasoconstrictors.","points":["💉 تعريف المخدّر الموضعي","🧂 آلية العمل: حجب قنوات الصوديوم","⚡ جهد الفعل","🧪 الكيمياء: إستر وأميد","❤️ تأثيرات الليدوكائين","☠️ سمّية الليدوكائين","📦 الأشكال المتوفرة","💪 مضيّقات الأوعية"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Primary mechanism of local anesthetics:","opts":["Block voltage-gated Na⁺ channels","Open K⁺ channels","Block Ca²⁺ channels","Activate GABA-A"],"a":0,"why":"بيحجب قنوات الصوديوم فما بيصير Action potential."},{"q":"Local anesthesia is:","opts":["Irreversible loss of consciousness","Reversible loss of sensation in a limited area","Loss of motion only","Systemic CNS depression"],"a":1,"why":"فقدان إحساس قابل للعكس بمنطقة محدودة."},{"q":"Resting membrane potential of nerve axon:","opts":["+40 mV","-95 mV","-90 to -60 mV","0 mV"],"a":2,"why":"جهد الراحة من -90 لـ -60."},{"q":"During excitation, Na⁺ current is:","opts":["Slow outward","Fast inward","Fast outward","Absent"],"a":1,"why":"الصوديوم بيدخل بسرعة."},{"q":"Depolarization moves membrane toward:","opts":["-95 mV","-60 mV","+40 mV","0 mV only"],"a":2,"why":"باتجاه جهد توازن الصوديوم +40."},{"q":"Repolarization is due to:","opts":["Na⁺ channels open, K⁺ closed","Na⁺ channels closed, K⁺ channels open","Ca²⁺ influx","Cl⁻ efflux"],"a":1,"why":"الصوديوم بيسكر والبوتاسيوم بيفتح."},{"q":"Repolarization drives the membrane toward:","opts":["+40 mV","-95 mV","-20 mV","+10 mV"],"a":1,"why":"-95."},{"q":"Typical local anesthetic structure has:","opts":["Only a lipophilic portion","Lipophilic and hydrophilic portions separated by ester or amide linkage","Only an amine","Two esters"],"a":1,"why":"جزء محب للدهن وجزء محب للماء ورابط."},{"q":"The intermediate linkage is:","opts":["Ether or ketone","Ester or amide","Peptide only","Disulfide"],"a":1,"why":"إستر أو أميد."},{"q":"The linkage mainly determines:","opts":["Color","Properties of the drug","Dose form only","Price"],"a":1,"why":"بيحدد خصائص الدوا."},{"q":"Lidocaine in ventricular tachycardia works by:","opts":["↑ myocardial excitability","↓ excitability, conduction, force of contraction","↑ force of contraction","Vasoconstriction"],"a":1,"why":"بيقلل استثارة عضلة القلب."},{"q":"Lidocaine anticonvulsant effect:","opts":["Lowers seizure threshold","Raises seizure threshold","No effect","Causes convulsion at all doses"],"a":1,"why":"بيرفع عتبة النوبات."},{"q":"Lidocaine analgesia mechanism:","opts":["↓ pain threshold","↑ pain threshold","Opioid receptor","NMDA block"],"a":1,"why":"بيرفع عتبة الألم."},{"q":"Toxic dose of lidocaine on CNS:","opts":["Depression only","Stimulation followed by depression","Stimulation only","No effect"],"a":1,"why":"تنبيه ثم تثبيط."},{"q":"Why can toxic lidocaine cause convulsions?","opts":["Increases inhibitory pathways","Inhibits the pathways that inhibit convulsions","Blocks K⁺ only","Vasodilatation"],"a":1,"why":"بيثبّط المسارات المثبّطة للتشنج."},{"q":"CNS toxicity range:","opts":["Mild restlessness to severe convulsion","Only coma","Only headache","None"],"a":0,"why":"من هيجان بسيط لتشنج شديد."},{"q":"Lidocaine toxicity on CVS:","opts":["↑ contractility","Overall inhibition of contractility","↑ conduction rate","↑ excitability"],"a":1,"why":"بيثبّط انقباضية القلب."},{"q":"Lidocaine vasculature effect:","opts":["Vasoconstriction","Vasodilatation by relaxing smooth muscle","No effect","Vasospasm"],"a":1,"why":"بيرخي العضل الأملس للأوعية."},{"q":"Vasodilatation by lidocaine contributes to:","opts":["Hypertension","Hypotension and CV collapse","Tachycardia only","Bleeding only"],"a":1,"why":"هبوط ضغط وانهيار."},{"q":"Most common cause of death in lidocaine overdose:","opts":["Respiratory arrest","Renal failure","Hepatic failure","Stroke"],"a":0,"why":"توقف التنفس."},{"q":"Neurotoxicity occurs when lidocaine is:","opts":["Applied at excessively high concentration","Applied with epinephrine","Given as jelly","Given dilute"],"a":0,"why":"بتركيز عالي جداً."},{"q":"Lidocaine dental cartridge epinephrine ratios:","opts":["1:80000, 1:100000, 1:200000","1:10, 1:20","1:500, 1:1000","1:10000 only"],"a":0,"why":"1:80000 و1:100000 و1:200000."},{"q":"Ointment form of lidocaine:","opts":["2%","5%","10%","1%"],"a":1,"why":"المرهم 5%."},{"q":"Vasoconstrictor addition causes all EXCEPT:","opts":["↓ blood flow to injection site","↓ absorption","↑ systemic toxicity","↑ duration of action"],"a":2,"why":"بيقلل السمّية الجهازية."},{"q":"Why does a vasoconstrictor ↑ duration of action?","opts":["Higher volume remains around the nerve longer","Increases metabolism","Blocks K⁺","Increases excretion"],"a":0,"why":"الدوا بيضل حول العصب أطول."}],"cards":[{"f":"Local anesthesia?","b":"Reversible loss of sensation, limited area"},{"f":"Cause of local anesthesia?","b":"Depression of excitation in nerve ending / inhibition of conduction in peripheral nerve"},{"f":"Mechanism of action?","b":"Block voltage-gated Na⁺ channels ← prevents action potential"},{"f":"Resting membrane potential?","b":"-90 to -60 mV"},{"f":"Depolarization?","b":"Na⁺ channels open, fast inward Na⁺, toward +40 mV"},{"f":"Repolarization?","b":"Na⁺ close, K⁺ open, toward -95 mV"},{"f":"Chemical structure?","b":"Lipophilic + ester/amide linkage + hydrophilic"},{"f":"What decides properties?","b":"Intermediate linkage"},{"f":"Lidocaine CVS effect?","b":"↓ excitability, conduction rate, force of contraction"},{"f":"Lidocaine CVS use?","b":"Ventricular tachycardia (hyperexcitable myocardium)"},{"f":"Lidocaine CNS effect?","b":"Anticonvulsant: ↑ seizure threshold; ↑ pain threshold"},{"f":"Toxic CNS?","b":"Stimulation then depression; restlessness to convulsion"},{"f":"Toxic CVS?","b":"Cardiac depression"},{"f":"Toxic vessels?","b":"Vasodilatation ← hypotension, collapse"},{"f":"Most common death in overdose?","b":"Respiratory arrest"},{"f":"Neurotoxicity?","b":"High concentration"},{"f":"Forms available?","b":"2% jelly, 5% ointment, 10-15% spray, dental cartridge, vial"},{"f":"Epinephrine ratios?","b":"1:80000, 1:100000, 1:200000"},{"f":"Vasoconstrictor purpose?","b":"Oppose vasodilatation, hemostasis"},{"f":"Vasoconstrictor effects?","b":"↓ blood flow, ↓ absorption, ↓ systemic toxicity, ↑ duration, ↓ bleeding"}],"subject":"pharm","date":"2026-11-22"},
 {"id":"micro-staph-1","system":"Bacteria","no":1,"title":"Staphylococci","url":"micro-staphylococci-1b.html","summary":"Staphylococci: Gram+ cocci in clusters, catalase +; S. aureus (coagulase +) vs CoNS; virulence factors (cell wall, enzymes, toxins), diseases, MRSA and treatment.","points":["Gram+ cocci in clusters, facultative anaerobe, catalase +, hardy on fomites","Species: S. aureus (coagulase +, most virulent), S. epidermidis (implants, PIA biofilm), S. saprophyticus (cystitis in women, novobiocin resistant)","S. aureus: yellow beta-hemolytic colonies, ferments mannitol (yellow on mannitol salt agar)","Cell wall: capsule, peptidoglycan, teichoic acid (fibronectin), protein A (binds Fc of IgG, anti-opsonin), clumping factor (fibrinogen)","Enzymes: coagulase, catalase, hyaluronidase (spreading), fibrinolysin/staphylokinase, lipases, nuclease","Toxins: α β γ δ, PVL (lyses PMNs), superantigens (enterotoxins, TSST-1), exfoliatin (cleaves desmoglein-1)","Skin: folliculitis, furuncle, carbuncle, impetigo; also osteomyelitis, septic arthritis, endocarditis, pneumonia (post-influenza)","Toxinoses: TSS (TSST-1), food poisoning (enterotoxin, incubation < 6 h), scalded skin (exfoliatin, children)","MRSA: PBP-2a (mecA); vancomycin or daptomycin; linezolid for pneumonia; VRSA via vanA","Penicillin G resistant via penicillinase; no vaccine"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which test best distinguishes S. aureus from most CoNS?","opts":["Catalase","Coagulase","Oxidase","Indole"],"a":1,"why":"Coagulase موجب مع S. aureus."},{"q":"Staphylococci differ from streptococci by:","opts":["Catalase positive","Gram negative","Strict anaerobe","Spore forming"],"a":0,"why":"الستافيلوكوك catalase موجب."},{"q":"Protein A:","opts":["Binds Fc of IgG","Lyses PMNs","Clots plasma","Cleaves desmoglein-1"],"a":0,"why":"بيرتبط بـ Fc ويمنع التهام الخلايا."},{"q":"Clumping factor binds:","opts":["Fibronectin","Fibrinogen","Collagen","Hyaluronic acid"],"a":1,"why":"بيرتبط بالفيبرينوجين."},{"q":"Spreading factor:","opts":["Coagulase","Hyaluronidase","Lipase","Nuclease"],"a":1,"why":"Hyaluronidase."},{"q":"Toxin lysing PMNs:","opts":["TSST-1","PVL","Enterotoxin","Exfoliatin"],"a":1,"why":"Panton-Valentine leukocidin."},{"q":"Which is NOT a superantigen?","opts":["TSST-1","Enterotoxin","Exfoliatin","All are"],"a":2,"why":"Exfoliatin بروتياز سيرين، مو superantigen."},{"q":"Staph food poisoning incubation:","opts":["< 6 hours","24-48 hours","1 week","Weeks"],"a":0,"why":"أقل من 6 ساعات، سمّ مسبق التشكل."},{"q":"Deeper, larger, multiloculated skin infection:","opts":["Folliculitis","Furuncle","Carbuncle","Impetigo"],"a":2,"why":"Carbuncle."},{"q":"MRSA resistance is due to:","opts":["PBP-2a","Penicillinase only","Altered ribosome","Vancomycin efflux"],"a":0,"why":"PBP-2a بألفة قليلة لـ β-lactam."},{"q":"MRSA pneumonia drug (NOT daptomycin):","opts":["Linezolid or vancomycin","Daptomycin","Penicillin G","Amoxicillin"],"a":0,"why":"Daptomycin بيتعطل بالسورفاكتانت الرئوي."},{"q":"S. saprophyticus is distinguished by:","opts":["Novobiocin resistance","Coagulase +","Mannitol +","Yellow colonies"],"a":0,"why":"مقاوم للنوفوبيوسين، وبيسبب التهاب مثانة عند النساء."}],"cards":[{"f":"Staphylococci shape?","b":"Gram+ cocci, grapelike clusters"},{"f":"Oxygen need?","b":"Facultative anaerobe"},{"f":"Catalase does?","b":"H₂O₂ → water + oxygen"},{"f":"Most virulent species?","b":"S. aureus"},{"f":"Enzyme clotting plasma?","b":"Coagulase"},{"f":"Fomites?","b":"Inanimate objects that carry infection"},{"f":"Protein A?","b":"Binds Fc of IgG: anti-opsonin"},{"f":"Clumping factor?","b":"Binds fibrinogen → fibrin, clump"},{"f":"Spreading factor?","b":"Hyaluronidase"},{"f":"Fibrinolysin?","b":"Staphylokinase: dissolves clots"},{"f":"PVL?","b":"Pore-forming, lyses PMNs"},{"f":"Superantigens?","b":"Enterotoxins, TSST-1: T-cell activation"},{"f":"Exfoliatin?","b":"Serine protease, cleaves desmoglein-1: scalded skin"},{"f":"Gastroenteritis incubation?","b":"< 6 h"},{"f":"Furuncle?","b":"Boil: subcutaneous abscess"},{"f":"Carbuncle?","b":"Larger, deeper, multiloculated"},{"f":"Most common cause of osteomyelitis?","b":"S. aureus"},{"f":"S. aureus colonies?","b":"Yellow, hemolytic, mannitol +"},{"f":"MRSA mechanism?","b":"PBP-2a (mecA), low affinity for β-lactams"},{"f":"MRSA bacteremia drug?","b":"Vancomycin or daptomycin"},{"f":"VISA / VRSA?","b":"1997 Japan / 2002 USA (vanA)"},{"f":"S. epidermidis feature?","b":"PIA: biofilm on implants"},{"f":"S. saprophyticus feature?","b":"Cystitis in women; novobiocin resistant"}],"subject":"micro","date":"2026-11-22"},
 {"id": "micro-strep-2", "system": "Bacteria", "no": 2, "title": "Genus Streptococcus (Lecture 2)", "url": "micro-strep-v2.html", "summary": "Genus Streptococcus (Gram-positive cocci): Lancefield grouping and hemolysis, S. pyogenes (M protein, scarlet fever, rheumatic fever, glomerulonephritis), S. agalactiae (GBS, CAMP), S. pneumoniae (capsule, optochin, bile solubility), viridans streptococci and Enterococcus.", "points": ["Classification: hemolysis and Lancefield groups", "S. pyogenes: virulence factors and diseases", "Post-streptococcal rheumatic fever and glomerulonephritis", "S. agalactiae (GBS) and neonatal infection", "S. pneumoniae, viridans streptococci, Enterococcus"], "mcqs": [{"q": "Most important virulence factor of S. pyogenes?", "opts": ["Hyaluronidase", "M protein", "Streptokinase", "DNase"], "a": 1, "why": "البروتين M هو الأهم لأنو بيمنع البلعمة."}, {"q": "S. pyogenes is identified by:", "opts": ["Optochin sensitivity", "Bacitracin sensitivity", "CAMP positivity", "Bile solubility"], "a": 1, "why": "باسيتراسين حساسة = pyogenes."}, {"q": "Hyaluronidase is also called:", "opts": ["Spreading factor", "Clot factor", "Cytolysin", "Adhesin"], "a": 0, "why": "بتوسّع الانتشار بالجلد."}, {"q": "Streptokinase converts:", "opts": ["Fibrin to plasmin", "Plasminogen to plasmin", "Hyaluronic acid to glucose", "IgG to IgA"], "a": 1, "why": "بتفعّل البلازمينوجين لبلازمين."}, {"q": "ASO titer indicates:", "opts": ["Immunity", "Prior streptococcal infection", "Viral infection", "Staph infection"], "a": 1, "why": "ASO فوق 200 = عدوى سابقة، مش مناعة."}, {"q": "Scarlet fever is caused by:", "opts": ["SLS", "Erythrogenic toxin", "Exotoxin B", "DNase"], "a": 1, "why": "السم الارتيروجينك بيعمل الطفح."}, {"q": "TSS is caused by:", "opts": ["Superantigen exotoxin A", "Hyaluronidase", "Pneumolysin", "SLO"], "a": 0, "why": "Exotoxin A superantigen بيعمل صدمة."}, {"q": "Necrotizing fasciitis: which toxin?", "opts": ["Exotoxin B", "SLO", "Erythrogenic", "Streptokinase"], "a": 0, "why": "Exotoxin B protease بيكسر الأنسجة."}, {"q": "Rheumatic fever is an example of:", "opts": ["Direct infection", "Post-streptococcal immune disease", "Toxin disease", "Septic shock"], "a": 1, "why": "بعد العدوى، المناعة بتهاجم القلب."}, {"q": "Glomerulonephritis follows:", "opts": ["Pharyngitis only", "Skin or pharyngeal infection", "Viral hepatitis", "UTI"], "a": 1, "why": "بعد الجلد أو الحلق، بسبب المناعة."}, {"q": "Aschoff bodies are seen in:", "opts": ["Glomerulonephritis", "Rheumatic carditis", "Cellulitis", "Pneumonia"], "a": 1, "why": "تجمعات خلايا بالقلب بالروماتيزم."}, {"q": "Group B streptococcus is identified by:", "opts": ["Optochin", "CAMP test", "PYR test", "Quellung"], "a": 1, "why": "CAMP موجب، ومعه hippurate."}, {"q": "Neonatal GBS infection usually occurs:", "opts": ["After 1 month", "Within 24 hours, first 3 days", "At 5-15 years", "Only in adults"], "a": 1, "why": "بأول أيام المولود."}, {"q": "Capsule is the main virulence factor of:", "opts": ["S. pyogenes", "S. agalactiae", "S. pneumoniae", "S. mutans"], "a": 2, "why": "الكبسولة متعددة السكر أهم عامل."}, {"q": "Quellung reaction identifies:", "opts": ["Gram stain", "Capsule type (serotype)", "Hemolysis", "Bile solubility"], "a": 1, "why": "انتفاخ الكبسولة بيدل على النوع."}, {"q": "Pneumococcus is:", "opts": ["Optochin resistant", "Bile soluble", "Lancefield group A", "Gram-negative"], "a": 1, "why": "بتذوب بالصفراء وحساسة للأوبتوتشين."}, {"q": "Viridans streptococci cause:", "opts": ["Subacute endocarditis", "Acute pyoderma only", "Scarlet fever", "Neonatal sepsis"], "a": 0, "why": "أهم سبب لالتهاب الشغاف تحت الحاد."}, {"q": "Viridans are Lancefield:", "opts": ["Group A", "Group B", "Negative", "Group D"], "a": 2, "why": "ما بيعطوا لانسفيلد."}, {"q": "Enterococcus most common species:", "opts": ["E. faecium", "E. faecalis", "E. gallinarum", "E. casseliflavus"], "a": 1, "why": "faecalis بـ80-90%."}, {"q": "Enterococcus tolerates:", "opts": ["6.5% NaCl", "0% NaCl", "Only CO₂", "Only anaerobic"], "a": 0, "why": "بينمو ب6.5% ملح."}, {"q": "Most common enterococcal infection:", "opts": ["Endocarditis", "UTI", "Pneumonia", "Meningitis"], "a": 1, "why": "UTI خصوصاً مع القسطرة."}, {"q": "Penicillin-resistant GPC in blood after cardiac surgery:", "opts": ["Enterococcus", "Group A strep", "Group B strep", "Neisseria"], "a": 0, "why": "بالمستشفى بعد جراحة، مقاومة للبنسلين."}, {"q": "Penicillin is drug of choice for:", "opts": ["Enterococci", "S. pneumoniae", "Viridans only", "None"], "a": 1, "why": "البنسلين الأول للـPneumococcus."}, {"q": "Pharyngitis first-line treatment:", "opts": ["Vancomycin", "Penicillin V or amoxicillin", "Chloramphenicol", "Metronidazole"], "a": 1, "why": "البنسلين V أو الأموكسيسيلين أول خط."}, {"q": "Erythrogenic toxin acts as:", "opts": ["Hyaluronidase", "Superantigen", "Protease", "Adhesin"], "a": 1, "why": "متل TSST بالـStaph."}], "cards": [{"f": "Which is the main virulence factor of S. pyogenes?", "b": "M protein (anti-phagocytosis)"}, {"f": "Strep: how does β-hemolysis appear?", "b": "Complete clearing of RBCs around colony"}, {"f": "Lancefield group of S. pyogenes?", "b": "Group A"}, {"f": "PYR test in S. pyogenes?", "b": "Positive"}, {"f": "Bacitracin result in pyogenes?", "b": "Wide zone of inhibition"}, {"f": "Hyaluronidase is called?", "b": "Spreading factor (cellulitis)"}, {"f": "Streptokinase function?", "b": "Converts plasminogen to plasmin"}, {"f": "IgG-degrading enzyme effect?", "b": "Prevents opsonization and complement"}, {"f": "Erythrogenic toxin disease?", "b": "Scarlet fever (superantigen)"}, {"f": "SLO and disease marker?", "b": "ASO titer, oxygen-labile"}, {"f": "SLS property?", "b": "Oxygen-stable, non-antigenic"}, {"f": "Exotoxin A disease?", "b": "Streptococcal TSS"}, {"f": "Exotoxin B effect?", "b": "Protease, necrotizing fasciitis"}, {"f": "Erysipelas age group?", "b": "Elderly, sharp spreading lesion"}, {"f": "Cellulitis edge?", "b": "Ill-defined margin"}, {"f": "Scarlet fever rash?", "b": "Diffuse red, peels in 5-7 days"}, {"f": "TSS mortality?", "b": "About 30%"}, {"f": "Rheumatic fever age?", "b": "Children 5-15 years"}, {"f": "Rheumatic fever mechanism?", "b": "Cross-reaction with cardiac muscle"}, {"f": "Aschoff bodies in?", "b": "Rheumatic carditis"}, {"f": "GN after infection?", "b": "Skin or pharyngeal, 1-5 weeks"}, {"f": "ASO >300 IU/mL means?", "b": "Strongly indicative of infection"}, {"f": "S. agalactiae hippurate?", "b": "Positive"}, {"f": "Neonatal GBS onset?", "b": "Usually within 24 h, first 3 days"}, {"f": "CAMP test result for GBS?", "b": "Positive, arrow-shaped hemolysis"}, {"f": "Pneumococcus morphology?", "b": "Lancet-shaped diplococci"}, {"f": "Pneumococcus virulence key?", "b": "Capsular polysaccharide"}, {"f": "Quellung reaction?", "b": "Capsule swelling test for serotype"}, {"f": "Pneumococcus optochin?", "b": "Sensitive"}, {"f": "Pneumococcus bile?", "b": "Soluble"}, {"f": "Viridans Lancefield?", "b": "Negative"}, {"f": "Viridans subacute disease?", "b": "Endocarditis on damaged valves"}, {"f": "Enterococcus most common species?", "b": "E. faecalis"}, {"f": "Enterococcus most common infection?", "b": "UTI (catheter)"}, {"f": "Enterococcus NaCl tolerance?", "b": "Grows in 6.5% NaCl"}, {"f": "VRE means?", "b": "Vancomycin-resistant enterococci"}, {"f": "Penicillin-resistant gram-positive cocci in blood after cardiac surgery?", "b": "Enterococcus species (nosocomial)"}, {"f": "Pyogenes first-line treatment?", "b": "Oral penicillin V or amoxicillin"}, {"f": "Pneumonia drug of choice?", "b": "Penicillin"}], "subject": "micro", "date": "2026-11-26"},
 {"id":"micro-immunity-2","system":"Immunity","no":10,"title":"Immunity to Infection (Lecture 10)","url":"micro-immunity-infection-2f.html","summary":"Host defense vs virulence; immunity to extracellular bacteria (humoral), intracellular bacteria (Th1, leprosy forms), viruses (IFN, Tc, antibodies), parasites (Th2, eosinophils), fungi; microbial escape mechanisms.","points":["Outcome = virulence vs host defense; pathogen factors: dose, virulence, route; host factors: non-specific defenses, immune competence, genetics, previous exposure, co-infection","Outside the cell → antibodies (humoral); inside the cell → cell-mediated immunity","Extracellular bacteria: phagocytosis, alternative complement; antibodies: opsonic IgG, agglutinating IgM, ADCC, blocking (V. cholerae), neutralizing, complement fixing; Th via MHC II","Intracellular bacteria (TB, leprosy): survive in macrophages; NK (IFN) then Th1 (IL-12, IFN-γ); humoral useless","Tuberculoid leprosy: Th1, controlled; lepromatous: Th2, humoral, fatal","Viruses: type I IFN (α, β), NK, MHC I, Tc kills with perforin + granzymes, IgA at mucosa","Helminths: Th2 (IL-4, IL-5, IL-13) → IgE + eosinophils (major basic protein); protozoa: Th1, IFN-γ activates macrophages","Escape: bacteria (capsule, protease, intracellular), viruses (latency, variation, ↓ MHC, IL-10), parasites (location, variation)","Fungi: neutrophils key; Th1 protective, Th2 harmful, antibodies not useful"],"mcqs":[{"q":"A pathogen lives freely in the blood. The main protective response is:","opts":["Humoral (antibodies)","Cell-mediated only","NK cells only","Th1 macrophage activation"],"a":0,"why":"برا الخلية ← أجسام مضادة."},{"q":"Which is a HOST factor, not a pathogen factor?","opts":["Dose","Virulence","Route of entry","Previous exposure"],"a":3,"why":"التعرض السابق عامل مضيف."},{"q":"Opsonic antibody for extracellular bacteria:","opts":["IgG","IgA","IgE","IgD"],"a":0,"why":"IgG بيغلّف الجرثومة فبتنبلع."},{"q":"Antibody causing agglutination:","opts":["IgM","IgE","IgD","IgA"],"a":0,"why":"IgM."},{"q":"Blocking antibodies prevent:","opts":["Adherence to mucous membrane","Phagocytosis","Complement activation","T-cell activation"],"a":0,"why":"متل Vibrio cholerae."},{"q":"Innate immunity is ineffective against intracellular bacteria because:","opts":["They resist degradation in phagocytes","They are too large","No complement","They lack antigens"],"a":0,"why":"بتقاوم الهضم جوا البلعميات."},{"q":"Cytokines promoting Th1:","opts":["IL-12 and IFN-γ","IL-4 and IL-5","IL-10 and TGF-β","IL-13 only"],"a":0,"why":"IL-12 من البلعميات وIFN-γ من NK."},{"q":"Lepromatous leprosy is associated with:","opts":["Th1 dominance","Th2 dominance","Strong CMI","No bacilli"],"a":1,"why":"Th2 ← مناعة خلطية ما بتنفع، فبكتيريا كتيرة."},{"q":"Infected cells are recognized by Tc through:","opts":["MHC I","MHC II","IgE","Complement"],"a":0,"why":"الببتيدات الفيروسية بتنعرض على MHC I."},{"q":"Th2 cytokines against helminths:","opts":["IL-4, IL-5, IL-13","IL-12, IFN-γ","IL-2 only","TNF only"],"a":0,"why":"بتحفّز IgE والحمضات."},{"q":"Adenovirus escapes immunity by:","opts":["Latency","Inhibiting MHC expression","Antigenic variation","IL-10"],"a":1,"why":"بيثبّط تعبير MHC."},{"q":"Key innate cell against fungi:","opts":["Neutrophil","Eosinophil","Mast cell","Basophil"],"a":0,"why":"العدلات."}],"cards":[{"f":"Outside the cell → which immunity?","b":"Humoral (antibodies)"},{"f":"Inside the cell → which immunity?","b":"Cell-mediated"},{"f":"Opsonic antibody?","b":"IgG: coats bacteria"},{"f":"Agglutinating antibody?","b":"IgM"},{"f":"Blocking antibody example?","b":"Vibrio cholerae adherence"},{"f":"Main response vs intracellular bacteria?","b":"Th1 macrophage activation"},{"f":"Cytokines promoting Th1?","b":"IL-12 (macrophage), IFN-γ (NK)"},{"f":"Tuberculoid leprosy?","b":"Th1: controlled"},{"f":"Lepromatous leprosy?","b":"Th2: humoral, useless, fatal"},{"f":"Respiratory burst?","b":"Rapid ↑ O₂ use → H₂O₂ kills"},{"f":"Type I IFN?","b":"IFN-α, IFN-β: antiviral state, NK, ↑ MHC I"},{"f":"Viral peptides presented on?","b":"MHC I"},{"f":"Tc kills by?","b":"Perforin + granzymes"},{"f":"IgA role in viruses?","b":"Neutralizes at mucosa"},{"f":"HSV escape?","b":"Latency"},{"f":"Influenza, HIV escape?","b":"Antigenic variation"},{"f":"Adenovirus escape?","b":"Inhibits MHC expression"},{"f":"EBV escape?","b":"IL-10"},{"f":"HCV escape?","b":"Persistence"},{"f":"Th2 cytokines vs helminths?","b":"IL-4, IL-5, IL-13"},{"f":"Eosinophil toxic protein?","b":"Major basic protein"},{"f":"T. cruzi escape?","b":"Lives in macrophages"},{"f":"Key innate cell vs fungi?","b":"Neutrophil"},{"f":"Fungi: Th1 vs Th2?","b":"Th1 protective, Th2 harmful"}],"subject":"micro","date":"2026-11-22"},
  {"id":"micro-antibiotic-3","system":"Bacteria","no":3,"title":"Antibiotic Resistance (Lecture 3)","url":"micro-antibiotic-resistance-3b.html","summary":"Antibiotics vs antimicrobials, MIC and resistance; bactericidal vs bacteriostatic; history (Fleming, penicillin, penicillinase) and the resistance crisis; antibiotic classification by target; intrinsic vs acquired resistance (mutation, plasmids); mechanisms: reduced permeability (porins), target change and enzymatic inactivation (beta-lactamase), efflux pumps (MDR); phenotypic vs genotypic detection; containing resistance (empirical vs definitive therapy).","points":["Antibiotic: anti = against, bios = life; antimicrobial covers bacteria, viruses, fungi, parasites","Resistance: not inhibited at the usual systemic concentration; MIC rises","Bactericidal kills (needed in weak immunity, severe infection); bacteriostatic only stops growth and needs host defense","Fleming 1928 penicillin; penicillinase breaks penicillin, so beta-lactams were developed; resistance means treatment failure, more deaths, higher cost","Classes by target: cell wall, protein synthesis (50S, 30S), nucleic acids, folic acid pathway, membrane","Intrinsic resistance (e.g. anaerobes vs aminoglycosides) vs acquired (mutation or plasmids)","Mechanisms: lower permeability (porin loss, e.g. Pseudomonas vs imipenem); target change (MRSA); enzyme inactivation (beta-lactamase; acetyl, phosphate, adenylyl groups); efflux pumps (MDR is worst)","Detection: phenotypic (disc diffusion, MIC) vs genotypic (PCR)","Containment: environment, drug, patient and doctor factors; empirical vs definitive therapy; infection control"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Antibiotic resistance is best defined as:","opts":["Slow drug absorption","Organism not inhibited by usual systemic concentration with normal dosage","Organism killed at low MIC","Drug allergy"],"a":1,"why":"المقاومة: الجرثومة ما بتتأثر بالجرعة العادية."},{"q":"Which is bactericidal?","opts":["Erythromycin","Sulfonamides","Aminoglycosides","Chloramphenicol"],"a":2,"why":"الأمينوغليكوزيدات قاتلة."},{"q":"Bacteriostatic drugs need which host mechanism?","opts":["Phagocytosis","Hemolysis","Fever only","Gluconeogenesis"],"a":0,"why":"بدها بلعمة."},{"q":"Streptomycin was isolated in 1944 by:","opts":["Koch","Selman and Albert","Fleming","Pasteur"],"a":1,"why":"سلمان وألبرت."},{"q":"Penicillinase is also called:","opts":["Transpeptidase","Gyrase","Polymerase","Beta-lactamase"],"a":3,"why":"Beta-lactamase."},{"q":"Which is NOT a target of antibiotics?","opts":["Host collagen synthesis","Cell wall synthesis","Protein synthesis","Folic acid"],"a":0,"why":"مش من الأهداف."},{"q":"Sulfonamides inhibit:","opts":["50S","Gyrase","Folic acid synthesis","Cell wall"],"a":2,"why":"حمض الفوليك."},{"q":"Natural resistance of anaerobes to aminoglycosides is an example of:","opts":["Acquired resistance","Plasmid resistance","Efflux","Intrinsic resistance"],"a":3,"why":"طبيعية."},{"q":"Porin channels are involved in:","opts":["Drug entry through outer membrane","Efflux only","Beta-lactamase","Mutation"],"a":0,"why":"مدخل الدوا."},{"q":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa resists imipenem by:","opts":["Acetylation","Plasmid loss","Preventing access","Efflux only"],"a":2,"why":"منع الدخول."},{"q":"Chloramphenicol resistance in Enterobacteriaceae is by:","opts":["Efflux","Porin","PBP","Acetylation"],"a":3,"why":"أستلة."},{"q":"Efflux pumps cause:","opts":["Drug activation","↓ intracellular drug concentration","↑ concentration","↑ uptake"],"a":1,"why":"تركيز أقل."},{"q":"Disc diffusion is a:","opts":["Efflux test","Plasmid method","Phenotypic method","Genotypic method"],"a":2,"why":"فينوتايب."},{"q":"Which is NOT a prescriber-related factor?","opts":["Poor adherence","Overuse","Inadequate dosing","Lack of training"],"a":0,"why":"عدم الالتزام عند المريض."},{"q":"Empirical use means:","opts":["Never","Antimicrobial before pathogen or susceptibility is known","After culture","Prophylaxis"],"a":1,"why":"قبل معرفة الجرثومة."}],"cards":[{"f":"Antibiotic: Greek meaning?","b":"Anti = against, bios = life"},{"f":"Resistance definition?","b":"Not inhibited by usual systemic concentration with normal dosage; MIC falls"},{"f":"MIC?","b":"Minimum inhibitory concentration"},{"f":"Bactericidal?","b":"Kills bacteria directly"},{"f":"Bacteriostatic?","b":"Stops growth; regrows if withdrawn; needs host defense"},{"f":"Fleming 1928?","b":"Penicillium notatum killed Staphylococcus"},{"f":"Streptomycin isolated by?","b":"Selman and Albert, 1944"},{"f":"Penicillinase?","b":"Beta-lactamase: breaks penicillin"},{"f":"Why resistance is a concern?","b":"Treatment failure, mortality, spread, cost, pre-antibiotic era"},{"f":"3 ways to classify?","b":"Mechanism, spectrum, mode of action"},{"f":"6 targets?","b":"Cell wall, protein, DNA, RNA, folic acid, mycolic acid"},{"f":"Intrinsic resistance?","b":"Born resistant; all strains of species"},{"f":"Intrinsic example?","b":"Anaerobes ← aminoglycosides"},{"f":"Acquired resistance?","b":"Mutation or horizontal gene acquisition"},{"f":"Plasmid?","b":"Extrachromosomal DNA carrying resistance genes"},{"f":"Mechanism 1?","b":"Preventing access (porins)"},{"f":"Aminoglycoside target?","b":"Ribosome"},{"f":"Beta-lactam target?","b":"PBPs"},{"f":"Mechanism 2?","b":"Target modification or drug degradation"},{"f":"Beta-lactamase action?","b":"Hydrolyzes beta-lactam ring ← penicilloic acid"},{"f":"Chloramphenicol resistance?","b":"Acetylation (Enterobacteriaceae)"},{"f":"Mechanism 3?","b":"Efflux pumps"},{"f":"MDR pump?","b":"Expels many different drugs"},{"f":"Phenotypic methods?","b":"Agar screen, disc diffusion, broth dilution, E-test, MIC, Vitek"},{"f":"Genotypic methods?","b":"DNA hybridization, PCR, microarray"},{"f":"4 factors of resistance?","b":"Environmental, drug, patient, prescriber"},{"f":"Empirical use?","b":"Antimicrobial before pathogen or susceptibility is known"},{"f":"Ideal antimicrobial?","b":"Selectively toxic, cidal, soluble, potent, no resistance, reaches site, reasonably priced"}],"subject":"micro","date":"2026-11-24"},
 {"id":"micro-neisseria-4","system":"Bacteria","no":4,"title":"Neisseria (Lecture 4)","url":"micro-neisseria-4.html","summary":"Neisseria are Gram-negative diplococci (kidney-shaped), oxidase positive. N. meningitidis (capsule, carriers in the nasopharynx, droplets; meningitis and meningococcemia with petechial rash) and N. gonorrhoeae (sexually transmitted; gonorrhea, pelvic inflammatory disease, infertility). Virulence factors: pili with antigenic variation, capsule, LOS endotoxin, IgA protease. Diagnosis: nasopharyngeal swab, blood, CSF; chocolate agar and Thayer-Martin; sugar fermentation (glucose only vs glucose and maltose). Treatment: ceftriaxone or cefotaxime, penicillin as alternative, and prevention.","points":["Neisseria: Gram-negative diplococci, kidney-shaped, oxidase positive; important species N. meningitidis and N. gonorrhoeae","Gonococcus ferments glucose only; meningococcus ferments glucose and maltose","Virulence: pili (antigenic variation, DNA uptake), capsule (meningococcus only), endotoxin LOS, IgA protease","Meningococcus: carriers in the nasopharynx, droplet spread, then septicemia or meningitis; petechial/purpuric rash that does not blanch","Samples: nasopharyngeal swab, blood, CSF (lumbar puncture when neck stiffness)","Culture on chocolate agar (blood agar inhibits growth); Thayer-Martin selective medium","Gonorrhea: sexually transmitted, may be asymptomatic then pelvic inflammatory disease and infertility","Treatment of meningococcal meningitis: third generation cephalosporin (ceftriaxone, cefotaxime) for 7 days; penicillin as an alternative","Prevention: infection control, close contact precautions"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which test differentiates N. gonorrhoeae from N. meningitidis?","opts":["Catalase test","Carbohydrate utilization","Oxidase test","Gram stain"],"a":1,"why":"الاتنين أوكسيداز وكاتالاز موجبين. التفريق بالسكر: الغونوريا غلوكوز بس والمننجيتيديس غلوكوز + مالتوز."},{"q":"Why can N. gonorrhoeae not be serogrouped?","opts":["No pili","No LOS","No IgA protease","No polysaccharide capsule"],"a":3,"why":"التقسيم لمجموعات مبني ع الكبسولة، والغونوريا ما عندها كبسولة."},{"q":"Major virulence factor of N. meningitidis:","opts":["IgA protease","Pili","Polysaccharide capsule","Opa proteins"],"a":2,"why":"الكبسولة بتحمي من البلعمة وبتخلّي البكتيريا تعيش بالدم."},{"q":"Antigenic variation of pili leads to:","opts":["Immune evasion","Capsule loss","Oxidase negativity","Glucose fermentation"],"a":0,"why":"تغيّر شكل الـPili بيخلّي المناعة ما تعرفها."},{"q":"Which virulence factor is NOT in N. gonorrhoeae?","opts":["LOS","Opa proteins","Polysaccharide capsule","Pili"],"a":2,"why":"الغونوريا بلا كبسولة."},{"q":"Most common route of meningococci to meninges:","opts":["Bloodstream","Olfactory nerve","Conjunctiva","Lymph"],"a":0,"why":"الأكتر: الدم (تسمم دم) ثم السحايا."},{"q":"Rare route through the cribriform plate:","opts":["Facial nerve","Optic nerve","Vagus","Olfactory nerve"],"a":3,"why":"عصب الشم عبر الصفيحة المنخلية."},{"q":"Waterhouse-Friderichsen includes:","opts":["Renal stones","Bilateral adrenal bleeding","Hepatic abscess","Pleural effusion"],"a":1,"why":"نزيف بالغدتين الكظريتين."},{"q":"Typical age of pyogenic meningococcal meningitis:","opts":["Elderly","Newborn only","Teenagers only","3-5 years"],"a":3,"why":"الأطفال بين 3 و5 سنين."},{"q":"Feature distinguishing meningococcal meningitis from other bacterial meningitis:","opts":["Headache","Vomiting","Skin rash","Fever"],"a":2,"why":"الطفح هو العلامة المميزة."},{"q":"Postmeningococcal reactive disease occurs:","opts":["4-10 days after infection","At the first hour","After 1 year","During incubation"],"a":0,"why":"معقدات مناعية بين مستضد الكبسولة وأجسامها المضادة."},{"q":"Ophthalmia neonatorum from N. gonorrhoeae is acquired:","opts":["From droplets","From water","Through the birth canal","From breast milk"],"a":2,"why":"المولود بيعدي من قناة الولادة."},{"q":"First specimen collected as routine check:","opts":["Nasopharyngeal swab","CSF","Urine","Sputum"],"a":0,"why":"لنشوف إذا حامل."},{"q":"CSF is taken only if:","opts":["Any fever","Mild cough","Rash only","Stiff neck with other symptoms"],"a":3,"why":"تصلّب الرقبة مع باقي الأعراض."},{"q":"Why is blood agar unsuitable for Neisseria?","opts":["No CO₂","Toxic trace metals and fatty acids inhibit growth","Too acidic","Too cold"],"a":1,"why":"المعادن السامة والأحماض الدهنية بتثبّطها."}],"cards":[{"f":"Genus Neisseria shape?","b":"Gram-negative diplococci, kidney-shaped"},{"f":"Two important species?","b":"N. meningitidis, N. gonorrhoeae"},{"f":"Oxidase and catalase?","b":"Both positive"},{"f":"Growth media?","b":"Chocolate agar, Thayer-Martin"},{"f":"CO₂ requirement?","b":"5-10%, humid"},{"f":"Sensitive to?","b":"Drying and cold"},{"f":"Glucose only?","b":"N. gonorrhoeae"},{"f":"Glucose + maltose?","b":"N. meningitidis"},{"f":"Serogroups?","b":"A, B, C, W, Y, X: polysaccharide capsule"},{"f":"Why no gonorrhoeae vaccine?","b":"No capsule, no serogroups"},{"f":"Pili functions?","b":"Adhesion, antigenic variation, DNA uptake"},{"f":"Meningococcus major virulence factor?","b":"Polysaccharide capsule"},{"f":"LOS effects?","b":"Cytokines, septic shock, vascular damage, petechiae"},{"f":"IgA protease?","b":"Cleaves secretory IgA: mucosal colonization"},{"f":"Opa proteins?","b":"Phase-variable outer membrane proteins"},{"f":"Reservoir of meningococci?","b":"Nasopharyngeal carriers, children"},{"f":"Most common route to meninges?","b":"Bloodstream (septicemia)"},{"f":"Other routes?","b":"Olfactory nerve (cribriform plate); conjunctiva (rare)"},{"f":"Non-blanching rash?","b":"Petechiae, purpura &gt; 80%"},{"f":"Waterhouse-Friderichsen?","b":"Purpura fulminans, shock, DIC, bilateral adrenal bleeding"},{"f":"Meningitis age group?","b":"3-5 years"},{"f":"Chronic meningococcemia?","b":"Recurring rash, fever, joint inflammation, enlarged spleen"},{"f":"Post-meningococcal disease?","b":"4-10 days: immune complexes, arthritis, iritis, pericarditis, polyserositis"},{"f":"Mortality?","b":"&gt; 10%; untreated up to 50%"},{"f":"Gonorrhea sites?","b":"Urethra (men), cervix (women)"},{"f":"Ophthalmia neonatorum?","b":"Neonatal conjunctivitis: birth canal; other cause Chlamydia trachomatis"},{"f":"CSF findings?","b":"↑ pressure, ↑ protein, ↓ glucose; Gram-negative diplococci"},{"f":"Chocolate agar blood heated to?","b":"80°C: inactivates inhibitors"},{"f":"Thayer-Martin VCNT?","b":"Vancomycin, colistin, nystatin, trimethoprim"},{"f":"Meningitis treatment?","b":"Ceftriaxone or cefotaxime 7 days; penicillin alternative"}],"subject":"micro","date":"2026-11-24"},
 {"id":"micro-listeria-5","system":"Bacteria","no":5,"title":"Listeria (Lecture 5)","url":"micro-listeria-5.html","summary":"Listeria monocytogenes: Gram-positive non-spore-forming rods, catalase positive, tumbling motility, narrow beta-hemolysis on blood agar. Found in soil, animals and plants; spread by unpasteurized milk, undercooked meat and raw vegetables. Intracellular pathogen: listeriolysin escapes the phagosome and actin rockets spread it cell to cell; cell-mediated immunity is key. Affects pregnant women, fetus and newborn, and immunocompromised patients (septicemia, meningitis). Treatment: ampicillin with or without gentamicin, TMP-SMX as alternative; gastroenteritis usually needs no treatment; no vaccine, prevention by reducing exposure.","points":["Listeria monocytogenes: Gram-positive rods, non-spore forming, catalase positive, tumbling (umbrella) motility","Narrow beta-hemolysis on blood agar; rods not cocci (differs from Staphylococcus)","Spread by food: unpasteurized milk, undercooked meat, raw vegetables","Intracellular: listeriolysin escapes the phagosome, actin rockets spread cell to cell","Cell-mediated immunity is key, so risk in pregnancy, newborns, transplant and immunocompromised patients","Mother may be mildly ill or asymptomatic while the fetus is harmed (placenta or birth canal)","Clinical forms: septicemia, meningitis, granulomatous skin lesions, mild gastroenteritis","Diagnosis: culture from blood or CSF; Gram stain, hemolysis, catalase, motility","Treatment: ampicillin with or without gentamicin; TMP-SMX alternative; no vaccine"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which group is NOT at higher risk for listeriosis?","opts":["Adults","Pregnant women","Newborns","Immunosuppressed people"],"a":0,"why":"الحوامل والمواليد والمناعة الضعيفة هنّي الأكتر خطر. البالغين الأصحاء مش ضمنهم."},{"q":"Best description of Listeria monocytogenes?","opts":["Gram-negative lactose-fermenting oxidase-negative bacilli","Gram-positive, facultative intracellular, motile bacilli","Gram-positive spore-forming strict aerobic cocci","Gram-negative curved microaerophilic rods"],"a":1,"why":"Gram+، داخل الخلية، ومتحركة."},{"q":"Only species that infects humans:","opts":["Listeria monocytogenes","Staphylococcus aureus","Streptococcus pyogenes","Neisseria meningitidis"],"a":0,"why":"المحاضرة قالت إنو النوع الوحيد."},{"q":"Catalase test in Listeria:","opts":["Negative","Positive","Variable","Not done"],"a":1,"why":"Listeria كاتالاز موجب."},{"q":"Key virulence factor that lets Listeria escape the phagosome:","opts":["Listeriolysin","LOS","IgA protease","Pili"],"a":0,"why":"Listeriolysin بيطلّعها من الفاجوسوم."},{"q":"Defense most important against Listeria:","opts":["Humoral immunity","Cell-mediated immunity","Complement only","Mucosal IgA only"],"a":1,"why":"لأنها بتعيش جوا الخلية، فالمناعة الخلوية أهم."},{"q":"Listeria can cause spontaneous abortion because it:","opts":["Destroys the placenta by toxin","Is transmitted to the fetus","Blocks progesterone","Causes hemolysis"],"a":1,"why":"بتنتقل للجنين وبتسبب إجهاض."},{"q":"Gastroenteritis from Listeria typically includes:","opts":["Bloody stools and high vomiting","Watery diarrhea, fever, headache, abdominal cramps","Rash and arthritis","Pneumonia"],"a":1,"why":"إسهال مائي وحرارة وصداع وتقلصات، وقليل قيء."},{"q":"Semi-solid agar motility result:","opts":["Growth only at surface","Umbrella-shaped zone ~0.5 cm below surface","No growth","Dark pigment"],"a":1,"why":"شكل المظلة تحت السطح."},{"q":"Listeria differs from Staphylococcus in:","opts":["Gram stain","Shape: rods vs cocci","Catalase","Hemolysis only"],"a":1,"why":"Listeria عصيات، Staph كروية."},{"q":"First-line drug for invasive Listeria disease:","opts":["Ceftriaxone only","Ampicillin ± gentamicin","Vancomycin only","Erythromycin"],"a":1,"why":"أمبيسيلين مع أو بدون جنتاميسين."},{"q":"Resistance of Listeria to first-line drugs is:","opts":["Common","Rare","Universal","Not described"],"a":1,"why":"المقاومة نادرة."},{"q":"Gastroenteritis from Listeria typically requires:","opts":["Ampicillin","Surgery","No treatment","Plasma exchange"],"a":2,"why":"عادة ما بيحتاج علاج."},{"q":"Neonatal Listeria meningitis is acquired:","opts":["From the environment only","From mother via placenta or birth canal","From breast milk only","Via skin contact only"],"a":1,"why":"من الأم بالمشيمة أو بقناة الولادة."},{"q":"Case: 2-week-old, Gram+ rods, narrow β-hemolysis. Most likely organism:","opts":["Listeria monocytogenes","Neisseria gonorrhoeae","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Candida albicans"],"a":0,"why":"الصورة مطابقة لـ Listeria."}],"cards":[{"f":"Gram stain of Listeria?","b":"Gram-positive short rods"},{"f":"Catalase in Listeria?","b":"Positive"},{"f":"Hemolysis on blood agar?","b":"Narrow zone of β-hemolysis"},{"f":"Motility pattern?","b":"Tumbling (end-over-end)"},{"f":"Wet mount motility result?","b":"Positive: end-over-end tumbling"},{"f":"Semi-solid agar motility?","b":"Umbrella-shaped growth ~0.5 cm below surface"},{"f":"Spore forming?","b":"No, non-spore forming"},{"f":"Intracellular?","b":"Facultative intracellular"},{"f":"Only species infecting humans?","b":"Listeria monocytogenes"},{"f":"Main food sources?","b":"Unpasteurized milk, undercooked meat, raw vegetables"},{"f":"Risk groups?","b":"Pregnant women, fetus, newborns, immunocompromised"},{"f":"Escape from phagosome by?","b":"Listeriolysin"},{"f":"Spread between cells by?","b":"Actin rockets"},{"f":"Key host defense?","b":"Cell-mediated immunity"},{"f":"Listeria in pregnancy?","b":"Mild flu-like illness, may cause abortion"},{"f":"Neonatal infection route?","b":"Placenta or birth canal"},{"f":"Most common forms?","b":"Septicemia and meningitis"},{"f":"Gastroenteritis features?","b":"Watery diarrhea, fever, headache, cramps, little vomiting"},{"f":"CAMP test result?","b":"Positive"},{"f":"ELISA and PCR in Listeria?","b":"Confirmatory tests"},{"f":"First-line for meningitis?","b":"Ampicillin ± gentamicin"},{"f":"Alternative drug?","b":"Trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole"},{"f":"Resistant strains?","b":"Rare"},{"f":"Gastroenteritis treatment?","b":"Usually none required"},{"f":"Prevention?","b":"No immunization; limit exposure"},{"f":"Storage risk?","b":"Cold refrigerated food can increase gastroenteritis risk"},{"f":"Listeria vs Staph catalase?","b":"Both positive; Listeria is rod, Staph cocci"},{"f":"Strep catalase?","b":"Negative"},{"f":"Listeria cocci or rods?","b":"Rods"},{"f":"Neonatal meningitis cause?","b":"Listeria monocytogenes (case)"}],"subject":"micro","date":"2026-11-25"},
 {"id":"micro-complement","system":"Immunity","title":"Complement System","url":"micro-complement.html","summary":"The complement system: about 34 plasma proteins, heat labile (56 C, 30 min). Three activation pathways: classical (antibody IgM or IgG, C1q), alternative (microbial surface, C3b with factors B, D and properdin) and lectin (MBL and MASP). All converge on C3 convertase, C5 convertase and the membrane attack complex C5b-9 which lyses the cell. Functions: lysis, opsonization (C3b), inflammation (anaphylatoxins C3a, C4a, C5a) and chemotaxis. Regulators: C1 inhibitor, C4bp, factor H and I, CD55, CD59. Deficiencies: C2 and C4 (SLE-like), C3 (recurrent pyogenic infections), C5-C9 (Neisseria), C1INH (hereditary angioedema).","points":["About 34 plasma proteins, inactive until activated; destroyed by heating at 56 C for 30 minutes","Three pathways: classical (IgM or IgG), alternative (microbial surface, factors B, D, P), lectin (MBL, MASP)","C1 = C1q, C1r, C1s; C1q binds antibody; one IgM is enough while IgG needs several; IgA and IgE do not activate","C3 convertase then C5 convertase then membrane attack complex C5b-9 (up to 19 C9) which lyses the cell","C3b is the main opsonin; C3a, C4a, C5a are anaphylatoxins (vascular permeability, mast cell histamine)","C5a and C3a attract neutrophils and macrophages (chemotaxis)","Regulators: C1 inhibitor, C4bp, factor H, factor I, CD55, CD59","C1INH deficiency causes hereditary angioedema","C2 and C4 deficiency: SLE-like disease; C3 deficiency: severe recurrent pyogenic infections"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Complement system is discovered by:","opts":["Koch","Bordet","Pasteur","Fleming"],"a":1,"why":"الاكتشاف كان من Bordet سنة 1894."},{"q":"Most abundant complement component:","opts":["C1","C3","C5","C9"],"a":1,"why":"C3 أكتر مكون."},{"q":"Classical pathway is activated by:","opts":["Endotoxin","Antigen-antibody complexes","Mannose only","Cobra venom only"],"a":1,"why":"المسار الكلاسيكي بيعتمد على الجسم المضاد."},{"q":"Alternative pathway is activated by:","opts":["Antigen-antibody complexes only","Endotoxin (LPS)","IgA","IgE"],"a":1,"why":"LPS بيفعّل البديل."},{"q":"C1 complex is composed of:","opts":["C1q, C1r, C1s","C3, C4, C5","B, D, P","MASP-1, MASP-2"],"a":0,"why":"C1 = C1q + C1r + C1s."},{"q":"Ig that cannot activate complement:","opts":["IgM","IgG","IgA","IgG3"],"a":2,"why":"IgA وIgE ما إلن C1q receptor."},{"q":"C5 convertase of the alternative pathway is:","opts":["C4b2b","C3bBbC3b","C5b67","C9 polymer"],"a":1,"why":"C3bBbC3b."},{"q":"Properdin role:","opts":["Binds C1q","Stabilizes C3bBb","Cleaves C5","Blocks CD59"],"a":1,"why":"P بيثبّت C3bBb."},{"q":"C9 polymerization into a tube causes:","opts":["Opsonization","Osmotic lysis","Chemotaxis only","Histamine release"],"a":1,"why":"الماي بيدخل والخلية بتنفجر."},{"q":"Chemotactic complement fragments:","opts":["C1q and C2","C3a and C5a","C4bp and C1INH","MASP-1"],"a":1,"why":"C3a وC5a بيجذبو الخلايا."},{"q":"Immune complexes are cleared by:","opts":["CR1 on RBCs to liver and spleen","Kidneys only","Lymph nodes only","Skin only"],"a":0,"why":"بالـCR1 والكبد والطحال."},{"q":"Factor I function:","opts":["Cleaves C3b into iC3b, C3c, C3d","Binds mannose","Forms MAC","Activates IgA"],"a":0,"why":"Factor I بيقسم C3b."},{"q":"CD55 (DAF) inhibits:","opts":["C3 convertases","C9 polymerization","IgM binding","MBL"],"a":0,"why":"DAF بيسرّع تفكيك C3 convertases."},{"q":"C3 deficiency is associated with:","opts":["Frequent serious pyogenic infections","Hereditary edema","Autoimmune hemolysis only","Hyperthyroidism"],"a":0,"why":"التهابات قيحية متكررة."},{"q":"Lectin pathway activates C4 and C2 without:","opts":["C1","MBL","MASP","C3"],"a":0,"why":"بدون C1."}],"cards":[{"f":"Complement definition?","b":"Series of ~34 inactive blood proteins that help eliminate pathogens"},{"f":"Discovered in?","b":"1894 by Bordet"},{"f":"Thermolabile at?","b":"56°C for 30 min"},{"f":"Share of serum protein?","b":"About 10%"},{"f":"Most abundant component?","b":"C3"},{"f":"Main producer?","b":"Hepatocytes (mainly)"},{"f":"Pathways of complement?","b":"Classical, alternative, lectin (MBL)"},{"f":"Classical activator?","b":"Antigen-antibody complexes (IgM or IgG)"},{"f":"Alternative activator?","b":"Microbe surfaces, e.g., endotoxin (LPS)"},{"f":"Lectin activator?","b":"Mannose-binding lectin (MBL) binding microbial carbohydrates"},{"f":"C1 components?","b":"C1q, C1r, C1s"},{"f":"Ig that activates classical with one molecule?","b":"IgM"},{"f":"Ig that cannot activate complement?","b":"IgA and IgE (no C1q receptor)"},{"f":"C3 convertase in classical?","b":"C4b2b"},{"f":"C5 convertase in classical?","b":"C4b2bC3b"},{"f":"Alternative C3 convertase stabilized by?","b":"Properdin (P)"},{"f":"Alternative C5 convertase?","b":"C3bBbC3b"},{"f":"MBL associated proteases?","b":"MASP-1 and MASP-2"},{"f":"Membrane attack complex components?","b":"C5b with C6, C7, C8, and up to 19 C9"},{"f":"Anaphylatoxins?","b":"C3a, C4a, C5a"},{"f":"Chemotaxis by?","b":"C5a and C3a"},{"f":"Opsonins?","b":"C3b and C4b"},{"f":"Receptor for immune complex clearance?","b":"CR1 on RBCs"},{"f":"C1 inhibitor deficiency disease?","b":"Hereditary angioneurotic edema"},{"f":"Factor H function?","b":"Binds C3b and displaces Bb"},{"f":"CD59 function?","b":"Blocks C8-C9 formation"},{"f":"C2 and C4 deficiency?","b":"SLE-like disease in about 50% of patients"},{"f":"Factors B, D, P deficiency?","b":"Susceptibility to pyogenic infections"}],"subject":"micro","date":"2026-11-25"},
       {"id":"path-hemolytic-anemias","system":"Hematology","title":"Hemolytic Anemias (Lecture 3)","url":"path-hemolytic-anemias-3f.html","summary":"Hemolysis means red cell lifespan under 120 days; below about 20 days causes hemolytic anemia. Extravascular (spleen, liver, marrow) vs intravascular hemolysis. Inherited causes: membrane defects (hereditary spherocytosis, spectrin deficiency, autosomal dominant, small dense spherocytes, splenomegaly, jaundice) and enzyme defects (G6PD deficiency, X-linked recessive, oxidative stress from infection, drugs or fava beans, Heinz bodies and bite cells), and hemoglobin defects. Diagnosis by family history, blood film, reticulocytosis and specific tests.","points":["Hemolysis: red cell lifespan under 120 days; under 20 days gives hemolytic anemia","Extravascular hemolysis (spleen, liver, marrow) is common; intravascular is less common","Hereditary spherocytosis: membrane defect, mostly autosomal dominant, spectrin deficiency, small dense spherocytes without central pallor","Spherocytes are trapped by the spleen: anemia, jaundice, splenomegaly, reticulocytosis","G6PD deficiency: X-linked recessive, less NADPH and reduced glutathione, so red cells are damaged by oxidant stress","Triggers: infections, drugs, fava beans (favism) causing sudden intravascular hemolysis","Blood film in G6PD: Heinz bodies and bite cells","Inherited causes also include hemoglobin defects"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Hemolysis is defined as red cell life span below:","opts":["20 days","120 days","90 days","60 days"],"a":1,"why":"العمر الطبيعي 120 يوم."},{"q":"Which is more common?","opts":["Intravascular hemolysis","Equal","Neither","Extravascular hemolysis"],"a":3,"why":"خارج الأوعية أكتر شيوعاً."},{"q":"Extravascular hemolysis occurs in:","opts":["Kidney only","Brain","Spleen, liver, bone marrow RES","Blood plasma only"],"a":2,"why":"خلايا RES."},{"q":"Hemosiderinuria occurs in:","opts":["Intravascular hemolysis","Extravascular hemolysis only","Iron deficiency","Aplastic anemia"],"a":0,"why":"صبغة حديد بالبول."},{"q":"Jaundice in hemolysis is due to elevated:","opts":["Albumin","ALP only","Unconjugated bilirubin","Conjugated bilirubin"],"a":2,"why":"البيليروبين غير المقترن."},{"q":"G6PD deficiency is classified as:","opts":["Metabolic defect (enzymopathy)","Membrane defect","Hb synthesis defect","Immune"],"a":0,"why":"عيب إنزيمي."},{"q":"Which is an extrinsic cause?","opts":["Spherocytosis","G6PD deficiency","Hemoglobinopathy","Immune hemolytic anemia"],"a":3,"why":"السبب خارجي."},{"q":"Morphologic hallmark of HS:","opts":["Heinz body","Microspherocyte","Target cell","Bite cell"],"a":1,"why":"الكرية الكروية الصغيرة."},{"q":"Most common defect in HS:","opts":["G6PD deficiency","Intrinsic factor","Hemoglobin S","Spectrin deficiency"],"a":3,"why":"نقص السبيكترين."},{"q":"In HS, increased permeability leads to entry of:","opts":["Iron","Glucose","Na⁺ with water","K⁺ only"],"a":2,"why":"صوديوم وماي."},{"q":"After splenectomy in HS:","opts":["Anemia improves, spherocytes persist","Spherocytes disappear","Anemia worsens","Jaundice persists, anemia unchanged"],"a":0,"why":"الأنيميا بتتحسن والكروية بتضل."},{"q":"Which test shows spherocyte fragility in hypotonic salt?","opts":["Enzyme assay","Fluorescence test","Osmotic fragility test","MRT"],"a":2,"why":"هشاشة الأسمزة."},{"q":"G6PD deficiency inheritance:","opts":["X-linked recessive","Autosomal dominant","Autosomal recessive","Mitochondrial"],"a":0,"why":"مرتبط بـX متنحي."},{"q":"G6PD converts NADP⁺ to:","opts":["NADH","ATP","FADH₂","NADPH"],"a":3,"why":"NADPH."},{"q":"Most frequently cited trigger food in G6PD:","opts":["Liver","Fava bean","Lentils","Spinach"],"a":1,"why":"الفول."}],"cards":[{"f":"Hemolysis?","b":"RBC life span &lt; 120 days"},{"f":"Anemia develops when?","b":"Life span &lt; 20 days"},{"f":"Intravascular hemolysis?","b":"Destruction in circulation"},{"f":"Extravascular hemolysis?","b":"Destruction by RES: spleen, liver, BM"},{"f":"More common?","b":"Extravascular"},{"f":"Extravascular features?","b":"Anemia, jaundice; splenectomy benefits"},{"f":"Intravascular features?","b":"Hb-emia, Hb-uria, hemosiderinuria, jaundice"},{"f":"Jaundice type?","b":"Unconjugated bilirubin ↑"},{"f":"Intrinsic defects?","b":"Membrane, enzyme, Hb synthesis"},{"f":"Extrinsic causes?","b":"Immune, mechanical, infection / toxins"},{"f":"HS inheritance?","b":"Autosomal dominant"},{"f":"HS hallmark?","b":"Microspherocyte"},{"f":"HS triad?","b":"Anemia, jaundice, splenomegaly"},{"f":"Commonest HS defect?","b":"Spectrin deficiency"},{"f":"HS mechanism?","b":"Permeability ↑ ← Na⁺ + water in ← sphere"},{"f":"Where spherocytes destroyed?","b":"Splenic cord macrophages"},{"f":"Splenectomy in HS?","b":"Anemia improves; spherocytes persist"},{"f":"Newborn HS symptom?","b":"Jaundice"},{"f":"HS specific tests?","b":"Osmotic fragility, flow cytometry, acidified glycerol lysis"},{"f":"HS treatment?","b":"Folic acid, medications, splenectomy"},{"f":"G6PD inheritance?","b":"X-linked recessive"},{"f":"G6PD role?","b":"NADP⁺ → NADPH → glutathione"},{"f":"Heinz bodies?","b":"Denatured Hb"},{"f":"Favism trigger?","b":"Fava bean"},{"f":"G6PD hematology?","b":"Heinz, bite, blister cells; retics ↑"},{"f":"G6PD tests?","b":"MRT, fluorescence, enzyme assay"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-26","no":3},
 {"id":"path-hematology-4","system":"Hematology","no":4,"title":"Immune and Mechanical Hemolytic Anemias (Lecture 4)","url":"path-immune-mechanical-hemolytic-4b.html","summary":"Immune hemolytic anemia (positive DAT): warm AIHA (IgG, 37°C, extravascular in the spleen), cold AIHA (IgM, below 30°C, intravascular), ABO and Rh hemolytic disease of the newborn, and mechanical (microangiopathic) hemolytic anemias.","points":["Immune hemolysis and classification (DAT positive)","Warm AIHA: IgG, 37°C, spleen","Cold and mixed AIHA: IgM, intravascular","Hemolytic disease of the newborn (ABO vs Rh)","Mechanical hemolytic anemias"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which antibody & temperature define warm AIHA?","opts":["IgM, <30°C","IgG, 37°C","IgA, 25°C","IgE, 37°C"],"a":1,"why":"Warm AIHA: IgG, max activity around 37°C."},{"q":"The defining character of all immune hemolytic anemia is:","opts":["Positive DAT (Coomb's)","Hemoglobinuria","Schistocytes","Low platelets"],"a":0,"why":"All IHA: positive direct antiglobulin test."},{"q":"Cold AIHA hemolysis is mainly:","opts":["Extravascular, spleen","Intravascular","Marrow only","None"],"a":1,"why":"Cold AIHA: IgM, intravascular hemolysis."},{"q":"Idiopathic percentage in warm AIHA:","opts":["10%","30%","50%","90%"],"a":1,"why":"Idiopathic in 30% of cases."},{"q":"Drug linked to warm AIHA in the lecture:","opts":["Methyldopa","Aspirin","Heparin","Insulin"],"a":0,"why":"Drugs: methyldopa."},{"q":"ABO HDN typically occurs in:","opts":["O baby, A mother","A or B baby, O mother","AB baby, A mother","Any, always severe"],"a":1,"why":"A and B babies born to O mothers. Mild."},{"q":"Rh HDN: first baby is usually:","opts":["Severely affected","Not affected","Stillborn","Hydrops"],"a":1,"why":"First born not affected. Mother sensitized at delivery."},{"q":"Rh prevention schedule:","opts":["Anti-D at 28 weeks + delivery","Anti-D after 2nd baby only","Steroids at 28 weeks","Exchange transfusion at 28 weeks"],"a":0,"why":"Routine anti-D IgG at 28 weeks + first delivery."},{"q":"Kernicterus means:","opts":["Severe jaundice ← neurological defects","Heart valve damage","Mild ABO HDN","Cold agglutinin"],"a":0,"why":"Severe neonatal jaundice with severe neurological defects."},{"q":"MAHA is characterized by:","opts":["Thrombocytosis","Thrombocytopenia + schistocytosis","Spherocytes only","Normal platelets"],"a":1,"why":"MAHA: thrombocytopenia + schistocytosis + intravascular signs."},{"q":"Which is NOT a cause of MAHA?","opts":["DIC","HUS/TTP","Vasculitis","Cold agglutinin"],"a":3,"why":"MAHA: DIC, platelet aggregate syndromes, vasculitis."},{"q":"Mixed AIHA initial treatment:","opts":["Corticosteroids + rituximab","Splenectomy only","Anti-D","Folic acid only"],"a":0,"why":"Initial management: corticosteroids + rituximab."}],"cards":[{"f":"Female, insidious months, jaundice + splenomegaly, spherocytes, DAT +. Antibody & temp?","b":"IgG, 37°C ← Warm AIHA. هدم extravascular بالطحال."},{"f":"Old patient, hands/feet cold-triggered hemolysis, DAT +. Antibody?","b":"IgM, reacts <30°C ← Cold AIHA. هدم intravascular."},{"f":"Cold AIHA secondary causes?","b":"Idiopathic, Mycoplasma infection, lymphoma."},{"f":"Warm AIHA idiopathic %?","b":"30%."},{"f":"Warm AIHA secondary causes?","b":"CLL, HD, NHL, SLE, RA, URTI, ovarian ca, methyldopa."},{"f":"Defining test of ALL immune hemolysis?","b":"DAT (Coomb's test) positive."},{"f":"Warm AIHA needs blood, what problem?","b":"No compatible blood. Choose least incompatible unit from panel."},{"f":"Rare: both IgG + IgM destroy RBC. Name + first treatment?","b":"Mixed AIHA. Corticosteroids + rituximab."},{"f":"A or B baby, O mother, mild jaundice. Dx?","b":"ABO HDN. Mild, no treatment, rarely exchange transfusion. 1st pregnancy can be affected."},{"f":"Rh HDN, which baby affected?","b":"Second baby onward. First baby spared: mother sensitized at delivery ← anti-D."}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-26"},
 {"id":"script-hematology-1","system":"Hematology","no":1,"title":"Hematology · Script 1 (Lecture 1)","url":"path-script-hemolytic-1b.html","summary":"Script and Cheat Code for hemolytic anemias: definition (RBC lifespan under 120 days, anemia under 20), extravascular vs intravascular hemolysis (hemoglobinemia, hemoglobinuria, hemosiderinuria), classification (intrinsic vs extrinsic), hereditary spherocytosis (membrane skeleton defect, spectrin, splenectomy) and G6PD deficiency (NADPH, glutathione, Heinz, bite and blister cells, favism). Includes high yields, extras and tap-to-reveal exam questions.","points":["Hemolysis: RBC lifespan under 120 days; anemia appears under 20 days","Extravascular (common): macrophages in spleen, anemia plus unconjugated jaundice; splenectomy helps","Intravascular: hemoglobinemia, then hemoglobinuria, then hemosiderinuria","Intrinsic: membrane, enzyme, hemoglobin defects; extrinsic: immune, mechanical, infection or toxins","HS: autosomal dominant, spectrin, microspherocytes, no central pallor, osmotic fragility test","After splenectomy in HS anemia improves but spherocytes remain","G6PD: X-linked recessive; low NADPH, low reduced glutathione, Hb oxidation, Heinz bodies","G6PD smear: Heinz bodies, bite cells, blister cells; trigger fava beans (favism)","G6PD diagnosis: MetHb reduction test or enzyme assay, repeat after the acute attack"],"mcqs":[{"q":"A child has anemia, jaundice and splenomegaly; the smear shows small dense cells without central pallor. Diagnosis?","opts":["Hereditary spherocytosis","G6PD deficiency","Iron deficiency anemia","Aplastic anemia"],"a":0,"why":"Weak membrane skeleton makes the cell spherical (microspherocyte) and the spleen traps it: extravascular hemolysis."},{"q":"After splenectomy in hereditary spherocytosis, what happens?","opts":["Anemia improves and spherocytes remain","Spherocytes disappear","Anemia worsens","Hemoglobinuria appears"],"a":0,"why":"The destruction site is removed, but the membrane defect is not corrected."},{"q":"Which finding points to intravascular hemolysis?","opts":["Hemoglobinuria","Splenomegaly only","Many spherocytes","High haptoglobin"],"a":0,"why":"Free Hb in plasma is filtered by the kidney; haptoglobin falls; hemosiderinuria follows."},{"q":"Which test is the classic specific test for hereditary spherocytosis?","opts":["Osmotic fragility test","MetHb reduction test","Direct Coombs","Heinz body stain"],"a":0,"why":"Spherical cells cannot swell, so they burst in hypotonic solution. EMA binding is the most accurate."},{"q":"Inheritance of G6PD deficiency?","opts":["X-linked recessive","Autosomal dominant","Autosomal recessive","Mitochondrial"],"a":0,"why":"Males are more often affected; carrier females can show disease by lyonization."},{"q":"Which smear finding is the earliest sign of oxidative membrane damage in G6PD deficiency?","opts":["Blister cells","Target cells","Spherocytes","Schistocytes"],"a":0,"why":"Blister cells appear first; bite cells form when the spleen removes Heinz bodies."},{"q":"Why can a G6PD test be falsely normal during an acute attack?","opts":["Old deficient cells were destroyed and young reticulocytes have normal enzyme","The enzyme is raised in hemolysis","Heinz bodies hide the enzyme","The test needs fasting"],"a":0,"why":"Repeat the test after a few weeks."},{"q":"A known HS patient suddenly becomes very pale with low reticulocytes. Cause?","opts":["Parvovirus B19 aplastic crisis","Gallstones","Favism","Splenic infarct"],"a":0,"why":"Parvovirus B19 stops the marrow, so compensation stops."},{"q":"Which stain shows Heinz bodies?","opts":["Supravital stain (crystal violet)","Wright stain","Gram stain","PAS"],"a":0,"why":"Heinz bodies are invisible with routine Wright stain."}],"cards":[{"f":"أنيميا + يرقان + طحال كبير، وبالدم خلايا صغيرة غامقة بدون منطقة شاحبة بالنص؟","b":"Hereditary spherocytosis (HS)، لأن هيكل الغشاء ضعيف فالخلية بتصير كروية (Microspherocyte) وبتنحبس بالطحال."},{"f":"مولود جديد عنده يرقان وبالعيلة نفس المرض؟","b":"HS، لأن عند المولود اليرقان هو العَرَض الأشهر، مش الأنيميا."},{"f":"مريض HS بعد ما شالوا طحاله، شو بيتحسن وشو بيضل؟","b":"الأنيميا (الهدم) بتتحسن، بس الـ spherocytes بتضل موجودة."},{"f":"بعد أكل فول: بول أحمر + ألم ظهر + شحوب سريع + يرقان؟","b":"Favism = Acute intravascular hemolysis (hemolytic crisis) بسبب G6PD deficiency."},{"f":"ذكر عنده هدم والوراثة مرتبطة بـ X؟","b":"G6PD deficiency (X-linked recessive، فالذكور أكتر إصابة)."},{"f":"وين بيصير الـ extravascular hemolysis وشو العلاج اللي بيفيد؟","b":"بخلايا الـ RES (طحال، كبد، نخاع)، ومعظمه بالطحال، فـ Splenectomy بتفيد."},{"f":"أي نوع هدم أشيع؟","b":"Extravascular. الـ intravascular أقل شيوعاً."},{"f":"شو علامات الـ intravascular hemolysis؟","b":"Anemia + Hemoglobinemia + Hemoglobinuria + Hemosiderinuria + jaundice (unconjugated bilirubin)."},{"f":"شو علامات الـ extravascular hemolysis؟","b":"Anemia + jaundice (unconjugated bilirubin)."},{"f":"أي نوع bilirubin بيرتفع بالهدم؟","b":"Unconjugated (indirect) bilirubin."},{"f":"إمتى بتظهر الأنيميا بالهدم؟","b":"لما عمر الـ RBC يصير أقل من 20 يوم (الطبيعي 120 يوم)."},{"f":"كيف بتنتقل HS بالوراثة؟","b":"Autosomal dominant بالأغلب، شوية recessive، وبعضها new mutation."},{"f":"أشهر بروتين ناقص بالـ HS؟","b":"Spectrin."},{"f":"ليش الخلية بتصير كروية؟","b":"نقص بروتينات الغشاء بيزيد النفاذية، فبيدخل Na ومعه ماء، فالخلية بتتورّم وبتصير كروية."},{"f":"ليش الطحال بيهدم الـ spherocytes؟","b":"لأنها ما بتقدر تطلع من الـ splenic cord (شكلها كروي ومرونتها قليلة)، فبتنحبس وبتبلعها الـ macrophages."},{"f":"شو بيطلع بفحص الدم بالـ HS؟","b":"Normochromic normocytic anemia + reticulocytosis + spherocytes."},{"f":"شو الفحوصات الخاصة لتشخيص الـ HS؟","b":"Osmotic fragility test + Flow cytometric analysis + Acidified glycerol lysis test."},{"f":"ليش فحص الـ osmotic fragility بيطلع إيجابي؟","b":"لأن الـ spherocytes بالمحلول ناقص التوتر (hypotonic) بيدخلها ماء وما عندها مساحة تتمدد."},{"f":"شو خيارات علاج الـ HS؟","b":"Folic acid (لنضج الـ RBC) + أدوية لتخفيف نشاط الطحال + Splenectomy للحالات الشديدة أو لما العلاجات الثانية ما بتكفي."},{"f":"كيف شدة الـ HS؟","b":"من خفيفة لشديدة، وأغلب المرضى moderate. الشديدة بتظهر بالطفولة المبكرة، والخفيفة ممكن ما تنكشف إلا بالكبر."},{"f":"شو بيعمل إنزيم الـ G6PD؟","b":"من الـ pentose pathway، بيحوّل NADP+ إلى NADPH."},{"f":"ليش الـ NADPH مهم؟","b":"بيحافظ على الـ glutathione بشكله المرجَع (reduced) اللي بيعادل المؤكسدات."},{"f":"السلسلة كلها بجملة وحدة؟","b":"G6PD ناقص ← NADPH ناقص ← glutathione مرجَع ناقص ← oxidative stress بيعمل denature للـ Hb ← Heinz bodies ← Intravascular hemolysis."},{"f":"شو اسم الـ Hb المتغيّر اللي بنشوفه بالدم؟","b":"Heinz bodies."},{"f":"شو المحفّزات اللي بتسبب الهدم؟","b":"Oxidant stress: عدوى، أدوية، أكل معيّن (أشهره الفول)."},{"f":"ليش الفول بيسبب هدم؟","b":"لأنه بيولّد oxidants لما بيتمثّل."},{"f":"كيف بتظهر نوبة الـ Favism؟","b":"ألم بطن + قشعريرة (rigors) + ألم ظهر + تقيؤ + شحوب سريع + بول أحمر (Hb-uria) + يرقان، وممكن shock وفشل كلوي (renal failure)."},{"f":"كيف بتظهر عند المولود؟","b":"Neonatal jaundice."},{"f":"شو العرض النادر؟","b":"Chronic hemolytic anemia."},{"f":"شو بيبين بالدم بالـ G6PD؟","b":"Normochromic normocytic anemia + Heinz bodies + Bite cells + Blister cells (أول علامة لأذى الغشاء بالأكسدة) + marked reticulocytosis + hemoglobinemia + Hb-uria + indirect hyperbilirubinemia."},{"f":"شو الفحوصات لتشخيص الـ G6PD؟","b":"Screening: MetHb reduction test (MRT) أو Fluorescence test، وبعدين Enzyme assay."},{"f":"أي نوع هدم بالـ G6PD؟","b":"Intravascular hemolysis."},{"f":"قديش انتشار نقص الـ G6PD؟","b":"أشهر نقص إنزيم بالـ RBC، لحد 400 مليون شخص بالعالم."},{"f":"HS مقابل G6PD: الوراثة / العيب / نوع الهدم / شكل الدم؟","b":"- HS: Autosomal dominant، عيب بروتينات الغشاء (Spectrin)، الهدم بالطحال (extravascular)، Microspherocytes. • G6PD: X-linked recessive، عيب إنزيم (NADPH)، Intravascular hemolysis، Heinz bodies + Bite cells + Blister cells."}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-26","kind":"script"},
 {"id":"script-hematology-2","system":"Hematology","kind":"script","no":2,"title":"Hematology · Script 2 (Lecture 2)","url":"path-script-hemolytic-2.html","summary":"Script and Cheat Code for immune and mechanical hemolytic anemias: DAT/Coombs, warm vs cold vs mixed AIHA, ABO and Rh hemolytic disease of the newborn (anti-D prophylaxis), and mechanical anemias (schistocytes, MAHA).","points":["Immune hemolysis and classification","Warm AIHA: IgG, 37°C","Cold and mixed AIHA","Hemolytic disease of the newborn","Mechanical anemias and MAHA"],"mcqs":[{"q":"What test is positive in ALL immune hemolytic anemias?","opts":["Osmotic fragility","DAT (Coombs)","MetHb reduction","Heinz body stain"],"a":1,"why":"All IHA: positive DAT = Coombs test."},{"q":"Warm AIHA: antibody and temperature?","opts":["IgM, below 30°C","IgG, 37°C","IgA, 25°C","IgE, 37°C"],"a":1,"why":"Warm AIHA is IgG, maximal at 37°C, extravascular in the spleen."},{"q":"Cold AIHA hemolysis is mainly:","opts":["Extravascular","Intravascular","Marrow only","None"],"a":1,"why":"Cold AIHA: IgM below 30°C, intravascular."},{"q":"Which drug is a known cause of warm AIHA?","opts":["Methyldopa","Aspirin","Warfarin","Insulin"],"a":0,"why":"Methyldopa is listed among the causes of warm AIHA."},{"q":"Best approach to transfusion in warm AIHA:","opts":["Any group-matched unit","Choose the least incompatible unit","Never transfuse","Use O negative only"],"a":1,"why":"Fully compatible blood is almost impossible, so the least incompatible unit is chosen."},{"q":"ABO HDN typically occurs when the baby is ___ and the mother is ___:","opts":["O / A","A or B / O","AB / O","O / B"],"a":1,"why":"Baby A or B, mother O. Usually mild; main problem is jaundice."},{"q":"Why is the first baby usually spared in Rh HDN?","opts":["Mother already has anti-D","Fetal cells enter the mother's blood at delivery, so sensitization happens after","Placenta blocks IgG","Baby is Rh negative"],"a":1,"why":"Sensitization happens at delivery, so later pregnancies are affected."},{"q":"Anti-D IgG prophylaxis is given to D-negative mothers at:","opts":["Week 12 only","Week 28 and at delivery of a D-positive baby","Only after stillbirth","Never"],"a":1,"why":"Given at week 28 and at delivery (or termination) of a D-positive baby."},{"q":"Hallmark of mechanical hemolytic anemia:","opts":["Spherocytes","Heinz bodies","Schistocytes","Target cells"],"a":2,"why":"Schistocytes with intravascular hemolysis; MAHA adds thrombocytopenia."}],"cards":[{"f":"شو الفحص اللي بيجمع كل الـ IHA؟","b":"DAT = Coombs test إيجابي."},{"f":"شو يعني immune hemolysis؟","b":"الـ RBC بتنهدم بسبب تفاعل antigen-antibody."},{"f":"وين بيصير الهدم؟","b":"Intravascular و extravascular سوا."},{"f":"كيف منقسم الـ IHA؟","b":"Autoimmune (warm و cold) + Alloimmune (HDN و transfusion reaction) + Drug-induced."},{"f":"شو الفرق بين autoimmune و alloimmune؟","b":"Autoimmune: الأجسام المضادة ضد RBC الشخص نفسه. Alloimmune: ضد شي مش من الجسم."},{"f":"قديش عدد الأدوية المشتبه فيها؟","b":"أكتر من 130."},{"f":"شو نوع الـ antibody وحرارته؟","b":"IgG عند 37°C."},{"f":"شو نوع الهدم ووينو؟","b":"Extravascular بالطحال."},{"f":"مين بيصاب؟","b":"كل الأعمار، والبنات أكتر."},{"f":"كيف بتبلّش الأعراض؟","b":"شوي شوي على مدى شهور (insidious)."},{"f":"شو الأعراض؟","b":"يرقان + أنيميا + splenomegaly."},{"f":"شو بيبين بالدم؟","b":"Normochromic normocytic + spherocytosis + normoblastaemia + reticulocytosis واضحة."},{"f":"قديش نسبة الـ idiopathic؟","b":"حوالي 30%."},{"f":"شو الأسباب الثانوية؟","b":"CLL و HD و NHL + SLE و RA + عدوى تنفسية + سرطان المبيض + methyldopa."},{"f":"كيف منشخّص؟","b":"سريرياً + شكل الـ RBC + Direct Coombs إيجابي."},{"f":"ليش نقل الدم مشكلة؟","b":"شبه مستحيل نلاقي دم متوافق، فبنختار الوحدة الأقل عدم توافق."},{"f":"شو نوع الـ antibody وحرارته؟","b":"IgM تحت 30°C."},{"f":"شو نوع الهدم؟","b":"Intravascular."},{"f":"مين بيصاب؟","b":"الكبار بالعمر."},{"f":"شو الأسباب؟","b":"Idiopathic أو mycoplasma أو lymphoma."},{"f":"بشو بيتكشف؟","b":"DCT."},{"f":"مقارنة warm و cold؟","b":"- Warm: IgG، 37°C، extravascular (طحال). • Cold: IgM، تحت 30°C، intravascular."},{"f":"شو هو؟","b":"نادر، فيه أجسام مضادة warm و cold سوا."},{"f":"شو العلاج الأولي؟","b":"Corticosteroids + rituximab."},{"f":"كيف بيصير؟","b":"IgG الأم بيعدّي المشيمة وبيهدم RBC الجنين."},{"f":"أي فصائل بتعمل ABO HDN؟","b":"طفل A أو B وأم O."},{"f":"شو شدته والمشكلة الأساسية؟","b":"خفيف، والمشكلة اليرقان، ونادراً بيحتاج exchange transfusion."},{"f":"الحمل الأول بيتأثر بالـ ABO؟","b":"إي ممكن. والخدّج أكتر تأثراً."},{"f":"شو السبب الأساسي لـ HDN؟","b":"Rh HDN (Erythroblastosis fetalis)."},{"f":"ليش البكر ما بيتأثر بالـ Rh؟","b":"لأن RBC الجنين بتعدّي لدم الأم وقت الولادة، فبتصنع anti-D وبيتأثر الطفل التاني."},{"f":"شو بيصير عند الطفل التاني؟","b":"أنيميا شديدة + يرقان شديد + ممكن kernicterus إلا إذا exchange transfusion بسرعة."},{"f":"شو بيصير بالولادات اللي بعدها؟","b":"Stillbirth + hydrops fetalis (شحوب + oedema + يرقان + بطن منتفخ + مشيمة كبيرة)."},{"f":"قديش نسبة الأمهات اللي بتتأثر؟","b":"حوالي 30%."},{"f":"شو بيعمل عدم توافق ABO؟","b":"بيقلل التحسس."},{"f":"شو بيبين بالدم؟","b":"أنيميا + reticulocytosis + normoblastaemia."},{"f":"كيف منمنعه؟","b":"Anti-D IgG للأم D-negative بالأسبوع 28 ووقت الولادة الأولى (أو إنهاء الحمل)."},{"f":"كيف بيشتغل الـ anti-D؟","b":"بيشيل RBC الجنين من دم الأم، فما بتتحسس."},{"f":"شو العلامة المميزة؟","b":"Schistocytes + intravascular hemolysis."},{"f":"شو السبب القلبي؟","b":"صمّامات أو رقع صناعية، لأن الدم بيجري بشكل مضطرب (turbulent)."},{"f":"شو هو الـ MAHA؟","b":"Microangiopathic hemolytic anaemia: الـ RBC بتتدمر بالأوعية الصغيرة."},{"f":"شو أسباب الـ MAHA؟","b":"DIC + HUS و TTP + Vasculitis."},{"f":"شو الزيادة بالـ MAHA؟","b":"Thrombocytopenia + hemoglobinuria + hemosiderinuria."},{"f":"مقارنة Warm و Cold و Mechanical؟","b":"- Warm: IgG، 37°C، extravascular، spherocytes، Coombs +. • Cold: IgM، تحت 30°C، intravascular، Coombs +. • Mechanical: مش مناعي، Schistocytes، intravascular."}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-26"},
 {"id": "script-micro-bacteria-2", "system": "Bacteria", "kind": "script", "no": 2, "title": "Bacteria · Script 2 (Lecture 2)", "url": "micro-script-strep-2g.html", "summary": "Script and Cheat Code for Genus Streptococcus: hemolysis and Lancefield, S. pyogenes, S. agalactiae, S. pneumoniae, Viridans, Enterococci, with high yields and a comparison table.", "points": ["بيتا/ألفا/غاما + Lancefield A B C F G", "M protein أهم ضراوة للـ pyogenes", "ASO عالي = rheumatic fever", "GBS: CAMP + وHippurate +", "Pneumoniae: capsule وOptochin", "Viridans = subacute endocarditis", "Enterococci = nosocomial UTI"], "mcqs": [{"q": "أهم عامل ضراوة للـ S. pyogenes؟", "opts": ["Hyaluronidase", "M protein", "DNase", "Streptokinase"], "a": 1, "why": "بروتين M بيمنع البلعمة (المسار البديل للمتممة)."}, {"q": "سلبي CAMP وحساس للباسيتراسين، PYR إيجابي:", "opts": ["S. agalactiae", "S. pneumoniae", "S. pyogenes", "Enterococcus"], "a": 2, "why": "هيدي صفات Group A."}, {"q": "ASO عالي بيدل على:", "opts": ["مناعة واقية", "Acute rheumatic fever", "Impetigo فقط", "Scarlet fever فقط"], "a": 1, "why": "ASO ضد SLO، مش ضد M، فما بيعني مناعة."}, {"q": "مولود جديد: sepsis خلال 24 ساعة، CAMP إيجابي:", "opts": ["S. pyogenes", "Viridans", "S. agalactiae", "S. pneumoniae"], "a": 2, "why": "Group B: hippurate + وCAMP +."}, {"q": "كروية رمحية بثنائيات، حساسة للأوبتوكين وبتذوب بالصفراء:", "opts": ["Viridans", "S. pneumoniae", "Enterococcus", "S. bovis"], "a": 1, "why": "Quellung إيجابي والمحفظة أهم ضراوة."}, {"q": "أكتر مسبب لـ subacute bacterial endocarditis:", "opts": ["Viridans streptococci", "S. pyogenes", "Enterococcus", "S. pneumoniae"], "a": 0, "why": "بتوصل من الفم لصمام متضرر بالحمى الرثوية."}, {"q": "أكتر مسبب لعدوى المستشفيات بالـ ICU، PYR + و6.5% NaCl +:", "opts": ["Viridans", "Enterococcus", "Group B", "S. pyogenes"], "a": 1, "why": "E. faecalis الأشهر، وE. faecium = VRE."}, {"q": "مقاومة للأوبتوكين وما بتذوب بالصفراء ولانسفيلد سلبي:", "opts": ["S. pneumoniae", "S. pyogenes", "Viridans", "Group B"], "a": 2, "why": "هيدي بصمة Viridans."}, {"q": "أول علاج لالتهاب الحلق العقدي:", "opts": ["Vancomycin", "Penicillin V أو Amoxicillin", "Clindamycin وحده", "Tetracycline"], "a": 1, "why": "وعند حساسية: Cephalosporins أو Macrolides."}], "cards": [{"f": "سيدة بعد الولادة معها حرارة والتهاب بالرحم (endometritis).", "b": "S. pyogenes (Puerperal fever)."}, {"f": "مريض بالـ ICU عندو urinary catheter وطلعلو UTI، والبكتيريا PYR positive وبتنمو بـ 6.5% NaCl.", "b": "Enterococcus."}, {"f": "سيدة عمرها 70، بعد cardiac surgery، حرارة و chills، Gram-positive coccus بالدم، مقاوم للـ penicillin.", "b": "Enterococcus species."}, {"f": "مولود عمرو أقل من 24 ساعة، أمو كان عندها prolonged rupture of membranes، عندو sepsis.", "b": "S. agalactiae (Group B)."}, {"f": "Gram-positive cocci، β-hemolytic، bacitracin resistant، hippurate positive، CAMP positive.", "b": "S. agalactiae."}, {"f": "Gram-positive lancet diplococci، α-hemolytic، optochin sensitive، bile soluble.", "b": "S. pneumoniae."}, {"f": "مريض عندو fever و pleural pain و rusty sputum.", "b": "S. pneumoniae (pneumonia)."}, {"f": "Gram-positive cocci، α-hemolytic، optochin resistant، bile insoluble، ما عندها Lancefield antigen.", "b": "Viridans streptococci."}, {"f": "مريض عندو rheumatic valve disease، وبعد شغل أسنان صار معو subacute endocarditis.", "b": "Viridans streptococci."}, {"f": "طفل عندو vesicles انفجرو وصارو crusted على جلد فيه eczema، ومعدي كتير.", "b": "Impetigo (streptococcal pyoderma) من S. pyogenes."}, {"f": "Rash أحمر منتشر من upper chest، وبعد 5 لـ 7 أيام desquamation.", "b": "Scarlet fever من Erythrogenic toxin."}, {"f": "Lesion أحمر كتير بحدّ واضح بس مش مستقيم عند مريض كبير بالسن.", "b": "Erysipelas."}, {"f": "Lesion flat وحدودو مش واضحة وانتشر بسرعة.", "b": "Cellulitis من Hyaluronidase."}, {"f": "بعد minor trauma صار عند المريض shock و multiorgan failure و necrotizing fasciitis (M1).", "b": "Streptococcal TSS."}, {"f": "طفل عمرو 8 سنين، بعد 3 أسابيع من skin infection عندو hematuria و hypertension و low complement.", "b": "Acute glomerulonephritis."}, {"f": "طفل عمرو 10 سنين، بعد أسبوعين من sore throat، عندو fever و polyarthritis و carditis.", "b": "Rheumatic fever، والـ ASO عالي."}, {"f": "ليش الـ M protein بيخلّي البكتيريا تهرب من الـ phagocytosis؟", "b": "لأنو بيوقّف الـ alternate complement pathway."}, {"f": "ليش ممكن الواحد ينصاب بـ S. pyogenes أكتر من مرة؟", "b": "لأنو المناعة type-specific، وفي أكتر من 150 M type."}, {"f": "ليش الـ rheumatic fever بتضرب القلب؟", "b": "لأنو antigenic mimicry: M protein يشبه عضلة القلب."}, {"f": "ليش الـ ASO ما بيحمّي مع إنو بيرتفع؟", "b": "لأنو ضد Streptolysin O، مش ضد M protein."}, {"f": "ليش الـ chemoprophylaxis مفيدة بالـ rheumatic fever مش بالـ nephritis؟", "b": "لأنو الـ carditis بيرجع يتنشّط مع كل infection، والـ nephritis ما بيرجع."}, {"f": "ليش منعطي Clindamycin مع Penicillin بالـ severe infections؟", "b": "لأنو بيمنع protein synthesis، فبيقلّل الـ toxins."}, {"f": "ليش Hyaluronidase اسمو spreading factor؟", "b": "لأنو بيكسّر hyaluronic acid، فالبكتيريا بتنتشر بسرعة بالجلد."}, {"f": "ليش مش كل S. pyogenes بيعمل Erythrogenic toxin؟", "b": "لأنو الجين بيجي من bacteriophage (lysogenized strains)."}, {"f": "ليش الـ superantigen خطير؟", "b": "لأنو بينشّط T cells بشكل كبير، فبيتحرّر كتير cytokines."}, {"f": "ليش SLO ما بيكسّر الـ RBC على سطح الـ agar؟", "b": "لأنو oxygen-labile، بيشتغل بس تحت السطح."}, {"f": "ليش مستعمرات Group B لزجة؟", "b": "بسبب الـ capsule."}, {"f": "ليش الـ Quellung reaction بتبيّن الـ capsule منتفخة؟", "b": "لأنو الـ type-specific antisera بتلتصق بالـ capsule."}, {"f": "ليش الـ Penicillin هو الـ drug of choice لـ S. pneumoniae؟", "b": "لأنو بيمنع بناء peptidoglycan، فالجدار بيضعف والبكتيريا بتموت."}, {"f": "ليش الـ Enterococci خطيرين بالـ ICU؟", "b": "بسبب catheters و antibiotics لوقت طويل، و biofilm، و resistance."}, {"f": "ليش الـ Viridans بتعمل endocarditis على valve متضررة بس؟", "b": "لأنها low virulence، بتلتصق وبتتكاثر بس على valve متضررة (من rheumatic fever)."}, {"f": "Erysipelas مقابل Cellulitis؟", "b": "Erysipelas: أحمر كتير، حدّ واضح. Cellulitis: flat، حدود مش واضحة."}, {"f": "SLO مقابل SLS؟", "b": "SLO: oxygen-labile، antigenic (ASO)، تحت السطح. SLS: oxygen-stable، non-antigenic، على السطح."}, {"f": "Rheumatic fever مقابل Acute glomerulonephritis؟", "b": "RF: بعد respiratory infection، 5 لـ 15 سنة، بيرجع مع كل infection. AGN: بعد skin infection، 5 لـ 12 سنة، ما بيرجع، low complement."}, {"f": "Pneumococcus مقابل Viridans؟", "b": "Pneumococcus: optochin sensitive، bile soluble، capsule، Quellung positive. Viridans: optochin resistant، bile insoluble، ما في capsule."}, {"f": "S. pyogenes مقابل S. agalactiae؟", "b": "Pyogenes: Group A، bacitracin sensitive، PYR positive، CAMP negative. Agalactiae: Group B، bacitracin resistant، hippurate positive، CAMP positive."}, {"f": "E. faecalis مقابل E. faecium؟", "b": "E. faecalis: الأكتر شيوعاً. E. faecium: أقل بس مقاوم كتير (VRE)."}, {"f": "شو الـ tests لتعريف S. pyogenes؟", "b": "PYR positive، bacitracin sensitive، Group A antigen، و ASO."}, {"f": "ASO كام بيدل على infection قبل؟ وكام دليل قوي؟", "b": "أكتر من 200 infection قبل. أكتر من 300 دليل قوي."}, {"f": "ASO عالي بيدل على شو؟ وإذا low أو moderate؟", "b": "High: acute rheumatic fever. Low أو moderate: post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis."}, {"f": "شو الـ definitive identification لـ Group B؟", "b": "منستخرج الـ group antigen، وبيصير agglutination مع anti-group B antisera."}, {"f": "شو الـ CAMP test؟", "b": "CAMP factor (من Group B) مع staphylococcal beta lysin، بيطلع arrowhead من hemolysis."}, {"f": "شو الـ specimens لتشخيص S. pneumoniae؟", "b": "Sputum، lung aspirate، pleural fluid، CSF."}, {"f": "شو أهم virulence factor لـ S. pneumoniae؟", "b": "Polysaccharide capsule."}, {"f": "علاج pharyngitis بـ S. pyogenes؟ وإذا في allergy؟", "b": "Penicillin V أو Amoxicillin. إذا allergy: Cephalosporins أو Macrolides."}, {"f": "علاج الـ severe infection بـ S. pyogenes؟", "b": "IV Penicillin + Clindamycin."}, {"f": "بدائل Penicillin لـ S. pneumoniae؟", "b": "Erythromycin، tetracycline، Vancomycin، 3rd generation cephalosporins."}, {"f": "شو معايير تشخيص Enterococci؟", "b": "Bile esculin positive، PYR positive، growth at 6.5% NaCl، growth at 10 to 45°C."}, {"f": "شو أنواع مقاومة Enterococci؟", "b": "Cephalosporins (intrinsic)، aminoglycoside، vancomycin، β-lactam، TMP-SMZ."}, {"f": "كيف منمنع انتشار VRE؟", "b": "Hand hygiene، sterilization، تقليل catheters، isolation، infection control."}, {"f": "عندك 5 بكتيريا كلها Gram-positive cocci. كيف منفرّقهن؟", "b": "- β-hemolytic + bacitracin sensitive + PYR positive: S. pyogenes • - β-hemolytic + bacitracin resistant + hippurate positive + CAMP positive: S. agalactiae • - α-hemolytic + optochin sensitive + bile soluble: S. pneumoniae • - α-hemolytic + optochin resistant + bile insoluble: Viridans • - PYR positive + bile esculin positive + 6.5% NaCl: Enterococcus"}], "subject": "micro", "date": "2026-11-26"},
 {"id": "script-pharm-autocoid-3", "system": "CNS", "kind": "script", "no": 8, "title": "CNS · Script 8 (Narcotic Analgesics)", "url": "pharm-script-autocoid-3d.html", "summary": "Script and Cheat Code for Narcotic (Opioid) Analgesics: pain, classification, pharmacokinetics, receptors, morphine actions, uses, interactions, tramadol, tapentadol, antagonists, with high yields.", "points": ["Tolerance vs Dependence vs Addiction", "µ: respiratory depression · κ: sedation · δ: tolerance", "Fentanyl أقوى من morphine بـ 100 مرة", "Meperidine → normeperidine seizures", "Codeine → morphine بالـ CYP2D6", "Naloxone 1-2h · Nalmefene 8-12h · Naltrexone 48h", "Methylnaltrexone للـ opioid constipation"], "mcqs": [{"q": "مريض بدو دوا بـ patch على الجلد بيعطي analgesia لحد 72 ساعة. أي دوا؟", "opts": ["Hydromorphone", "Morphine", "Fentanyl", "Buprenorphine"], "a": 2, "why": "Fentanyl بيجي كـ transdermal patch وبيعطي analgesia لحد 72 h."}, {"q": "0.1 mg من أي دوا بتعطي نفس الـ analgesia تبع 10 mg morphine؟", "opts": ["Hydromorphone", "Methadone", "Oxymorphone", "Fentanyl"], "a": 3, "why": "Fentanyl أقوى من morphine مية مرة بالـ potency."}, {"q": "تصنيف الـ opioids لـ strong و moderate و weak agonists هو بالأساس حسب؟", "opts": ["الـ Potency", "Strength of analgesia وهو مستقل عن الـ potency", "الـ Route of administration", "الـ Duration of action"], "a": 1, "why": "التصنيف مش مرتبط بالـ potency، والـ strong agonists بيختلفوا كتير بالـ potency."}, {"q": "دوا بيعطي analgesia أقل من morphine حتى لو زدنا الـ dose. شو نوعو؟", "opts": ["Natural opiate", "Pure competitive antagonist", "Partial agonist", "Full agonist"], "a": 2, "why": "الـ Partial agonist بيفعّل الـ receptor لـ submaximal response بس."}, {"q": "أي زوج من الأدوية كلو partial agonists؟", "opts": ["Naloxone و Naltrexone", "Codeine و Hydrocodone", "Buprenorphine و Nalbuphine", "Fentanyl و Methadone"], "a": 1, "why": "الـ Partial agonists حسب المحاضرة: codeine و hydrocodone."}, {"q": "شو معنى Mixed agonist-antagonist؟", "opts": ["بيحجب كل الـ subtypes بشكل competitive", "بيفعّل الـ receptor لـ submaximal response بس", "بيفعّل subtype وبيحجب subtype تاني", "بيفعّل كل الـ subtypes وما بيحجب ولا واحد"], "a": 2, "why": "الخيار التاني تعريف الـ full agonist، والتالت تعريف الـ pure antagonist، والرابع تعريف الـ partial agonist."}, {"q": "أي زوج هو pure antagonists؟", "opts": ["Nalbuphine و Naloxone", "Codeine و Naloxone", "Buprenorphine و Naltrexone", "Naloxone و Naltrexone"], "a": 3, "why": "Nalbuphine و buprenorphine هنن mixed agonist-antagonists."}, {"q": "أي opioid ما عندو extensive first-pass metabolism وبيجي كـ transdermal patch؟", "opts": ["Oxymorphone", "Fentanyl", "Hydromorphone", "Morphine"], "a": 1, "why": "الـ extensive first-pass هو لـ morphine و hydromorphone و oxymorphone."}, {"q": "إمرا حامل بتاخد opioids باستمرار. شو بيصير للـ neonate بعد الولادة؟", "opts": ["Serotonin syndrome", "Hyperpyrexic coma", "Withdrawal", "Neuroexcitation من M3G"], "a": 2, "why": "الـ opioids بتعبر الـ placenta وبيصير physical dependence مع exposure مستمر، فبيطلع withdrawal."}, {"q": "أي metabolite هو الـ primary metabolite تبع morphine وهو neuroexcitatory؟", "opts": ["Morphine-6-glucuronide", "Oxymorphone", "Normeperidine", "Morphine-3-glucuronide"], "a": 3, "why": "M6G active analgesic، أما M3G فهو الـ primary وneuroexcitatory."}, {"q": "أي metabolite عندو analgesic activity متل morphine؟", "opts": ["الـ glucuronide conjugates الـ inactive بشكل عام", "Morphine-6-glucuronide", "Morphine-3-glucuronide", "Normeperidine"], "a": 1, "why": "M6G active وبنفس قوة morphine."}, {"q": "مريض أخد codeine وما صار عندو analgesia. أفضل تفسير؟", "opts": ["Delta receptors عملوا tolerance من أول dose", "Extensive first-pass metabolism تبع codeine", "M3G بيعاكس الـ analgesia", "قليل تحويل لـ morphine بسبب CYP2D6 genotypic variability"], "a": 3, "why": "الـ codeine بيتحوّل لـ morphine بالـ CYP2D6 وهاد الـ enzyme عندو genotypic variability."}, {"q": "أي مجموعة كلها بتتحوّل لـ morphine بالـ CYP2D6؟", "opts": ["Meperidine و Codeine و Tramadol", "Hydromorphone و Oxymorphone و Morphine", "Codeine و Oxycodone و Hydrocodone", "Codeine و Fentanyl و Methadone"], "a": 2, "why": "المحاضرة: codeine و oxycodone و hydrocodone."}, {"q": "مريض أخد meperidine بـ plasma levels عالية وصار عندو seizures. المسؤول؟", "opts": ["Morphine-6-glucuronide", "Dextromethorphan", "Normeperidine", "Naloxone withdrawal"], "a": 2, "why": "الـ meperidine بيتحوّل لـ normeperidine وهاد بيعمل seizures عند تركيز عالي."}, {"q": "شو بيصير بالـ opioids عند مريض liver disease؟", "opts": ["الـ half-life بيقصر", "بيزيد الـ first-pass بالـ intestine بس", "الـ kidney بتعوّض وما بيتغير شي", "الـ elimination half-life بيطول"], "a": 3, "why": "الـ hepatic enzymes هنن اللي بيعملوا metabolism للـ opioids."}, {"q": "مريض شرب alcohol وطلع عندو peak serum level عالي كتير لـ opioid. أي opioid من هدول؟", "opts": ["Hydromorphone", "Morphine", "Fentanyl", "Codeine"], "a": 0, "why": "الـ alcohol بيرفع الـ peak levels تبع hydromorphone و oxymorphone."}, {"q": "أي ترتيب صحيح بالـ duration من الأقصر للأطول؟", "opts": ["Fentanyl (1-2 h) ثم Buprenorphine (6-8 h) ثم long-acting formulations (24 h أو أكتر)", "Fentanyl و Buprenorphine نفس الـ duration", "Buprenorphine (6-8 h) ثم Fentanyl (1-2 h) ثم long-acting", "Long-acting ثم Buprenorphine ثم Fentanyl"], "a": 0, "why": "fentanyl و sufentanil 1-2 h، و buprenorphine 6-8 h، والـ long-acting 24 h أو أكتر."}, {"q": "ليش Remifentanil و Alfentanil half-life تبعهن قصير كتير؟", "opts": ["لأنو بيتحوّلوا لـ morphine", "لأنو بيتكسروا بسرعة", "لأنو عندن extensive first-pass", "لأنو ما بيعبروا الـ BBB"], "a": 1, "why": "هنن congeners تبع fentanyl وبيتكسروا بسرعة، فالـ half-life دقائق لعشرات الدقايق."}, {"q": "أي receptor subtype مسؤول بالتحديد عن الـ respiratory depression؟", "opts": ["delta", "mu2", "kappa", "mu1"], "a": 1, "why": "mu1: analgesia و euphoria و dependence. mu2: respiratory depression و reduced gut motility."}, {"q": "أي receptor مرتبط بالـ sedation؟", "opts": ["mu2", "Mu", "Delta", "Kappa"], "a": 3, "why": "kappa بيبطّئ الـ GI transit مع mu، وكمان بيعمل sedation."}, {"q": "أي receptors بيبطّؤوا الـ GI transit؟", "opts": ["Mu و Kappa", "Kappa و Delta", "Mu و Delta", "Delta بس"], "a": 0, "why": "mu و kappa مع بعض."}, {"q": "أي receptor ممكن يلعب دور بتطوير الـ tolerance؟", "opts": ["Kappa", "Delta", "mu2", "mu1"], "a": 1, "why": "المحاضرة: delta ممكن يكون إلو دور بالـ tolerance."}, {"q": "أي ترتيب صحيح للـ affinity؟", "opts": ["Endorphin لـ mu، Enkephalin لـ kappa، Dynorphin لـ delta", "Endorphin لـ delta، Enkephalin لـ mu، Dynorphin لـ kappa", "Endorphin لـ kappa، Enkephalin لـ delta، Dynorphin لـ mu", "Endorphin لـ mu، Enkephalin لـ delta، Dynorphin لـ kappa"], "a": 3, "why": "Endorphins mu، Enkephalins delta، Dynorphins kappa."}, {"q": "أي جملة صحيحة عن mu1 و mu2؟", "opts": ["mu1 و mu2 الاثنين respiratory depression بس", "mu1: analgesia و euphoria و dependence. mu2: respiratory depression و reduced gut motility", "mu1: reduced gut motility. mu2: dependence", "mu1: respiratory depression. mu2: analgesia و euphoria"], "a": 1, "why": "هيك قسمتها المحاضرة."}, {"q": "شو الـ effect النهائي على الـ postsynaptic neuron؟", "opts": ["بيسكّر voltage-gated Ca channels", "بيفتح K channels فبيصير hyperpolarization", "بيسكّر K channels فبيصير depolarization", "بيفتح Ca channels فبيزيد الـ neurotransmitter release"], "a": 1, "why": "الـ postsynaptic: potassium channels بتنفتح وبيصير hyperpolarization (IPSPs). سكر الـ Ca channels بيصير بالـ presynaptic."}, {"q": "شو بيصير بالـ presynaptic terminal؟", "opts": ["بيفتح Ca channels فبيزيد الـ release", "بيفتح K channels فبيصير hyperpolarization", "بيفعّل adenylyl cyclase فبيزيد الـ release", "بيسكّر voltage-gated Ca channels فبيقل الـ neurotransmitter release"], "a": 3, "why": "الـ Ca2+ ما بيفوت، فبيقل إطلاق الـ neurotransmitter."}, {"q": "الـ opioid receptors مربوطة بـ G proteins. شو بتعمل؟", "opts": ["بتفعّل phospholipase C أو بتثبّط adenylyl cyclase", "بتثبّط phospholipase C وبتفعّل adenylyl cyclase", "بتثبّط الاثنين", "بتفعّل الاثنين"], "a": 0, "why": "هيك وصفتها المحاضرة."}, {"q": "مريض أخد morphine وطلع عندو vomiting و miosis. هدول من أي نوع تأثير؟", "opts": ["CNS excitation", "CNS depression", "Smooth muscle spasm", "Peripheral anti-inflammatory effect"], "a": 0, "why": "المحاضرة حطت vomiting و miosis تحت الـ CNS excitation."}, {"q": "ليش الـ morphine بيعمل constipation؟", "opts": ["Bronchospasm", "Biliary tract relaxation", "Vasodilatation بالـ veins", "GI muscle spasm فالمحتويات بتتأخر"], "a": 3, "why": "الـ spasm بيأخّر مرور المحتويات."}, {"q": "أي مجموعة صحيحة لتأثير morphine على الـ smooth muscle؟", "opts": ["GI relaxation و biliary spasm و bronchodilation", "GI spasm و biliary tract spasm و bronchospasm", "GI spasm و biliary relaxation و bronchospasm", "Bronchospasm بس"], "a": 1, "why": "كلهن stimulation للـ smooth muscle فبيصير spasm."}, {"q": "شو تأثير morphine على الـ cardiovascular system؟", "opts": ["ما إلو أي تأثير", "Constriction للـ arterioles", "Dilatation للـ arterioles بس", "Dilatation للـ arterioles وللـ veins"], "a": 3, "why": "المحاضرة: dilatation للـ arterioles والـ veins."}, {"q": "مريض عندو acute pulmonary edema. أي دوا ولأي سبب؟", "opts": ["Morphine parenteral بسبب الـ hemodynamic actions والـ calming effect", "Codeine لأنو antitussive", "Fentanyl transdermal لأنو بيعطي analgesia 72 h", "Naloxone لأنو بيعكس الـ overdose"], "a": 0, "why": "الـ hemodynamic actions هي السبب الأساسي، والـ calming effect بيساعد."}, {"q": "أي opioids هني المكوّن الأساسي بـ anesthesia تبع cardiac surgery؟", "opts": ["Naloxone و nalmefene", "Codeine و dextromethorphan", "High-dose IV morphine و fentanyl", "Tramadol و tapentadol"], "a": 2, "why": "المحاضرة: high-dose IV opioids (morphine, fentanyl)."}, {"q": "شو فايدة الـ epidural administration لـ fentanyl و morphine؟", "opts": ["بيطوّل الـ analgesia لـ 72 h", "بيمنع الـ first-pass metabolism", "بيقلل الـ side effects", "بيمنع الـ tolerance"], "a": 2, "why": "المحاضرة: epidural بيقلل الـ side effects."}, {"q": "شاب أخد جرعة كبيرة من OTC cough suppressant وصار عندو hallucinations و nystagmus و seizures. شو الدوا؟", "opts": ["Codeine", "Loperamide", "Dextromethorphan", "Diphenoxylate"], "a": 2, "why": "الـ dextromethorphan OTC وعليه FDA warnings للـ abuse، والجرعات العالية بتعمل هيك أعراض."}, {"q": "أي زوج هو selective antidiarrheal opioids؟", "opts": ["Codeine و Dextromethorphan", "Fentanyl و Methadone", "Diphenoxylate و Loperamide", "Naloxone و Naltrexone"], "a": 2, "why": "المحاضرة: diphenoxylate و loperamide."}, {"q": "مريض بياخد MAO inhibitor وانعطى meperidine. شو الخطر؟", "opts": ["Hyperpyrexic coma", "Biliary spasm", "Serotonin syndrome", "Respiratory alkalosis"], "a": 0, "why": "Meperidine مع MAO inhibitors بيزيد حدوث hyperpyrexic coma، ومع SSRIs بيعمل serotonin syndrome."}, {"q": "مريض على SSRI. أي مجموعة فيها خطر serotonin syndrome؟", "opts": ["Naloxone و Naltrexone و Nalmefene", "Morphine و Fentanyl و Codeine", "Loperamide و Diphenoxylate و Buprenorphine", "Meperidine و Tramadol و Tapentadol"], "a": 3, "why": "المحاضرة ربطت الثلاثة بالـ serotonin syndrome."}, {"q": "أي دوا من هدول ما بيعمل additive CNS depression مع opioids؟", "opts": ["Naloxone", "Ethanol", "Antihistamines", "Tricyclic antidepressants"], "a": 0, "why": "الـ naloxone antagonist وبيعاكس الـ opioids، بينما الباقي بيثبّطوا الـ CNS."}, {"q": "أي ترتيب صحيح بالـ analgesia؟", "opts": ["Buprenorphine و Nalbuphine أكتر من Pentazocine، و Pentazocine مثل Codeine", "Pentazocine أكتر من Morphine", "كلهن نفس الـ analgesia", "Pentazocine أكتر من Buprenorphine و Nalbuphine"], "a": 0, "why": "هيك قالت المحاضرة."}, {"q": "الـ analgesic activity تبع tramadol مبنية أساساً على؟", "opts": ["Blocking serotonin reuptake", "Norepinephrine reuptake inhibition", "Strong mu agonism", "Kappa agonism"], "a": 0, "why": "Tramadol weak mu agonist، والـ naloxone بيعاكسو جزئياً."}, {"q": "بالمقارنة مع oxycodone، الـ tapentadol؟", "opts": ["نفس الفعالية و نفس الـ side effects", "أكتر فعالية و nausea أقل", "أقل فعالية بس GI distress و nausea أقل", "أكتر فعالية و GI distress أكتر"], "a": 2, "why": "Tapentadol عندو strong norepinephrine reuptake inhibition و modest mu affinity."}, {"q": "أي دوا relatively contraindicated مع seizure disorders؟", "opts": ["Methylnaltrexone", "Fentanyl transdermal", "Tramadol", "Naloxone"], "a": 2, "why": "المحاضرة: tramadol relatively contraindicated، و tapentadol بدو حذر."}, {"q": "ليش ممكن نحتاج doses متعددة من naloxone بالـ overdose؟", "opts": ["لأنو إلو extensive first-pass", "لأنو partial agonist", "لأنو duration تبعو قصير (1-2 h)", "لأنو ما بيعبر الـ BBB"], "a": 2, "why": "فممكن يخلص مفعولو قبل ما يخلص مفعول الـ opioid."}, {"q": "أي antagonist الـ duration تبعو 8-12 h؟", "opts": ["Nalmefene", "Naltrexone", "Methylnaltrexone", "Naloxone"], "a": 0, "why": "Naloxone 1-2 h، nalmefene 8-12 h، naltrexone حتى 48 h."}, {"q": "أي دوا oral بيبلوك heroin حتى 48 ساعة ومعتمد بـ alcohol dependency؟", "opts": ["Nalmefene", "Naloxone", "Alvimopan", "Naltrexone"], "a": 3, "why": "Naltrexone عندو long half-life."}, {"q": "ليش Methylnaltrexone بيعالج opioid constipation بدون ما يضيّع الـ analgesia؟", "opts": ["ما بيعبر الـ BBB فبيبلوك الـ peripheral mu receptors (GI) بس", "لأنو بيفعّل الـ kappa receptors", "لأنو بيتحوّل لـ morphine", "لأنو partial agonist"], "a": 0, "why": "هيك كمان alvimopan."}, {"q": "شو هو Naloxegol؟", "opts": ["Antitussive", "Pegylated naloxone بيعكس الـ opioid constipation", "Mixed agonist-antagonist", "Opioid peptide داخلي"], "a": 1, "why": "المحاضرة: naloxegol هو pegylated form من naloxone."}, {"q": "شو الفرق الأساسي بين Narcotic و Non-narcotic analgesics؟", "opts": ["Narcotic بالـ CNS وبيعمل drowsiness، و Non-narcotic غالباً peripherally", "Narcotic peripherally و Non-narcotic بالـ CNS", "الاثنين بالـ CNS بس بيختلفوا بالـ potency", "Narcotic بيعمل tolerance بس"], "a": 0, "why": "مثال Non-narcotic: diclofenac."}, {"q": "شخص بيحس إنو مجبر ياخد الدوا وبيقلق لما يبعد عنو. شو هيدا؟", "opts": ["Addiction", "Dependence", "Tolerance", "Withdrawal فقط"], "a": 0, "why": "Tolerance: بدك dose أكبر. Dependence: أعراض لما توقّف الدوا. Addiction: مجبر + anxiety."}], "cards": [{"f": "مريض عندو pain شديدة، وعطوه دوا بـ patch على الجلد بيعطي analgesia 72 ساعة. أي دوا؟", "b": "Fentanyl (transdermal)."}, {"f": "دوا قوي أكتر من morphine مية مرة بالـ potency؟", "b": "Fentanyl."}, {"f": "دوا بيتحوّل لـ normeperidine وبيعمل seizures؟", "b": "Meperidine."}, {"f": "مريض عالج MAO inhibitor وانعطى opioid وصار عندو hyperpyrexic coma. أي opioid؟", "b": "Meperidine."}, {"f": "مريض عالج SSRI وانعطى opioid وصار عندو serotonin syndrome. شو ممكن يكون؟", "b": "Meperidine أو Tramadol أو Tapentadol."}, {"f": "مريض ماخد جرعات عالية من OTC cough suppressant وعندو hallucinations و nystagmus و seizures؟", "b": "Dextromethorphan."}, {"f": "مريض بالـ ER، pupils مصغرة (miosis)، تنفسو بطيء بعد overdose. شو الـ antidote؟", "b": "Naloxone (IV)."}, {"f": "مريض بـ alcohol dependency program عطوه دوا بيبلوك الـ opioids 48 ساعة؟", "b": "Naltrexone."}, {"f": "مريض عنده acute pulmonary edema، أي opioid بينعطى؟", "b": "Morphine parenteral، بسبب الـ hemodynamic actions والـ calming effect."}, {"f": "أي opioid هو المكوّن الأساسي بالـ anesthesia تبع cardiac surgery؟", "b": "High-dose IV morphine أو fentanyl."}, {"f": "دوا بيعالج الـ diarrhea وهو opioid؟", "b": "Diphenoxylate و Loperamide."}, {"f": "ليش الـ strong agonist مش دايماً الأعلى بالـ potency؟", "b": "لأنو التصنيف strong/moderate/weak حسب الـ efficacy، وبيختلف عن الـ potency."}, {"f": "ليش morphine الـ oral جرعتو أعلى من الـ parenteral؟", "b": "لأنو بيمرق بـ extensive first-pass metabolism بالـ liver."}, {"f": "ليش الـ codeine ممكن يختلف مفعولو من شخص لشخص؟", "b": "لأنو بيتحوّل لـ morphine بـ CYP2D6 وهاد الـ enzyme فيه genotypic variability."}, {"f": "ليش الـ morphine بيعمل constipation؟", "b": "لأنو بيعمل GI smooth muscle spasm فالمحتويات بتتأخر، وبيمر عبر mu و kappa."}, {"f": "ليش بيصير respiratory depression؟", "b": "تفعيل mu receptors، وتحديداً mu2."}, {"f": "ليش الـ naloxone بدو doses متعددة بالـ overdose؟", "b": "لأنو duration تبعو قصير 1-2 h وعادةً أقصر من الـ opioid."}, {"f": "ليش الـ patient بيحتاج dose أكبر بعد فترة؟", "b": "Tolerance، وممكن delta receptors عندها دور."}, {"f": "ليش الـ opioid بيوقف نقل الـ pain على مستوى الـ cell؟", "b": "بيفتح K channels (hyperpolarization postsynaptic) وبيسكّر Ca channels (قلة release presynaptic)."}, {"f": "ليش الـ neonate ممكن يطلعلو withdrawal؟", "b": "لأنو الـ opioids بتعبر الـ placenta وبيصير physical dependence مع exposure مستمر."}, {"f": "ليش الـ liver disease بيخلي الـ opioid يضل أكتر بالجسم؟", "b": "لأنو بيطوّل الـ elimination half-life."}, {"f": "ليش الـ opioid + alcohol أو sedatives خطر؟", "b": "Additive CNS depression."}, {"f": "ليش Methylnaltrexone بيعالج الـ constipation بلا ما يضيّع الـ analgesia؟", "b": "لأنو ما بيعبر الـ BBB، فبيبلوك الـ peripheral mu receptors (GI) بس."}, {"f": "ليش الـ Tramadol بيتحذر مع SSRIs؟", "b": "لأنو بيبلوك serotonin reuptake، فخطر serotonin syndrome."}, {"f": "ليش الـ Tramadol relatively contraindicated بالـ seizure disorders؟", "b": "لأنو الـ lecture حاطو relatively contraindicated مع seizure disorders."}, {"f": "Morphine-6-glucuronide ضد Morphine-3-glucuronide؟", "b": "M6G active analgesic. M3G هو الـ primary metabolite وهو neuroexcitatory."}, {"f": "Endorphin و Enkephalin و Dynorphin: كل واحد لأي receptor؟", "b": "Endorphin لـ mu، Enkephalin لـ delta، Dynorphin لـ kappa."}, {"f": "mu1 ضد mu2؟", "b": "mu1: analgesia و euphoria و dependence. mu2: respiratory depression و reduced gut motility."}, {"f": "Naloxone ضد Nalmefene ضد Naltrexone بالـ duration؟", "b": "Naloxone 1-2 h. Nalmefene 8-12 h. Naltrexone حتى 48 h."}, {"f": "Fentanyl ضد Buprenorphine بالـ duration؟", "b": "Fentanyl 1-2 h. Buprenorphine 6-8 h."}, {"f": "Tapentadol ضد Oxycodone؟", "b": "Tapentadol أقل فعالية بس بيعمل GI distress و nausea أقل."}, {"f": "Pentazocine ضد Buprenorphine و Nalbuphine؟", "b": "Buprenorphine و Nalbuphine analgesia أكتر. Pentazocine متل codeine."}, {"f": "Opiate ضد Opioid؟", "b": "Opiate من alkaloids تبع opium poppy. Opioid الصف الأكبر وبيشمل opiates + peptides + synthetic و semisynthetic."}, {"f": "Full agonist ضد Partial ضد Mixed؟", "b": "Full: morphine, fentanyl. Partial: codeine, hydrocodone (analgesia أقل حتى مع جرعة أعلى). Mixed: buprenorphine, nalbuphine (بيفعّل subtype وبيسكّر تاني)."}, {"f": "Tolerance ضد Dependence ضد Addiction؟", "b": "Tolerance: لازم تزيد الجرعة. Dependence: شيل الدوا بيعمل أعراض. Addiction: مجبر ياخد الدوا وبيقلق من غيابو."}, {"f": "أي receptor بيعمل sedation؟", "b": "Kappa."}, {"f": "أي receptor ممكن يلعب دور بالـ tolerance؟", "b": "Delta."}, {"f": "أي receptors بيبطّؤوا الـ GI transit؟", "b": "Mu و Kappa."}, {"f": "الـ receptor مربوط بأي شي وشو بيعمل؟", "b": "G proteins: بيفعّلوا phospholipase C أو بيثبّطوا adenylyl cyclase."}, {"f": "أي أدوية بتزيد الـ CNS depression مع opioids؟", "b": "Ethanol و sedative-hypnotics و anesthetics و antipsychotics و TCAs و antihistamines."}, {"f": "أي أدوية فيها خطر serotonin syndrome؟", "b": "Meperidine و Tramadol و Tapentadol مع SSRIs."}, {"f": "أي أدوية بدها حذر بالـ seizure disorders؟", "b": "Tramadol و Tapentadol، وكمان meperidine بسبب normeperidine."}, {"f": "شو بيزيد peak level تبع hydromorphone و oxymorphone؟", "b": "Alcohol."}, {"f": "قارن بين Naloxone و Naltrexone و Methylnaltrexone.", "b": "Naloxone: 1-2 h، IV (+ nasal)، acute opioid overdose. • Naltrexone: حتى 48 h، oral، adjunct بـ alcohol dependency وبيبلوك heroin. • Methylnaltrexone: ما بيعبر BBB، opioid constipation بلا ما يأثر عالـ analgesia."}], "subject": "pharm", "date": "2026-11-27"},
 {"id": "cns-narcotic-8", "system": "CNS", "no": 8, "title": "Narcotic (Opioid) Analgesics", "url": "pharm-narcotic-3.html", "summary": "Pain and analgesia, opioid classification, pharmacokinetics, mu/kappa/delta receptors, morphine actions, clinical uses, interactions, tramadol, tapentadol, and opioid antagonists.", "points": ["Tolerance vs Dependence vs Addiction", "µ: respiratory depression · κ: sedation · δ: tolerance", "Fentanyl أقوى من morphine بـ 100 مرة", "Meperidine → normeperidine → seizures", "Codeine → morphine بالـ CYP2D6", "Naloxone 1-2h · Nalmefene 8-12h · Naltrexone 48h", "Methylnaltrexone للـ opioid constipation"], "mcqs": [{"q": "Narcotic analgesics act mainly on:", "opts": ["Peripheral nerves", "CNS", "Kidney", "Liver"], "a": 1, "why": "بيشتغلو بالدماغ والنخاع."}, {"q": "Drug requiring more dose for same effect shows:", "opts": ["Dependence", "Tolerance", "Addiction", "Analgesia"], "a": 1, "why": "التحمل: لازم جرعة أكبر."}, {"q": "Withdrawal on drug removal describes:", "opts": ["Tolerance", "Dependence", "Addiction", "Adjuvant"], "a": 1, "why": "الاعتماد: أعراض سحب لما توقف."}, {"q": "Fentanyl analgesic strength vs morphine:", "opts": ["Weaker", "Equal", "About 100× stronger", "Inactive"], "a": 2, "why": "0.1 mg فنتانيل = 10 mg مورفين."}, {"q": "Partial agonist example:", "opts": ["Morphine", "Codeine", "Fentanyl", "Methadone"], "a": 1, "why": "codeine partial."}, {"q": "Pure antagonist example:", "opts": ["Naloxone", "Buprenorphine", "Tramadol", "Codeine"], "a": 0, "why": "naloxone pure."}, {"q": "Mixed agonist-antagonist example:", "opts": ["Naltrexone", "Nalbuphine", "Naloxone", "Methylnaltrexone"], "a": 1, "why": "nalbuphine mixed."}, {"q": "Endorphins act most on:", "opts": ["δ", "κ", "µ", "α"], "a": 2, "why": "endorphin → µ."}, {"q": "Enkephalins act most on:", "opts": ["µ", "δ", "κ", "β"], "a": 1, "why": "enkephalin → δ."}, {"q": "Dynorphins act most on:", "opts": ["µ", "δ", "κ", "γ"], "a": 2, "why": "dynorphin → κ."}, {"q": "Opioid receptor activation opens:", "opts": ["Ca²⁺ channels", "K⁺ channels", "Na⁺ pumps", "Cl⁻ pumps"], "a": 1, "why": "K⁺ open ← hyperpolarization."}, {"q": "Morphine causes constipation via:", "opts": ["Relaxation of GI", "GI spasm", "Vasodilation", "Bronchodilation"], "a": 1, "why": "تشنج عضلات الأمعاء."}, {"q": "Morphine dilates:", "opts": ["Capillaries only", "Arterioles and veins", "Bronchi", "Ureters"], "a": 1, "why": "وعيات الأوعية."}, {"q": "Codeine becomes active by:", "opts": ["CYP2D6", "CYP3A4", "Glucuronide only", "Renal excretion"], "a": 0, "why": "CYP2D6 ← morphine."}, {"q": "Meperidine metabolite causing seizures:", "opts": ["Morphine-6-glucuronide", "Normeperidine", "Naloxone", "Tapentadol"], "a": 1, "why": "high plasma levels."}, {"q": "Fentanyl transdermal duration:", "opts": ["1 h", "24 h", "72 h", "7 days"], "a": 2, "why": "بلاصقة لـ72 ساعة."}, {"q": "Naloxone duration:", "opts": ["1-2 h", "8-12 h", "24 h", "48 h"], "a": 0, "why": "قصير، ويحتاج جرعات متكررة."}, {"q": "Naltrexone blocks heroin up to:", "opts": ["2 h", "8 h", "24 h", "48 h"], "a": 3, "why": "48 ساعة."}, {"q": "Peripheral antagonist that does not cross BBB:", "opts": ["Naloxone", "Methylnaltrexone", "Morphine", "Codeine"], "a": 1, "why": "بيوقف الإمساك وبيبقى برا الدماغ."}, {"q": "Cough suppressant opioid:", "opts": ["Loperamide", "Dextromethorphan", "Naloxone", "Alvimopan"], "a": 1, "why": "مع codeine."}, {"q": "Antidiarrheal opioid:", "opts": ["Codeine", "Loperamide", "Naloxone", "Buprenorphine"], "a": 1, "why": "diphenoxylate و loperamide."}, {"q": "MAOI with meperidine causes:", "opts": ["Hypothermia", "Hyperpyrexic coma", "Bradycardia", "Hypoglycemia"], "a": 1, "why": "حرارة عالية وغيبوبة."}, {"q": "Meperidine with SSRI causes:", "opts": ["Serotonin syndrome", "Opioid overdose", "Tolerance", "Dependence"], "a": 0, "why": "متلازمة السيروتونين."}, {"q": "Tramadol mechanism:", "opts": ["Potent µ agonist", "Weak µ agonist + serotonin reuptake block", "Pure antagonist", "Naloxone-like"], "a": 1, "why": "ضعيف + سيروتونين."}, {"q": "Tapentadol main mechanism:", "opts": ["Serotonin reuptake", "Norepinephrine reuptake inhibition", "Opioid antagonism", "GABA agonism"], "a": 1, "why": "NE reuptake."}, {"q": "Morphine-3-glucuronide effect:", "opts": ["Analgesic", "Neuroexcitatory", "Antitussive", "Antidiarrheal"], "a": 1, "why": "primary metabolite excitatory."}], "cards": [{"f": "مريض عندو overdose من opioid، وصل مرتخي ونَفَسو بطيء. شو بنعطيه؟", "b": "Naloxone (IV أو nasal). بس duration قصير (1 لـ 2 ساعة)، فممكن نعيد الجرعة."}, {"f": "مريض عم يخلّص من heroin وبدو دوا طويل المفعول يحجب تأثيرو، وكمان بيستعمل مع alcohol dependency.", "b": "Naltrexone (يحجب لحد 48 ساعة)."}, {"f": "مريض عندو opioid-induced constipation وما بدنا نأثّر على الـ analgesia.", "b": "Methylnaltrexone أو alvimopan (ما بيعبرو الـ BBB). كمان naloxegol."}, {"f": "مريض عندو acute pulmonary edema.", "b": "Morphine (parenteral)."}, {"f": "مريض عندو diarrhea وبدنا opioid selective.", "b": "Diphenoxylate أو loperamide."}, {"f": "مريض عندو سعال وبدنا دوا OTC.", "b": "Dextromethorphan. (بالجرعات الكبيرة: hallucinations و nystagmus و seizures.)"}, {"f": "مريض عندو seizures بعد جرعات عالية من opioid، وكان ياخد meperidine.", "b": "Normeperidine (metabolite تبع meperidine)."}, {"f": "مريض ياخد MAO inhibitor وانعطى opioid وصار عندو hyperpyrexic coma.", "b": "Meperidine."}, {"f": "مريض ياخد SSRI وانعطى opioid وصار عندو serotonin syndrome.", "b": "Meperidine (أو tramadol أو tapentadol)."}, {"f": "مريض عندو history من seizures، أي opioid لازم نتجنبو أو نحذر فيه؟", "b": "Tramadol (relatively contraindicated) و tapentadol (caution)."}, {"f": "مريض عندو pain مزمن moderate وبدنا دوا مع serotonin reuptake blockade.", "b": "Tramadol."}, {"f": "مريض بدو patch يعطي analgesia لـ 72 ساعة.", "b": "Fentanyl transdermal."}, {"f": "سيدة حامل ياخد opioids باستمرار، شو الخطر على الجنين؟", "b": "Respiratory depression، وبعد الولادة withdrawal effect عند الـ neonate."}, {"f": "ليش الـ morphine بيعمل constipation؟", "b": "لأنو بيعمل GI muscle spasm، فالمحتويات بتتأخر."}, {"f": "ليش الـ opioids بيعملو respiratory depression؟", "b": "لأنو µ receptor (µ2 بالتحديد) بيشتغل بهالتأثير."}, {"f": "ليش الـ opioids بيعملو miosis وvomiting؟", "b": "لأنهن من تأثيرات CNS excitation."}, {"f": "ليش الـ liver disease بيخلّي الـ opioids تضل أكتر؟", "b": "لأنو الـ liver هو يلي بيعمل الـ metabolism، فالـ half-life بيزيد."}, {"f": "ليش الـ codeine بيعمل analgesia مع إنو weak؟", "b": "لأنو بيتحوّل لـ morphine بالـ CYP2D6."}, {"f": "ليش الـ CYP2D6 مهم؟", "b": "لأنو عندو genotypic variability، فالتأثير بيختلف من شخص لشخص."}, {"f": "ليش الـ naloxone ممكن نحتاج نعيد جرعتو بالـ overdose؟", "b": "لأنو duration قصير (1 لـ 2 ساعة)."}, {"f": "ليش الـ methylnaltrexone ما بيأثّر على الـ analgesia؟", "b": "لأنو ما بيعبر الـ blood-brain barrier، فبيحجب بس الـ peripheral µ receptors."}, {"f": "ليش الـ opioids بتمنع انتقال الـ pain؟", "b": "بتفتح K+ channels (hyperpolarization) وبتسكّر Ca2+ channels (بيقلّ تحرير الـ neurotransmitters)."}, {"f": "ليش الـ fentanyl أقوى من morphine بس هنن الاثنين strong agonists؟", "b": "لأنو الـ strength (strong/moderate/weak) مستقل عن الـ potency. fentanyl أقوى بـ 100 مرة بالـ potency."}, {"f": "ليش الـ opioid partial agonist عندو analgesia أقل من morphine؟", "b": "لأنو بيفعّل الـ receptor لـ submaximal response، مهما زدنا الجرعة."}, {"f": "ليش الـ epidural بيقلّل الـ side effects؟", "b": "(حسب المحاضرة) epidural administration لـ fentanyl و morphine بيقلّل الـ side effects."}, {"f": "Opiate مقابل Opioid؟", "b": "Opiate: مشتق من alkaloids تبع الـ opium poppy. Opioid: كل يلي بيقلّد الـ opiates (منها opiates و opioid peptides و synthetic و semisynthetic)."}, {"f": "Tolerance مقابل Dependence مقابل Addiction؟", "b": "Tolerance: بدك جرعة أكتر. Dependence: أعراض سحب لما توقّف. Addiction: إحساس إجبار و anxiety."}, {"f": "Narcotic مقابل Non-Narcotic analgesics؟", "b": "Narcotic: بالـ CNS و drowsiness (opioids). Non-Narcotic: بالأساس peripherally (مثال diclofenac)."}, {"f": "µ1 مقابل µ2؟", "b": "µ1: analgesia، euphoria، dependence. µ2: respiratory depression، reduced gut motility."}, {"f": "Endorphins مقابل Enkephalins مقابل Dynorphins؟", "b": "Endorphins → µ، Enkephalins → δ، Dynorphins → κ."}, {"f": "Naloxone مقابل Nalmefene مقابل Naltrexone؟", "b": "Naloxone: 1 لـ 2 ساعة. Nalmefene: 8 لـ 12 ساعة. Naltrexone: half-life طويل، 48 ساعة، oral، alcohol dependency."}, {"f": "Tramadol مقابل Tapentadol؟", "b": "Tramadol: weak µ agonist + serotonin reuptake blockade. Tapentadol: norepinephrine reuptake inhibition + modest µ affinity، أقل GI distress من oxycodone."}, {"f": "Pentazocine مقابل Buprenorphine و nalbuphine؟", "b": "Buprenorphine و nalbuphine: analgesia أكتر. Pentazocine: analgesia متل codeine."}, {"f": "Morphine-6-glucuronide مقابل Morphine-3-glucuronide؟", "b": "M6G: analgesic متل morphine. M3G: primary metabolite، neuroexcitatory."}, {"f": "شو الـ µ receptor بيعمل؟", "b": "Analgesia و respiratory depression وبيبطّئ GI transit."}, {"f": "شو الـ κ receptor بيعمل؟", "b": "Analgesia و sedation وبيبطّئ GI transit."}, {"f": "شو الـ δ receptor بيعمل؟", "b": "Analgesia، وممكن إلو دور بتطوّر tolerance."}, {"f": "شو أعراض dextromethorphan بالجرعات العالية؟", "b": "Hallucinations، confusion، excitation، تغيّر حجم الـ pupil، nystagmus، seizures، coma، decreased ventilation."}, {"f": "شو الـ adjuvant drugs؟", "b": "أدوية منستعملها مع الـ analgesics بعلاج الـ pain."}, {"f": "مين بيعبر الـ placenta؟", "b": "الـ opioids."}, {"f": "شو أدوية الـ opioid agonists؟", "b": "Fentanyl، hydromorphone، meperidine، morphine، methadone، oxymorphone."}, {"f": "شو الـ partial agonists؟", "b": "Codeine و hydrocodone."}, {"f": "شو الـ mixed agonist-antagonists؟", "b": "Buprenorphine و nalbuphine."}, {"f": "شو أدوية الـ opioid antagonists الأساسية؟", "b": "Naloxone و naltrexone (و nalmefene)."}, {"f": "عندك 4 مجموعات opioids. كيف منفرّقهن؟", "b": "- Strong agonists (morphine, fentanyl, hydromorphone, meperidine, methadone, oxymorphone): بيفعّلو الـ receptor كامل، للـ moderate لـ severe pain. • - Partial agonists (codeine, hydrocodone): analgesia أقل مهما زدنا الجرعة، للـ pain الأخف أو للسعال. • - Mixed agonist-antagonists (buprenorphine, nalbuphine, pentazocine): بيفعّلو subtype وبيحجبو غيرو، analgesia أقل من morphine. • - Antagonists (naloxone, nalmefene, naltrexone): بيحجبو، للـ opioid overdose."}], "subject": "pharm", "date": "2026-11-27"},
 {"id": "autocoid-kinin-3", "system": "Autocoid", "no": 3, "title": "Kinins, Endothelin and Purines (Autacoids)", "url": "pharm-kinin-3.html", "summary": "Kinin biosynthesis and receptors (B1/B2), actions, ACE inhibitor side effects, hereditary angioedema, icatibant, endothelin and its antagonists, purines (ATP, adenosine), methylxanthines, and adenosine as a drug.", "points": ["Kallikrein يقصّ kininogen فبيطلع kinin", "B1 و B2: B من Bradykinin مش beta", "ACE inhibitors: kinin يزيد فسعال وangioedema", "Icatibant: مضاد B2 للـ HAE", "Endothelin: vasoconstriction قوية، ambrisentan مضاد", "Adenosine: فرامل الجسم، والـ caffeine بتحجبو"], "mcqs": [{"q": "Kinins are formed by the action of kallikreins on:", "opts": ["Kininogens", "Endothelin", "Angiotensinogen", "Histamine"], "a": 0, "why": "الكاليكرين (أو كينينوجينيز) بيشتغل عالكينينوجين (Kininogen) وبيطلّع الكينين."}, {"q": "Kinin receptors are:", "opts": ["A1, A2", "B1, B2", "ETA, ETB", "P2Y, P2X"], "a": 1, "why": "B1 و B2. الباقي مستقبلات الإندوثيلين والبيورينات."}, {"q": "The letter B in kinin receptors stands for:", "opts": ["Bronchus", "Blocker", "Bradykinin", "β adrenoceptor"], "a": 2, "why": "B = Bradykinin، مش بيتا."}, {"q": "Bradykinin effect on arterioles of heart, kidney, liver:", "opts": ["Calcification", "Constriction", "No effect", "Marked dilation"], "a": 3, "why": "الكينين بيوسّع الشرينات (Arterioles) بالأعضاء، رغم إنو بيقبّض عضل الأحشاء."}, {"q": "Bradykinin potency compared with histamine:", "opts": ["10 × more potent", "2 × less potent", "Equal", "100 × more potent"], "a": 0, "why": "بحرفية الملف: أقوى بعشر مرات."}, {"q": "Cough and angioedema with ACEI are due to:", "opts": ["↑ endothelin", "↑ bradykinin", "↓ adenosine", "↓ bradykinin"], "a": 1, "why": "ACEI بترفع مستوى البرادي كينين، وهو المسؤول عن السعال والوذمة."}, {"q": "HAE is caused by deficiency of:", "opts": ["Kallikrein", "ACE", "C1 esterase inhibitor", "Kininogen"], "a": 2, "why": "نقص C1 inh ← الكاليكرين بلا فرامل ← بحر برادي كينين."}, {"q": "HAE inheritance:", "opts": ["X-linked recessive", "Mitochondrial", "Autosomal recessive", "Autosomal dominant"], "a": 3, "why": "الملف: Autosomal dominant."}, {"q": "Icatibant is:", "opts": ["B2 receptor antagonist", "ET blocker", "Kallikrein enzyme", "B1 agonist"], "a": 0, "why": "إيكاتيبانت مضاد لمستقبل B2، ببتيد من 10 أحماض أمينية."}, {"q": "ACEI angioedema: icatibant is used:", "opts": ["Never", "Only when life-threatening", "Only orally", "Always first line"], "a": 1, "why": "الملف: بيُستعمل بس لما تكون الحالة مهدّدة للحياة."}, {"q": "Most important endothelin and receptor:", "opts": ["ET2 / ETB", "ET1 / B2", "ET1 / ETA", "ET3 / ETB"], "a": 2, "why": "الأهم ET1 والمستقبل ETA."}, {"q": "Endothelin special effect among mediators:", "opts": ["Marked vasodilation", "Sleepiness", "↓ A-V conduction", "Severe vasoconstriction"], "a": 3, "why": "بيعمل تضيّق وعائي شديد."}, {"q": "FDA-approved ET blocker for women with pulmonary HT:", "opts": ["Ambrisentan", "Theophylline", "Adenosine", "Icatibant"], "a": 0, "why": "Ambrisentan. وكمان Sildenafil و Prostacyclin ممكن."}, {"q": "Adenosine receptor effect in bronchi:", "opts": ["No effect", "Severe bronchoconstriction", "Mucus ↓", "Bronchodilatation"], "a": 1, "why": "مستقبل A بالقصبات بيسبّب تضيّق شديد جداً."}, {"q": "Adenosine effect on conductive system of heart:", "opts": ["↑ A-V conduction", "No effect", "↓ A-V conduction", "Tachycardia"], "a": 2, "why": "بينقّص التوصيل الأذيني البطيني."}, {"q": "Methylxanthines act by:", "opts": ["Blocking B2", "Blocking ETA", "Stimulating A1 receptor", "Blocking A1 receptor"], "a": 3, "why": "الكافيين والثيوفيلين بيحجبو A1."}, {"q": "Methylxanthines are contraindicated in:", "opts": ["Palpitation, arrhythmias", "Bronchial asthma", "Sleepiness", "HAE"], "a": 0, "why": "بيزيدو سرعة القلب (Tachycardia)."}, {"q": "Theophylline is used in:", "opts": ["HAE", "Bronchial asthma", "SVT", "Pulmonary HT"], "a": 1, "why": "عشان بيعمل توسّع قصبات."}, {"q": "Adenosine as a drug treats:", "opts": ["HAE", "Essential HT", "Severe tachyarrhythmias (atrial, SVT)", "Bronchial asthma"], "a": 2, "why": "بينقّص التوصيل الأذيني البطيني، وبيضبط الاضطراب خلال ثواني."}, {"q": "Adenosine dose:", "opts": ["0.6 mg SC", "6–12 g oral", "60–120 mg IV", "6–12 mg IV"], "a": 3, "why": "الملف: من 6 لـ 12 ملغ بالوريد."}], "cards": [{"f": "Kinins are?", "b": "Peptides (protein), formed from kininogens"}, {"f": "Enzymes forming kinin?", "b": "Kallikreins = kininogenases"}, {"f": "Kinin receptors?", "b": "B1, B2; bradykinin highest affinity at B2"}, {"f": "B in B1, B2 stands for?", "b": "Bradykinin, not β adrenoceptor"}, {"f": "Kinin on smooth muscle / vessels?", "b": "Contraction (viscera, bronchi); marked arteriolar dilation (heart, skeletal muscle, kidney, liver, intestine)"}, {"f": "Bradykinin potency?", "b": "10 × histamine"}, {"f": "4 classic signs of inflammation by bradykinin?", "b": "Redness, local heat, swelling, pain (+ itching)"}, {"f": "Why do ACEI cause cough, angioedema?", "b": "Bradykinin level ↑"}, {"f": "HAE cause?", "b": "Mutation: C1 esterase inhibitor gene; autosomal dominant"}, {"f": "HAE mechanism?", "b": "C1 inh deficient → kallikrein not inhibited → huge bradykinin"}, {"f": "Icatibant?", "b": "2nd-generation B2 antagonist, decapeptide, SC; HAE"}, {"f": "Icatibant in ACEI angioedema?", "b": "Only if life-threatening"}, {"f": "Endothelin source / main type?", "b": "Vascular endothelium / ET1"}, {"f": "Main endothelin receptor?", "b": "ETA"}, {"f": "Endothelin special effect?", "b": "Severe vasoconstriction"}, {"f": "Ambrisentan?", "b": "ET receptor blocker; FDA: women, pulmonary HT"}, {"f": "Other drugs in pulmonary HT?", "b": "Sildenafil, prostacyclin"}, {"f": "Purine chain?", "b": "ATP → ADP → adenosine"}, {"f": "Adenosine receptor effects?", "b": "Bronchoconstriction (severe), ↓ A-V conduction, ↓ CNS"}, {"f": "Methylxanthines?", "b": "Caffeine, theophylline; block A1"}, {"f": "Methylxanthines effects?", "b": "Tachycardia, CNS stimulation, bronchodilatation"}, {"f": "Theophylline use?", "b": "Bronchial asthma"}, {"f": "Adenosine drug use?", "b": "Severe tachyarrhythmias (atrial, SVT): seconds; 6–12 mg IV"}, {"f": "Adenosine contraindication?", "b": "Bronchial asthma"}], "subject": "pharm", "date": "2026-11-28"},
 {"id": "script-autocoid-3", "system": "Autocoid", "kind": "script", "no": 3, "title": "Autocoid · Script 3 (Kinins, Endothelin, Purines)", "url": "pharm-script-kinin-3d.html", "summary": "Script and Cheat Code: kinins, ACE inhibitors, hereditary angioedema, icatibant, endothelin and ambrisentan, purines, methylxanthines and adenosine, with 50 MCQs.", "points": ["Kininogen + kallikrein → kinin", "ACEI: bradykinin → cough و angioedema", "HAE: C1 inhibitor ناقص", "Icatibant: B2 antagonist", "Ambrisentan: ET blocker", "Adenosine: SVT، ممنوع بالـ asthma"], "mcqs": [{"q": "Kinin من kininogen بـ", "opts": ["ACE", "Kallikrein", "ECE", "C1 inh"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Kallikrein"}, {"q": "HAE سببه", "opts": ["B2 overactive", "↓ kininogen", "C1 inh deficiency", "↑ ACE"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: C1 inh deficiency"}, {"q": "HAE inheritance", "opts": ["X-linked", "AD", "Mito", "AR"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: AD"}, {"q": "ACEI cough", "opts": ["↑ bradykinin", "↓ Ang II", "↑ ET", "↑ adenosine"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: ↑ bradykinin"}, {"q": "Icatibant", "opts": ["ETA blocker", "B1 agonist", "B2 antagonist", "A1 blocker"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: B2 antagonist"}, {"q": "Icatibant بـ ACEI angioedema", "opts": ["ممنوع", "cough", "دايماً", "life threatening فقط"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: life threatening فقط"}, {"q": "Icatibant", "opts": ["Steroid IV", "Tripeptide oral", "Decapeptide SC", "Decapeptide oral"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Decapeptide SC"}, {"q": "\"B\" =", "opts": ["Bronchial", "Bradykinin", "β", "Basal"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Bradykinin"}, {"q": "Highest affinity", "opts": ["B1", "B2", "P2X", "ETA"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: B2"}, {"q": "Potency vs histamine", "opts": ["نفسه", "×100", "×10", "×2"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: ×10"}, {"q": "مش bradykinin", "opts": ["Visceral SM contraction", "Arteriolar dilation", "Bronchodilation", "Bronchoconstriction"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Bronchodilation"}, {"q": "Itching", "opts": ["الاثنين", "ولا واحد", "Bradykinin", "Histamine"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: الاثنين"}, {"q": "Kinin pain", "opts": ["Afferent stimulation", "↑ prostacyclin", "Nociceptor blockade", "↓ histamine"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: Afferent stimulation"}, {"q": "Kinin antagonists", "opts": ["Anti-inflammatory + antinociceptive", "Antiarrhythmic", "Antihypertensive", "Bronchodilator"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: Anti-inflammatory + antinociceptive"}, {"q": "مش HAE", "opts": ["Jaundice", "Tongue swelling", "Genitalia angioedema", "GIT angioedema"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: Jaundice"}, {"q": "Kinin drugs", "opts": ["SVT first line", "Wide use", "ولا واحد wide use", "Asthma first line"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: ولا واحد wide use"}, {"q": "مش icatibant", "opts": ["Thermal injury", "Ascites", "SVT", "Pancreatitis"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: SVT"}, {"q": "ET source", "opts": ["Platelets", "Mast cells", "Endothelium", "Liver"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Endothelium"}, {"q": "الأهم", "opts": ["ETB", "ET2", "ET1", "ET3"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: ET1"}, {"q": "Receptor الأهم", "opts": ["ETB", "B2", "P2Y", "ETA"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: ETA"}, {"q": "استثناء ETA", "opts": ["Pain", "Severe vasoconstriction", "Bronchospasm", "SM contraction"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Severe vasoconstriction"}, {"q": "ET بـ", "opts": ["SVT", "HAE", "Asthma", "Essential HT"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: Essential HT"}, {"q": "Idiopathic pulmonary HT", "opts": ["Children", "Smokers", "Women", "Men"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Women"}, {"q": "FDA women pulmonary HT", "opts": ["Adenosine", "Ambrisentan", "Icatibant", "Theophylline"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Ambrisentan"}, {"q": "Pulmonary HT كمان", "opts": ["Caffeine + icatibant", "Sildenafil + prostacyclin", "Adenosine + theophylline", "ولا واحد"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Sildenafil + prostacyclin"}, {"q": "ATP →", "opts": ["Kininogen", "ADP + adenosine", "ET1", "Kinin"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: ADP + adenosine"}, {"q": "ATP receptor", "opts": ["ETA", "P2X", "A", "P2Y"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: P2Y"}, {"q": "ADP receptor", "opts": ["P2X", "A", "B2", "P2Y"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: P2X"}, {"q": "الأهم", "opts": ["P2Y", "A", "B1", "P2X"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: A"}, {"q": "Adenosine bronchi", "opts": ["Mild constriction", "Severe constriction", "Dilation", "ولا شي"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Severe constriction"}, {"q": "Adenosine heart", "opts": ["Vasoconstriction", "↑ A-V conduction", "↑ HR", "↓ A-V conduction"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: ↓ A-V conduction"}, {"q": "Adenosine CNS", "opts": ["Seizures", "ولا شي", "Stimulation", "↓ function"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: ↓ function"}, {"q": "Methylxanthines", "opts": ["Caffeine + theophylline", "Ambrisentan + sildenafil", "Icatibant + adenosine", "ATP + ADP"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: Caffeine + theophylline"}, {"q": "Mechanism", "opts": ["A1 stimulation", "B2 blockade", "ETA blockade", "A1 inhibition"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: A1 inhibition"}, {"q": "Heart", "opts": ["ولا شي", "Tachycardia", "A-V block", "Bradycardia"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Tachycardia"}, {"q": "ممنوعة بـ", "opts": ["Pulmonary HT", "Palpitation + arrhythmias", "Asthma", "HAE"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Palpitation + arrhythmias"}, {"q": "CNS", "opts": ["Sedation", "Amnesia", "Depression", "Stimulation"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: Stimulation"}, {"q": "Theophylline asthma لأنو", "opts": ["↓ A-V conduction", "Sedation", "Bronchodilation", "↓ HR"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Bronchodilation"}, {"q": "Adenosine drug", "opts": ["HAE", "Pulmonary HT", "Atrial tachyarrhythmia + SVT", "Asthma"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Atrial tachyarrhythmia + SVT"}, {"q": "Adenosine mechanism", "opts": ["↑ kinins", "B2 blockade", "A stimulation → ↓ A-V conduction", "A1 blockade"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: A stimulation → ↓ A-V conduction"}, {"q": "Onset", "opts": ["Hours", "Days", "Minutes", "Seconds"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: Seconds"}, {"q": "Dose", "opts": ["6–12 mg oral", "60–120 mg IV", "1–2 mg IV", "6–12 mg IV"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: 6–12 mg IV"}, {"q": "Adenosine ممنوع", "opts": ["HAE", "SVT", "Atrial tachycardia", "Asthma"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: Asthma"}, {"q": "ACEI + airway swelling life threatening", "opts": ["Adenosine", "Ambrisentan", "Icatibant", "Theophylline"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Icatibant"}, {"q": "Asthmatic + SVT، ليش لا adenosine؟", "opts": ["Sedation", "Itching", "Bradycardia", "Severe bronchoconstriction"], "a": 3, "why": "الجواب الصح: Severe bronchoconstriction"}, {"q": "امرأة idiopathic pulmonary HT", "opts": ["Caffeine", "Ambrisentan", "Icatibant", "Adenosine"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: Ambrisentan"}, {"q": "Caffeine بتسرّع القلب لأنها", "opts": ["Stimulates B2", "بتحجب A1 فبيرجع A-V conduction وHR يزيد", "↑ bradykinin", "↑ ET"], "a": 1, "why": "الجواب الصح: بتحجب A1 فبيرجع A-V conduction وHR يزيد"}, {"q": "Mediator مشترك ACEI angioedema + HAE", "opts": ["ATP", "ET", "Bradykinin", "Adenosine"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Bradykinin"}, {"q": "Bronchoconstriction", "opts": ["Bradykinin + adenosine", "Icatibant + theophylline", "ET + caffeine", "ADP + sildenafil"], "a": 0, "why": "الجواب الصح: Bradykinin + adenosine"}, {"q": "عكس بالأوعية", "opts": ["Adenosine + ATP", "Kinin + histamine", "Bradykinin (dilation) + ETA (vasoconstriction)", "P2X + P2Y"], "a": 2, "why": "الجواب الصح: Bradykinin (dilation) + ETA (vasoconstriction)"}], "cards": [{"f": "مريض بياخد ACEI وصار عندو cough و angioedema. شو السبب؟", "b": "زيادة bradykinin."}, {"f": "مريض عنده swelling بالـ tongue والـ larynx، والـ family history positive، والـ C1 inhibitor ناقص؟", "b": "Hereditary Angioedema (HAE)."}, {"f": "مريض ACEI عندو angioedema وصارت life threatening. شو بينعطى؟", "b": "Icatibant (B2 antagonist، subcutaneous)."}, {"f": "مرا عندها idiopathic pulmonary HT، شو دوا معتمد من FDA؟", "b": "Ambrisentan (ET receptor blocker)."}, {"f": "مريض عندو atrial tachyarrhythmia شديدة وبدك تسيطر عليها خلال ثواني؟", "b": "Adenosine 6-12 mg IV."}, {"f": "مريض بالـ asthma عندو SVT، ليش ما بتعطيو adenosine؟", "b": "لأنو الـ adenosine بيعمل severe bronchoconstriction."}, {"f": "مريض عندو asthma، أي دوا من عيلة القهوة بينستعمل؟", "b": "Theophylline، لأنو بيعمل bronchodilatation."}, {"f": "مريض عندو palpitation و arrhythmia، شو لازم يتجنب؟", "b": "Methylxanthines (caffeine، theophylline) لأنها بتعمل tachycardia."}, {"f": "ليش الـ ACEI بيعمل cough؟", "b": "لأنو بيرفع الـ bradykinin."}, {"f": "ليش الـ HAE بيعمل bradykinin كتير؟", "b": "الـ C1 inhibitor ناقص، فالـ kallikrein ما حدا بيوقفو."}, {"f": "ليش الـ bradykinin بيعمل pain؟", "b": "بينبّه nociceptive afferents بالـ skin والـ viscera."}, {"f": "ليش الـ endothelin بيعمل pulmonary HT و essential HT؟", "b": "لأنو severe vasoconstriction، وعندو دور بهدول الحالات."}, {"f": "ليش الـ caffeine بتصحيك؟", "b": "لأنو بيبلوك A1 receptor، والـ adenosine أصلاً بيعمل نعاس."}, {"f": "ليش الـ caffeine بتعمل خفقان؟", "b": "بيبلوك الـ adenosine فبيصير tachycardia."}, {"f": "ليش الـ adenosine بيوقف الـ SVT؟", "b": "بيقلل الـ A-V conduction."}, {"f": "ليش الـ theophylline بيفيد بالـ asthma والـ adenosine بيضر؟", "b": "الـ adenosine بيعمل bronchoconstriction، والـ theophylline بيبلوكو فبيعمل bronchodilatation."}, {"f": "B1 ضد B2؟", "b": "الاتنين kinin receptors. Bradykinin أعلى affinity بالـ B2."}, {"f": "ETA ضد ETB؟", "b": "الاتنين endothelin receptors. الأهم ETA."}, {"f": "Adenosine ضد Methylxanthines بالـ heart؟", "b": "Adenosine بيقلل الـ A-V conduction. Methylxanthines بيعملوا tachycardia."}, {"f": "Adenosine ضد Methylxanthines بالـ CNS؟", "b": "Adenosine بيقلل الـ CNS function. Methylxanthines بيحفّزوه."}, {"f": "Adenosine ضد Theophylline بالـ bronchi؟", "b": "Adenosine bronchoconstriction. Theophylline bronchodilatation."}, {"f": "Icatibant ضد Ambrisentan؟", "b": "Icatibant يبلوك B2 (للـ HAE). Ambrisentan يبلوك ET receptors (للـ pulmonary HT)."}, {"f": "ET1 ضد ET2 و ET3؟", "b": "كلهن endothelins، بس ET1 الأهم."}, {"f": "الـ kinin أقوى من histamine بكام مرة؟", "b": "10 مرات."}, {"f": "وراثة الـ HAE؟", "b": "Autosomal dominant."}, {"f": "طريقة إعطاء icatibant؟", "b": "Subcutaneous."}, {"f": "جرعة adenosine؟", "b": "6-12 mg IV."}, {"f": "سرعة adenosine؟", "b": "خلال ثواني."}, {"f": "مين بيصيبو الـ idiopathic pulmonary HT أكتر؟", "b": "Women."}, {"f": "قارن بين Kinins و Endothelin و Adenosine.", "b": "Bradykinin: B2، pain + inflammation + bronchoconstriction + arteriolar dilation، دواه Icatibant. • Endothelin: ETA، severe vasoconstriction + bronchospasm، دواه Ambrisentan. • Adenosine: A receptor، bronchoconstriction + decrease A-V conduction + CNS depression، دواه adenosine نفسو لـ SVT وmethylxanthines كـ blockers."}], "subject": "pharm", "date": "2026-11-28"},
    {"id":"path-hematology-1","system":"Hematology","no":1,"title":"Iron Deficiency and Megaloblastic Anemias (Lecture 1)","url":"path-iron-megaloblastic-anemias-1d.html","summary":"Anemia: reduced red cells or hemoglobin (WHO cut-offs by age and sex). Iron deficiency anemia (IDA) is the commonest anemia worldwide: iron absorption (duodenum, 10-15% of dietary iron; heme vs non-heme; enhancers and inhibitors; hepcidin), causes (blood loss, diet, demand, malabsorption), features (fatigue, pallor, pica, koilonychia), labs (low Hb, MCV, ferritin; high TIBC) and smear (hypochromic microcytic, target cells). Megaloblastic anemia: macrocytic, nuclear-cytoplasmic dissociation from B12 or folate deficiency (DNA synthesis), hypersegmented neutrophils; B12 absorption needs intrinsic factor in the terminal ileum, stores last 3-4 years; causes include pernicious anemia, gastrectomy, Crohn disease, methotrexate, alcohol.","points":["Anemia: low red cells or hemoglobin; hemoglobin carries oxygen, so fatigue is the first symptom","Iron deficiency anemia is the commonest anemia worldwide","Iron absorbed in duodenum and proximal jejunum (about 10-15% of dietary iron); heme iron absorbs best; vitamin C and acid help; tea and antacids inhibit; hepcidin reduces absorption","IDA features: fatigue, pallor, tachycardia, pica, koilonychia, glossitis","IDA labs: low Hb, low MCV, low ferritin, high TIBC, low transferrin saturation; hypochromic microcytic smear with target cells","Megaloblastic anemia: macrocytic, nucleus matures late while cytoplasm matures normally (nuclear-cytoplasmic dissociation)","Cause: B12 or folate deficiency (needed for DNA synthesis); also methotrexate and alcohol","B12: animal foods, needs intrinsic factor, absorbed in terminal ileum, liver stores last 3-4 years","Smear: macro-ovalocytes and hypersegmented neutrophils; causes of B12 deficiency: vegan diet, pernicious anemia, gastrectomy, Crohn disease"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Which anemia type has HIGH reticulocytes?","opts":["Stem cell failure","Hemolytic anemia","Iron deficiency","B12 deficiency"],"a":1,"why":"الانحلال بيحفّز النخاع فالريتيكولوسايت عالية."},{"q":"Most common cause of IDA in adults:","opts":["Poor diet","Malabsorption","Chronic blood loss","Pregnancy"],"a":2,"why":"النزيف المزمن عند الكبار."},{"q":"Daily iron actually absorbed for balance:","opts":["0.1 mg","1 mg","10 mg","20 mg"],"a":1,"why":"1 ملغ."},{"q":"Iron absorption occurs mainly in:","opts":["Stomach","Duodenum and jejunum","Terminal ileum","Colon"],"a":1,"why":"الاثنا عشري وأول الصائم."},{"q":"Which DECREASES iron absorption?","opts":["Acidic pH","Heme iron","Pregnancy","Increased hepcidin"],"a":3,"why":"الهيبسيدين الزايد."},{"q":"Heme iron compared to non-heme:","opts":["Lower absorption","Higher absorption","Plant source","No risk if excess"],"a":1,"why":"الهيم امتصاصو أعلى."},{"q":"First symptom of IDA:","opts":["Pica","Koilonychia","Fatigue","Hair loss"],"a":2,"why":"التعب بيجي أول."},{"q":"Spoon-shaped nails:","opts":["Koilonychia","Glossitis","Cheilosis","Pica"],"a":0,"why":"Koilonychia."},{"q":"IDA TIBC and ferritin:","opts":["TIBC ↑, ferritin ↓","TIBC ↓, ferritin ↑","Both ↑","Both ↓"],"a":0,"why":"المخزن فاضي."},{"q":"After oral iron, reticulocytes rise in:","opts":["1 day","5-7 days","4 weeks","3 months"],"a":1,"why":"5 لـ7 أيام."},{"q":"Neutrophil finding in megaloblastic anemia:","opts":["Toxic granulation","Hypersegmented","Pelger-Huet","Left shift"],"a":1,"why":"مفرطة التقسيم."},{"q":"B12 absorption site:","opts":["Duodenum","Jejunum","Terminal ileum","Colon"],"a":2,"why":"اللفائفي الانتهائي."},{"q":"B12 stores last about:","opts":["4 months","1 year","3-4 years","10 years"],"a":2,"why":"3 لـ4 سنين."},{"q":"Pernicious anemia is due to:","opts":["Autoimmune gastritis, IF ↓","Ileal resection","Vegan diet","Crohn"],"a":0,"why":"التهاب معدة مناعي."},{"q":"B12 deficiency causes:","opts":["Mania","Demyelination","Hearing loss","Jaundice"],"a":1,"why":"أعصاب."}],"cards":[{"f":"Anemia definition?","b":"Hb / RBC mass below normal"},{"f":"Normal Hb men / women?","b":"130-170 / 120-150 g/L"},{"f":"WHO anemia: pregnant / men?","b":"&lt;110 / &lt;130 g/L"},{"f":"Low retics anemia?","b":"Production ↓"},{"f":"High retics anemia?","b":"Destruction ↑"},{"f":"Commonest anemia?","b":"IDA"},{"f":"IDA adult commonest cause?","b":"Chronic blood loss"},{"f":"Iron transport protein?","b":"Transferrin"},{"f":"RBC lifespan?","b":"120 days"},{"f":"Iron absorbed daily?","b":"1 mg"},{"f":"Absorbed of intake?","b":"10-15%"},{"f":"Iron absorption site?","b":"Duodenum + jejunum"},{"f":"Vitamin C action?","b":"Chelates Fe³⁺; donates electron ← Fe²⁺"},{"f":"Reduce absorption?","b":"Fe³⁺, antacids, tea, overload, infection, hepcidin ↑"},{"f":"Heme source?","b":"Animal; absorption high"},{"f":"Non-heme source?","b":"Plant; absorption poor"},{"f":"First IDA symptom?","b":"Fatigue"},{"f":"Pica?","b":"Craving non-food"},{"f":"Koilonychia?","b":"Spoon-shaped nails"},{"f":"IDA marrow iron stain?","b":"Absent"},{"f":"IDA ferritin / TIBC?","b":"↓ / ↑"},{"f":"Oral iron response?","b":"Retics ↑ 5-7 days"},{"f":"Megaloblastic cause?","b":"B12 or folate deficiency"},{"f":"Megaloblastic marrow sign?","b":"Nuclear cytoplasmic dissociation"},{"f":"Hypersegmented neutrophils?","b":"Megaloblastic sign"},{"f":"B12 absorption?","b":"IF → terminal ileum; passive 1%"},{"f":"B12 stores?","b":"Liver 3-4 years"},{"f":"Folate stores?","b":"Liver ~4 months"},{"f":"Pernicious anemia?","b":"Autoimmune gastritis ← IF ↓"},{"f":"NTD prevention?","b":"Folic acid 0.4 mg daily"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-25"},
 {"id":"path-hematology-2","system":"Hematology","no":2,"title":"Aplastic Anemia (Lecture 2)","url":"path-aplastic-anemia-2.html","summary":"Aplastic anemia: bone marrow failure with pancytopenia and a hypocellular fatty marrow. Congenital (Fanconi anemia, autosomal recessive, DNA repair defect, short stature, skin pigmentation, thumb and radial anomalies) vs acquired (idiopathic or secondary to radiation, drugs such as chloramphenicol, toxins, viral infections such as hepatitis). Peak around 30 years, male predominance. Mechanisms: stem cell defect or immune-mediated damage of the marrow microenvironment. Features: anemia, infection, bleeding. Lab: pancytopenia, normochromic normocytic or mildly macrocytic anemia, low reticulocytes, hypocellular marrow. Treatment: remove the cause, immunosuppressive drugs, transfusions, bone marrow transplantation.","points":["Aplastic anemia: bone marrow stops producing blood cells, causing pancytopenia","Congenital (Fanconi anemia) vs acquired (idiopathic or secondary)","Fanconi anemia: rare, autosomal recessive, DNA repair defect, congenital anomalies","Acquired causes: radiation, drugs, toxins, viral infections; most common peak age about 30, more in males","Mechanism: stem cell defect or immune-mediated destruction of marrow","Symptoms from low cells: anemia, infections, bleeding","Blood: low Hb, normochromic normocytic or macrocytic, low reticulocytes, pancytopenia","Marrow: hypocellular with fat replacement","Treatment: remove cause, drugs, transfusions, bone marrow transplantation"],"mcqs":[{"q":"Aplastic anemia is best defined as:","opts":["Excess hemolysis","Chronic primary hematopoietic failure with pancytopenia","Isolated RBC loss","Marrow infiltration by tumor"],"a":1,"why":"فشل مزمن أولي بالنخاع مع نقص كل الخلايا."},{"q":"Marrow finding in aplastic anemia:","opts":["Hypoplasia","Normal cellularity","Blast excess","Hyperplasia"],"a":0,"why":"النخاع قليل التصنيع."},{"q":"Suspected mechanism in the majority of patients:","opts":["Vitamin loss","Hemolysis","Autoimmune","Iron overload"],"a":2,"why":"عند الأغلبية منشك بآلية مناعية ذاتية."},{"q":"Second common congenital form:","opts":["Diamond-Blackfan anemia","Benzene aplasia","Chernobyl aplasia","Idiopathic aplasia"],"a":0,"why":"ديموند بلاكفان."},{"q":"Fanconi anemia defect involves:","opts":["Iron absorption","Intrinsic factor","Multiprotein complex for DNA repair","Hemoglobin chain synthesis"],"a":2,"why":"عيب بمجموعة بروتينات لإصلاح المادة الوراثية."},{"q":"Fanconi anemia usually presents at:","opts":["Birth only","5-10 years","~30 years","Over 60 years"],"a":1,"why":"عمر الظهور من 5 لـ10 سنين."},{"q":"Which anomaly occurs in Fanconi anemia?","opts":["Cleft lip only","Polydactyly of toes only","Hearing loss only","Thumb or radius anomalies"],"a":3,"why":"تشوهات بالإبهام والكعبرة."},{"q":"Fanconi anemia increases the risk of:","opts":["Cataract only","Malignancies","Gout","Hypertension"],"a":1,"why":"بيزيد خطر السرطان."},{"q":"Which is an organic solvent causing aplastic anemia?","opts":["Ethanol only","Water","Glucose","Benzene"],"a":3,"why":"البنزين مذيب عضوي."},{"q":"Which virus is NOT listed as a cause?","opts":["Herpes zoster","Rabies virus","Cytomegalovirus","Epstein-Barr virus"],"a":1,"why":"الفيروسات بالمحاضرة: التهاب الكبد، CMV، EBV، الهربس النطاقي."},{"q":"Which radiation exposure is a risk for marrow aplasia?","opts":["Nuclear accidents (Chernobyl)","Sunlight","Microwave oven","Mobile phone"],"a":0,"why":"تشيرنوبل مذكور بالمحاضرة."},{"q":"Acquired aplastic anemia sex predominance:","opts":["Equal","Neonates only","Male","Female"],"a":2,"why":"أكتر عند الرجال."},{"q":"Bleeding tendency result from:","opts":["Thrombocytopenia","Neutropenia","Macrocytosis","Reticulocytosis"],"a":0,"why":"نقص الصفايح."},{"q":"Which marrow component remains in aplastic anemia?","opts":["Blasts","Megaloblasts","Normoblasts","Fat cells and fibrous stroma"],"a":3,"why":"خلايا دهنية وأنسجة ليفية ولمفاويات وبلازما."},{"q":"Peripheral blood film shows:","opts":["Schistocytes only","No abnormal cells","Blasts","Target cells only"],"a":1,"why":"ما في خلايا شاذة."}],"cards":[{"f":"Aplastic anemia definition?","b":"Chronic primary hematopoietic failure + pancytopenia"},{"f":"Pancytopenia?","b":"RBCs, WBCs, platelets ↓"},{"f":"Marrow in aplastic anemia?","b":"Hypoplasia"},{"f":"Suspected mechanism (majority)?","b":"Autoimmune"},{"f":"Commonest congenital forms?","b":"Fanconi, Diamond-Blackfan"},{"f":"Fanconi inheritance?","b":"Autosomal recessive"},{"f":"Fanconi defect?","b":"DNA repair multiprotein complex"},{"f":"Fanconi cell finding?","b":"Spontaneous chromosomal breakage"},{"f":"Fanconi age of presentation?","b":"5-10 years"},{"f":"Fanconi anomalies?","b":"Kidney / spleen hypoplasia; thumbs, radii"},{"f":"Fanconi skin / growth?","b":"Café-au-lait, short stature"},{"f":"Fanconi risk?","b":"Malignancy"},{"f":"Fanconi treatment?","b":"Androgens, stem cell transplantation"},{"f":"Acquired causes?","b":"Idiopathic; chemicals, drugs; viruses; irradiation"},{"f":"Solvent causing aplasia?","b":"Benzene"},{"f":"Viruses?","b":"Hepatitis, CMV, EBV, herpes zoster"},{"f":"Radiation example?","b":"Chernobyl"},{"f":"Acquired peak age?","b":"~30 years"},{"f":"Acquired sex?","b":"Male predominance"},{"f":"Neutropenia causes?","b":"Recurrent infections"},{"f":"Thrombocytopenia causes?","b":"Bleeding tendencies"},{"f":"Pathogenesis?","b":"Stem cell or marrow microenvironment defect"},{"f":"Blood: Hb type?","b":"Normochromic normocytic or macrocytic"},{"f":"Retics?","b":"Reticulopenia"},{"f":"Marrow picture?","b":"Hypocellular: fat, fibrous stroma, lymphocytes, plasma cells"},{"f":"Treatment options?","b":"Remove cause, medications, transfusion, BMT"}],"subject":"path","date":"2026-11-26"}
